αἰδώς|a�d�j|aidzs|1) a sense of shame or honour, modesty, bashfulness, reverence, regard for others, respect<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:169, 26|<b>G127</b><br />Perhaps from G1 (as a negative particle) and G1492 (through the idea of <i>downcast</i> eyes); <i>bashfulness</i>, that is, (towards men), <i>modesty</i> or (towards God) <i>awe:</i> - reverence, shamefacedness.<br />|127|
