αὐτάρκεια|a�t�rkeia|autarkeia|1) a perfect condition of life in which no aid or support is needed<br />2) sufficiency of the necessities of life<br />3) a mind contented with its lot, contentment<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:466, 78|<b>G841</b><br />From G842; <i>self satisfaction</i>, that is, (abstractly) <i>contentedness</i>, or (concretely) a <i>competence:</i> - contentment, sufficiency.<br />|841|
