αὐτός|a�t�j|autps|1) himself, herself, themselves, itself<br />2) he, she, it<br />3) the same<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> pronoun|<b>G846</b><br />From the particle <span class="uni">αὖ</span> au (perhaps akin to the base of G109 through the idea of a <i>baffling</i> wind; <i>backward</i>); the reflexive pronoun <i>self</i>, used (alone or in the compound of G1438) of the third person, and (with the proper personal pronoun) of the other persons: - her, it (-self), one, the other, (mine) own, said, ([self-], the) same, ([him-, my-, thy-]) self, [your-] selves, she, that, their (-s), them ([-selves]), there [-at, -by, -in, -into, -of, -on, -with], they, (these) things, this (man), those, together, very, which. Compare G848.<br />|846|
