Βαλαάμ|Bala�m|balaam|1) A native of Pethor a city in Mesopotamia, endued by Jehovah with prophetic power. He was hired by Balak to curse the Israelites; and influenced by the love of reward, he wished to gratify Balak; but he was compelled by Jehovah's power to bless them. Hence later the Jews saw him as a most abandoned deceiver.<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:524, 91|<b>G903</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H1109]; <i>Balaam</i>, a mesopotamian (symbolic of a false teacher): - Balaam.<br />|903|
