βαρύς|bar�j|barus|1) heavy in weight<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) burdensome<br />2b) severe, stern<br />2c) weighty<br />2c1) of great moment<br />2d) violent, cruel, unsparing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:556, 95|<b>G926</b><br />From the same as G922; <i>weighty</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>burdensome</i>, <i>grave:</i> - grievous, heavy, weightier.<br />|926|
