βασκαίνω|baska�nw|baskainz|1) to speak ill of one, to slander, traduce him<br />2) to bring evil on one by feigning praise or an evil eye<br />3) to charm, to bewitch<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:594, 102|<b>G940</b><br />Akin to G5335; to <i>malign</i>, that is, (by extension) to <i>fascinate</i> (by false representations): - bewitch.<br />|940|
βαστάζω|bast�zw|bastafz|1) to take up with the hands<br />2) to take up in order to carry or bear, to put upon one's self<br />2a) to bear what is burdensome<br />3) to bear, to carry<br />3a) to carry on one's person<br />3b) to sustain, i.e. uphold, support<br />4) to bear away, carry off<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:596, 102|<b>G941</b><br />Perhaps remotely derived from the base of G939 (through the idea of <i>removal</i>); to <i>lift</i>, literally or figuratively (<i>endure</i>, <i>declare</i>, <i>sustain</i>, <i>receive</i>, etc.): - bear, carry, take up.<br />|941|
