βρῶσις|br�sij|brzsis|1) act of eating<br />1a) in a wider sense, corrosion<br />2) that which is eaten, food, ailment<br />2a) of the soul's food, either which refreshes the soul, or nourishes and supports it<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:642, 111|<b>G1035</b><br />From the base of G977; (abstractly) <i>eating</i> (literally or figuratively); by extension (concretely) <i>food</i> (literally or figuratively): - eating, food, meat.<br />|1035|
