Γαλατία|Galat�a|calatia|Galatia = "land of the Galli, Gauls"<br />1) the Roman province of Galatia my be roughly described as the central region of the peninsula of Asia Minor, bounded on the north by Bithynia and Paphlagonia; on the east by Pontus; on the south by Cappadocia and Lycaonia; on the west by Phrygia<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G1053</b><br />Of foreign origin; <i>Galatia</i>, a region of Asia: - Galatia.<br />|1053|
