γενεά|gene�|cenea|1) fathered, birth, nativity<br />2) that which has been begotten, men of the same stock, a family<br />2a) the several ranks of natural descent, the successive members of a genealogy<br />2b) metaphorically a group of men very like each other in endowments, pursuits, character<br />2b1) especially in a bad sense, a perverse nation<br />3) the whole multitude of men living at the same time<br />4) an age (i.e. the time ordinarily occupied be each successive generation), a space of 30 - 33 years<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:662, 114|<b>G1074</b><br />From (a presumed derivative of) G1085; a <i>generation</i>; by implication an <i>age</i> (the period or the persons): - age, generation, nation, time.<br />|1074|
γενεαλογέομαι|genealog�omai|cenealpcepmai|1) to recount a family's origin and lineage, trace ancestry<br />2) to draw one's origin, derive one's pedigree<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:665, 114|<b>G1075</b><br />From G1074 and G3056; to <i>reckon by generations</i>, that is, <i>trace in genealogy:</i> - count by descent.<br />|1075|
