γένεσις|g�nesij|cenesis|1) source, origin<br />1a) a book of one's lineage, i.e. in which his ancestry or progeny are enumerated<br />2) used of birth, nativity<br />3) of that which follows origin, viz. existence, life<br />3a) the wheel of life (Jam 3:6), other explain it, the wheel of human origin which as soon as men are born begins to run, i.e. its course of life<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:682, 117|<b>G1078</b><br />From the same as G1074; <i>nativity</i>; figuratively <i>nature:</i> - generation, nature (-ral).<br />|1078|
