γεννάω|genn�w|cennaz|1) of men who fathered children<br />1a) to be born<br />1b) to be begotten<br />1b1) of women giving birth to children<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) to engender, cause to arise, excite<br />2b) in a Jewish sense, of one who brings others over to his way of life, to convert someone<br />2c) of God making Christ his son<br />2d) of God making men his sons through faith in Christ's work<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:665, 114|<b>G1080</b><br />From a variation of G1085; to <i>procreate</i> (properly of the father, but by extension of the mother); figuratively to <i>regenerate:</i> - bear, beget, be born, bring forth, conceive, be delivered of, gender, make, spring.<br />|1080|
