γλυκύς|gluk�j|clukus|1) sweet<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G1099</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; <i>sweet</i> (that is, not bitter nor salt): - sweet, fresh.<br />|1099|
γλῶσσα|gl�ssa|clzssa|1) the tongue, a member of the body, an organ of speech<br />2) a tongue<br />1a) the language or dialect used by a particular people distinct from that of other nations<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:719, 123|<b>G1100</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; the <i>tongue</i>; by implication a <i>language</i> (specifically one naturally unacquired): - tongue.<br />|1100|
