γόης|g�hj|cpgs|1) a wailer, a howler<br />2) a juggler, enchanter (because incantations used to be uttered in a kind of howl)<br />3) a deceiver, imposter<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:737, 126|<b>G1114</b><br />From <span class="uni">γοάω</span> goa&ocirc; (to <i>wail</i>); properly a <i>wizard</i> (as <i>muttering</i> spells), that is, (by implication) an <i>impostor:</i> - seducer.<br />|1114|
