διαγίνομαι|diag�nomai|diacinpmai|1) to be through, continue<br />2) to be between, intervene, used of time, to have intervened, elapsed, passed meanwhile<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1230</b><br />From G1223 and G1096; to <i>elapse meanwhile:</i> - X after, be past, be spent.<br />|1230|
διαγινώσκω|diagin�skw|diacinzskz|1) to distinguish, i.e. to know accurately, ascertain exactly<br />2) in a legal sense, to examine, determine, decide<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1231</b><br />From G1223 and G1097; to <i>know thoroughly</i>, that is, <i>ascertain exactly:</i> - (would) enquire, know the uttermost.<br />|1231|
