διάγνωσις|di�gnwsij|diacnzsis|1) to distinguish<br />2) in a legal sense, examination, opinion, decision<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G1233</b><br />From G1231; (magisterial) <i>examination</i> ("diagnosis"): - hearing.<br />|1233|
διαγογγύζω|diagogg�zw|diacpccufz|1) to murmur<br />1a) either of a whole crowd, or among one another<br />1b) always used of many indignantly complaining<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:735, 125|<b>G1234</b><br />From G1223 and G1111; to <i>complain throughout</i> a crowd: - murmur.<br />|1234|
