διαδέχομαι|diad�comai|diadexpmai|1) to receive through another, anything left or bequeathed by him, to receive in succession, receive in turn, succeed to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1237</b><br />From G1223 and G1209; to <i>receive in turn</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>succeed to:</i> - come after.<br />|1237|
διάδημα|di�dhma|diadgma|1) a diadem<br />1a) a blue band marked with white which Persian kings used to bind on the turban or tiara<br />1b) the kingly ornament for the head, the crown<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G1238</b><br />From a compound of G1223 and G1210; a "diadem" (as <i>bound about</i> the head): - crown. Compare G4735.<br />|1238|
διαδίδωμι|diad�dwmi|diadidzmi|1) to distribute, divide among several<br />2) to give over, deliver<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1239</b><br />From G1223 and G1325; to <i>give throughout</i> a crowd, that is, <i>deal out</i>; also to <i>deliver</i> over (as to a successor): - (make) distribute (-ion), divide, give.<br />|1239|
διάδοχος|di�docoj|diadpxps|1) succeeding, a successor<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G1240</b><br />From G1237; a <i>successor</i> in office: - room.<br />|1240|
διαζώννυμι|diaz�nnumi|diafznnumi|1) to bind or gird all around<br />2) to gird one's self with a thing, gird a thing around one's self<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:302, 702|<b>G1241</b><br />From G1223 and G2224; to <i>gird tightly:</i> - gird.<br />|1241|
διαθήκη|diaq�kh|diahgkg|1) a disposition, arrangement, of any sort, which one wishes to be valid, the last disposition which one makes of his earthly possessions after his death, a testament or will<br />2) a compact, a covenant, a testament<br />2a) God's covenant with Noah, etc.<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:106, 157|<b>G1242</b><br />From G1303; properly a <i>disposition</i>, that is, (specifically) a <i>contract</i> (especially a devisory <i>will</i>): - covenant, testament.<br />|1242|
διαίρεσις|dia�resij|diairesis|1) division, distribution<br />2) distinction, difference<br />2a) in particular, a distinction arising from a different distribution to different persons<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:184, 27|<b>G1243</b><br />From G1244; a <i>distinction</i> or (concretely) <i>variety:</i> - difference, diversity.<br />|1243|
διαιρέω|diair�w|diairez|1) to divide into parts, to part, to tear, cleave or cut asunder<br />2) to distribute<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:184, 27|<b>G1244</b><br />From G1223 and G138; to <i>separate</i>, that is, <i>distribute:</i> - divide.<br />|1244|
