διασείω|diase�w|diaseiz|1) to shake thoroughly<br />2) to make to tremble<br />3) to terrify<br />4) to agitate<br />5) to extort from one by intimidation money or other property<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1286</b><br />From G1223 and G4579; to <i>shake thoroughly</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>intimidate:</i> - do violence to.<br />|1286|
διασκορπίζω|diaskorp�zw|diaskprqifz|1) to scatter abroad, disperse, to winnow<br />1a) to throw the grain a considerable distance, or up into the air, that it may be separated from the chaff<br />1b) to gather the wheat, freed from the chaff into the granary<br />1c) to winnow grain<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:418, 1048|<b>G1287</b><br />From G1223 and G4650; to <i>dissipate</i>, that is, (generally) to <i>rout</i> or <i>separate</i>; specifically to <i>winnow</i>; figuratively to <i>squander:</i> - disperse, scatter (abroad), strew, waste.<br />|1287|
