διαστέλλομαι|diast�llomai|diastellpmai|1) to draw asunder, divide, distinguish, dispose, order<br />2) to open one's self, i.e. one's mind, to set forth distinctly<br />3) to admonish, order, charge<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:591,*|<b>G1291</b><br />Middle voice from G1223 and G4724; to <i>set</i> (oneself) <i>apart</i> (figuratively <i>distinguish</i>), that is, (by implication) to <i>enjoin:</i> - charge, that which was (give) commanded (-ment).<br />|1291|
διάστημα|di�sthma|diastgma|1) an interval, distance, space of time<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G1292</b><br />From G1339; an <i>interval:</i> - space.<br />|1292|
διαστολή|diastol�|diastplg|1) a distinction, difference<br />1a) of the different sounds musical instruments make<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:592, 1074|<b>G1293</b><br />From G1291; a <i>variation:</i> - difference, distinction.<br />|1293|
διαστρέφω|diastr�fw|diastrevz|1) to distort, turn aside<br />1a) to oppose, plot against the saving purposes and plans of God<br />2) to turn aside from the right path, to pervert, corrupt<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:717, 1093|<b>G1294</b><br />From G1223 and G4762; to <i>distort</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>misinterpret</i>, or (morally) <i>corrupt:</i> - perverse (-rt), turn away.<br />|1294|
διασῴζω|dias�zw|diaszfz|1) to preserve through danger, to bring safely through<br />1a) to save, i.e. cure one who is sick, bring him through<br />2) to save, keep from perishing<br />3) to save out of danger, rescue<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1295</b><br />From G1223 and G4982; to <i>save thoroughly</i>, that is, (by implication or analogy) to <i>cure</i>, <i>preserve</i>, <i>rescue</i>, etc.: - bring safe, escape (safe), heal, make perfectly whole, save.<br />|1295|
διαταγή|diatag�|diatacg|1) a disposition, arrangement, ordinance<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:36, 1156|<b>G1296</b><br />From G1299; <i>arrangement</i>, that is, <i>institution:</i> - instrumentality.<br />|1296|
