διαταράσσω|diatar�ssw|diatarassz|1) to agitate greatly, trouble greatly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1298</b><br />From G1223 and G5015; to <i>disturb wholly</i>, that is, <i>agitate</i> (with alarm): - trouble.<br />|1298|
διατάσσω|diat�ssw|diatassz|1) to arrange, appoint, ordain, prescribe, give order<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:34, 1156|<b>G1299</b><br />From G1223 and G5021; to <i>arrange thoroughly</i>, that is, (specifically) <i>institute</i>, <i>prescribe</i>, etc.: - appoint, command, give, (set in) order, ordain.<br />|1299|
διατελέω|diatel�w|diatelez|1) to bring thoroughly to an end, accomplish<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1300</b><br />From G1223 and G5055; to <i>accomplish thoroughly</i>, that is, (subjectively) to <i>persist:</i> - continue.<br />|1300|
διατηρέω|diathr�w|diatgrez|1) to keep continually or carefully<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:151, 1174|<b>G1301</b><br />From G1223 and G5083; to <i>watch thoroughly</i>, that is, (positively and transitively) to <i>observe</i> strictly, or (negatively and reflexively) to <i>avoid</i> wholly: - keep.<br />|1301|
διατί|diat�|diati|1) through, by, with, because of, for the sake of<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> pronoun|<b>G1302</b><br />From G1223 and G5101; <i>through what</i> cause?, that is, <i>why?</i>: - wherefore, why.<br />|1302|
διατίθεμαι|diat�qemai|diatihemai|1) to arrange, dispose of, one's own affairs<br />1a) of something that belongs to one<br />1b) to dispose of by will, make a testament<br />2) to make a covenant, enter into a covenant, with one<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:104, 157|<b>G1303</b><br />Middle voice from G1223 and G5087; to <i>put apart</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>dispose</i> (by assignment, compact or bequest): - appoint, make, testator.<br />|1303|
διατρίβω|diatr�bw|diatribz|1) to rub between, rub hard<br />2) to wear away, consume<br />3) to spend, pass time<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1304</b><br />From G1223 and the base of G5147; to <i>wear through</i> (time), that is, <i>remain:</i> - abide, be, continue, tarry.<br />|1304|
διατροφή|diatrof�|diatrpvg|1) sustenance<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G1305</b><br />From a compound of G1223 and G5142; <i>nourishment:</i> - food.<br />|1305|
διαυγάζω|diaug�zw|diaucafz|1) to shine through, to dawn<br />1a) of daylight breaking through the darkness of night<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1306</b><br />From G1223 and G826; to <i>glimmer through</i>, that is, <i>break</i> (as day): - dawn.<br />|1306|
διαυγής|diaug�j|diaucgs|1) transparent, translucent<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G1307</b><br />From G1223 and G5316; <i>appearing through</i>, that is, "diaphanous": - transparent.<br />|1307|
διαφέρω|diaf�rw|diaverz|1) to bear or carry through any place<br />2) to carry different ways<br />2a) to carry in different directions, to different places<br />2a1) of people who are carried hither and thither in a ship, driven to and fro<br />2b) to differ, to test, prove, the good things that differ<br />2b1) to distinguish between good and evil, lawful and unlawful, to approve of things that excel, to differ from one<br />2b2) to excel, surpass one<br />2c) impersonally, it makes a difference, it matters, is of importance<br /><b>Part of Speech: </b>none<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:62, 1252|<b>G1308</b><br />From G1223 and G5342; to <i>bear through</i>, that is, (literally) <i>transport</i>; usually to <i>bear apart</i>, that is, (objectively) to <i>toss about</i> (figuratively <i>report</i>); subjectively to <i>"differ"</i>, or (by implication) <i>surpass:</i> - be better, carry, differ from, drive up and down, be (more) excellent, make matter, publish, be of more value.<br />|1308|
διαφεύγω|diafe�gw|diaveucz|1) to flee through danger, to escape<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1309</b><br />From G1223 and G5343; to <i>flee through</i>, that is, <i>escape:</i> - escape.<br />|1309|
διαφημίζω|diafhm�zw|diavgmifz|1) to spread abroad, blaze abroad<br />2) to spread abroad his fame or renown<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1310</b><br />From G1223 and a derivative of G5345; to <i>report thoroughly</i>, that is, <i>divulgate:</i> - blaze abroad, commonly report, spread abroad, fame.<br />|1310|
διαφθείρω|diafqe�rw|diavheirz|1) to change for the worse, to corrupt<br />1a) of minds, morals<br />2) to destroy, ruin<br />2a) to consume<br />2a1) of bodily vigour and strength<br />2a2) of the worm or moth that eats provisions, clothing, etc.<br />2b) to destroy, to kill<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:93, 1259|<b>G1311</b><br />From G1223 and G5351; to <i>rot thoroughly</i>, that is, (by implication) to <i>ruin</i> (passively <i>decay</i> utterly, figuratively <i>pervert</i>): - corrupt, destroy, perish.<br />|1311|
