διδακτός|didakt�j|didaktps|1) that can be taught<br />2) taught, instructed by one<br />3) teachings, precepts<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:165, 161|<b>G1318</b><br />From G1321; (subjectively) <i>instructed</i> or (objectively) <i>communicated</i> by teaching: - taught, which . . . teacheth.<br />|1318|
