διέρχομαι|di�rcomai|dierxpmai|1) to go through, pass through<br />1a) to go, walk, journey, pass through a place<br />1b) to travel the road which leads through a place, go, pass, travel through a region<br />2) to go different places<br />2a) of people, to go abroad<br />2b) of a report, to spread, go abroad<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:676, 257|<b>G1330</b><br />From G1223 and G2064; to <i>traverse</i> (literally): - come, depart, go (about, abroad, every where, over, through, throughout), pass (by, over, through, throughout), pierce through, travel, walk through.<br />|1330|
διερωτάω|dierwt�w|dierztaz|1) to ask through<br />1a) ask many, one after another<br />1b) to find out by asking, enquire out<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1331</b><br />From G1223 and G2065; to <i>question throughout</i>, that is, <i>ascertain</i> by interrogation: - make enquiry for.<br />|1331|
