διηνεκής|dihnek�j|dignekgs|1) continuously, continuous<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G1336</b><br />Neuter of a compound of G1223 and a derivative of an alternate of G5342; <i>carried through</i>, that is, (adverb with G1519 and G3588 prefixed) <i>perpetually:</i> - +continually, for ever.<br />|1336|
διθάλασσος|diq�lassoj|dihalassps|1) resembling or forming two seas: thus of the Euxine Sea<br />2) lying between two seas, i.e. washed on both sides by the sea<br />2a) an isthmus or tongue of land, the extremity of which is covered by the waves<br />2b) a projecting reef or bar against which the waves dash on both sides<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G1337</b><br />From G1364 and G2281; <i>having two seas</i>, that is, a <i>sound</i> with a double outlet: - where two seas met.<br />|1337|
