δουλεύω|doule�w|dpuleuz|1) to be a slave, serve, do service<br />1a) of a nation in subjection to other nations<br />2) metaphorically to obey, submit to<br />2a) in a good sense, to yield obedience<br />2b) in a bad sense, of those who become slaves to some base power, to yield to, give one's self up to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:261, 182|<b>G1398</b><br />From G1401; to <i>be a slave</i> to (literally or figuratively, involuntarily or voluntarily): - be in bondage, (do) serve (-ice).<br />|1398|
