δοῦλος|do�loj|dpulps|1) a slave, bondman, man of servile condition<br />1a) a slave<br />1b) metaphorically, one who gives himself up to another's will those whose service is used by Christ in extending and advancing his cause among men<br />1c) devoted to another to the disregard of one's own interests<br />2) a servant, attendant<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:261, 182|<b>G1401</b><br />From G1210; a <i>slave</i> (literally or figuratively, involuntarily or voluntarily; frequently therefore in a qualified sense of <i>subjection</i> or <i>subserviency</i>): - bond (-man), servant.<br />|1401|
