δοχή|doc�|dpxg|1) a feast, banquet<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:54, 146|<b>G1403</b><br />From G1209; a <i>reception</i>, that is, convivial <i>entertainment:</i> - feast.<br />|1403|
δράκων|dr�kwn|drakzn|1) a dragon, a great serpent, a name for Satan<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:281, 186|<b>G1404</b><br />Probably from an alternate form of <span class="uni">δέρκομαι</span> derkomai (to <i>look</i>); a fabulous kind of <i>serpent</i> (perhaps as supposed to <i>fascinate</i>): - dragon.<br />|1404|
