ἐθελοθρησκία|�qeloqrhsk�a|ehelphrgskia|1) voluntary, arbitrary worship<br />1a) worship which one prescribes and devises for himself, contrary to the contents and nature of faith which ought to be directed to Christ<br />1b) said of the misdirected zeal and the practice of ascetics<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:155, 337|<b>G1479</b><br />From G2309 and G2356; <i>voluntary</i> (<i>arbitrary</i> and <i>unwarranted</i>) <i>piety</i>, that is, <i>sanctimony:</i> - will worship.<br />|1479|
