ἐθνικός|�qnik�j|ehnikps|1) adapted to the genius or customs of a people, peculiar to a people, national<br />2) suited to the manners or language of foreigners, strange, foreign<br />3) in the NT savouring of the nature of pagans, alien to the worship of the true God, heathenish<br />3a) of the pagan, the Gentile<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:372, 201|<b>G1482</b><br />From G1484; <i>national</i> ("ethnic"), that is, (specifically) a <i>Gentile:</i> - heathen (man).<br />|1482|
