εἰσακούω|e�sako�w|eisakpuz|1) to give heed to, comply with admonition, to obey<br />2) to listen to, assent to, a request, to be heard, have request granted<br />2a) of persons offering prayers to God<br />2b) of prayers offered up<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:222, 34|<b>G1522</b><br />From G1519 and G191; to <i>listen</i> to: - hear.<br />|1522|
εἰσδέχομαι|e�sd�comai|eisdexpmai|1) to receive kindly, to treat with favour<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:57, 146|<b>G1523</b><br />From G1519 and G1209; to <i>take into</i> one's favor: - receive.<br />|1523|
