εἰσφέρω|e�sf�rw|eisverz|1) to bring into, in or to<br />2) to lead into<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:64, 1252|<b>G1533</b><br />From G1519 and G5342; to <i>carry inward</i> (literally or figuratively): - bring (in), lead into.<br />|1533|
εἶτα|e�ta|eita|1) then<br />2) next, after that<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G1534</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; a particle of <i>succession</i> (in time or logical enumeration), <i>then</i>, <i>moreover</i>: - after that (-ward), furthermore, then. See also G1899.<br />|1534|
