ἐκβολή|�kbol�|ekbplg|1) a casting out<br />2) the throwing overboard of goods and lading whereby sailors lighten a ship in a storm to keep her from sinking<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G1546</b><br />From G1544; <i>ejection</i>, that is, (specifically) a <i>throwing overboard</i> of the cargo: - + lighten the ship.<br />|1546|
ἔκγαμίζω|�kgam�zw|ekcamifz|1) to give away in marriage: a daughter<br />2) to marry, to be given in marriage<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G1547</b><br />From G1537 and a form of G1061 (compare G1548); to <i>marry off</i> a daughter: - give in marriage.<br />|1547|
