εὐαγγελιστής|e�aggelist�j|euaccelistgs|1) a bringer of good tidings, an evangelist<br />2) the name given to the NT heralds of salvation through Christ who are not apostles<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:736, 267|<b>G2099</b><br />From G2097; a <i>preacher</i> of the gospel: - evangelist.<br />|2099|
εὐαρεστέω|e�arest�w|euarestez|1) to be well pleasing<br />2) to be well pleased with a thing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:456, 77|<b>G2100</b><br />From G2101; to <i>gratify entirely:</i> - please (well).<br />|2100|
