εὐδοκία|e�dok�a|eudpkia|1) will, choice<br />1a) good will, kindly intent, benevolence<br />2) delight, pleasure, satisfaction<br />3) desire<br />3a) for delight in any absent thing easily produces longing for it<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:742, 273|<b>G2107</b><br />From a presumed compound of G2095 and the base of G1380; <i>satisfaction</i>, that is, (subjectively) <i>delight</i>, or (objectively) <i>kindness</i>, <i>wish</i>, <i>purpose:</i> - desire, good pleasure (will), X seem good.<br />|2107|
