εὐλάβεια|e�l�beia|eulabeia|1) caution, circumspection, discretion<br />1a) avoidance<br />1b) a reasonable shunning<br />2) reverence, veneration<br />2a) reverence toward God, godly fear, piety<br />3) fear anxiety, dread<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:751, 275|<b>G2124</b><br />From G2126; properly <i>caution</i>, that is, (religiously) <i>reverence</i> (<i>piety</i>); by implication <i>dread</i> (concretely): - fear (-ed).<br />|2124|
