ἐφίστημι|�f�sthmi|evistgmi|1) to place at, place upon, place over<br />1a) to stand by, be present<br />1b) to stand over one, place one's self above<br />1b1) used especially of persons coming upon one suddenly<br />1b1a) an angel, of the advent of angels<br />1b1b) of dreams<br />1b2) of evils coming upon one<br />1c) to be at hand<br />1c1) be ready<br />1d) of time<br />1d1) to come upon<br />1d1a) of rain<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2186</b><br />From G1909 and G2476; to <i>stand upon</i>, that is, <i>be present</i> (in various applications, friendly or otherwise, usually literally): - assault, come (in, to, unto, upon), be at hand (instant), present, stand (before, by, over).<br />|2186|
