Ἠλίας|'Hl�aj|glias|Elijah = "my God is Jehovah"<br />1) a prophet born at Thisbe, the unflinching champion of the theocracy in the reigns of the idolatrous kings Ahab and Ahaziah. He was taken up to heaven without dying, whence the Jews expected he would return just before the advent of the Messiah, whom he would prepare the minds of the Israelites to receive.<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:928, 306|<b>G2243</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H452]; <i>Helias</i> (that is, <i>Elijah</i>), an Israelite: - Elias.<br />|2243|
