Θαδδαῖος|Qadda�oj|haddaips|Thaddaeus = "large hearted, courageous"<br />1) one of the twelve apostles. From a comparison with the catalogue of apostles in Luk 6:16, and Act 1:13, is seems that Judas, Lebbaeus and Thaddaeus were the same person, and the writer of the book of Jude.<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G2280</b><br />Of uncertain origin; <i>Thaddaeus</i>, one of the Apostles: - Thaddus.<br />|2280|
