θαρρέω|qarr�w|harrez|1) to be of good courage, be of good cheer<br />2) to be bold<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:25, 315|<b>G2292</b><br />Another form for G2293; to <i>exercise courage</i>: - be bold, X boldly, have confidence, be confident. Compare G5111.<br />|2292|
