θαῦμα|qa�ma|hauma|1) a wonderful thing, a marvel<br />2) wonder<br />2a) to wonder [with great wonder i.e.] exceedingly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:27, 316|<b>G2295</b><br />Apparently from a form of G2300; <i>wonder</i> (properly concrete; but by implication abstract): - admiration.<br />|2295|
θαυμάζω|qaum�zw|haumafz|1) to wonder, wonder at, marvel<br />2) to be wondered at, to be had in admiration<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:27, 316|<b>G2296</b><br />From G2295; to <i>wonder</i>; by implication to <i>admire:</i> - admire, have in admiration, marvel, wonder.<br />|2296|
θαυμάσιος|qaum�sioj|haumasips|1) wonderful, marvellous<br />2) wonderful deeds, wonders<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:27, 316|<b>G2297</b><br />From G2295; <i>wondrous</i>, that is, (neuter as noun) a <i>miracle:</i> - wonderful thing.<br />|2297|
θαυμαστός|qaumast�j|haumastps|1) wonderful, marvellous<br />1a) worthy of pious admiration, admirable, excellent<br />1b) passing human comprehension<br />1c) causing amazement joined with terror<br />1d) marvellous<br />1d1) extraordinary, striking, surprising<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:27, 316|<b>G2298</b><br />From G2296; <i>wondered</i> at, that is, (by implication) <i>wonderful:</i> - marvel (-lous).<br />|2298|
