θεομάχος|qeom�coj|hepmaxps|1) fighting against God, resisting God<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:528, 573|<b>G2314</b><br />From G2316 and G3164; an <i>opponent of deity:</i> - to fight against God.<br />|2314|
θεόπνευστος|qe�pneustoj|hepqneustps|1) inspired by God<br />1a) the contents of the scriptures<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:453, 876|<b>G2315</b><br />From G2316 and a presumed derivative of G4154; <i>divinely breathed</i> in: - given by inspiration of God.<br />|2315|
θεός|qe�j|heps|1) a god or goddess, a general name of deities or divinities<br />2) the Godhead, trinity<br />2a) God the Father, the first person in the trinity<br />2b) Christ, the second person of the trinity<br />2c) Holy Spirit, the third person in the trinity<br />3) spoken of the only and true God<br />3a) refers to the things of God<br />3b) his counsels, interests, things due to him<br />4) whatever can in any respect be likened unto God, or resemble him in any way<br />4a) God's representative or viceregent<br />4a1) of magistrates and judges<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:65, 322|<b>G2316</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; a <i>deity</i>, especially (with G3588) <i>the</i> supreme <i>Divinity</i>; figuratively a <i>magistrate</i>; by Hebraism <i>very:</i> - X exceeding, God, god [-ly, -ward].<br />|2316|
θεοσέβεια|qeos�beia|hepsebeia|1) reverence towards God's goodness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:123, 331|<b>G2317</b><br />From G2318; <i>devoutness</i>, that is, <i>piety:</i> - godliness.<br />|2317|
θεοσεβής|qeoseb�j|hepsebgs|1) worshipping God, pious<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:123, 331|<b>G2318</b><br />From G2316 and G4576; <i>reverent of God</i>, that is, <i>pious:</i> - worshipper of God.<br />|2318|
θεοστυγής|qeostug�j|hepstucgs|1) hateful to God, exceptionally impious and wicked<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G2319</b><br />From G2316 and the base of G4767; <i>hateful to God</i>, that is, <i>impious:</i> - hater of God.<br />|2319|
θεότης|qe�thj|heptgs|1) deity<br />1a) the state of being God, Godhead<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:119, 322|<b>G2320</b><br />From G2316; <i>divinity</i> (abstractly): - godhead.<br />|2320|
Θεόφιλος|Qe�filoj|hepvilps|Theophilus = "friend of God"<br />1) the person to whom Luke addressed his Gospel and the book of Acts<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G2321</b><br />From G2316 and G5384; <i>friend of God</i>; <i>Theophilus</i>, a Christian: - Theophilus.<br />|2321|
θεραπεία|qerape�a|heraqeia|1) service rendered by one to another<br />2) spec. medical service: curing, healing<br />3) household service<br />3a) body of attendants, servants, domestics<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:131, 331|<b>G2322</b><br />From G2323; <i>attendance</i> (specifically medical, that is, <i>cure</i>); figuratively and collectively <i>domestics:</i> - healing, household.<br />|2322|
θεραπεύω|qerape�w|heraqeuz|1) to serve, do service<br />2) to heal, cure, restore to health<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:128, 331|<b>G2323</b><br />From the same as G2324; to <i>wait upon</i> menially, that is, (figuratively) to <i>adore</i> (God), or (specifically) to <i>relieve</i> (of disease): - cure, heal, worship.<br />|2323|
θεράπων|qer�pwn|heraqzn|1) an attendant, servant: of God<br />1a) spoken of Moses discharging the duties committed to him by God<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:132, 331|<b>G2324</b><br />Apparently a participle from an otherwise obsolete derivation of the base of G2330; a menial <i>attendant</i> (as if <i>cherishing</i>): - servant.<br />|2324|
θερίζω|qer�zw|herifz|1) to reap, harvest<br />2) proverbial expression for sowing and reaping<br />3) cut off, destroy<br />3a) as crops are cut down with a sickle<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:132, 332|<b>G2325</b><br />From G2330 (in the sense of the <i>crop</i>); to <i>harvest:</i> - reap.<br />|2325|
θερισμός|qerism�j|herismps|1) harvest, the act of reaping<br />1a) fig. of the gathering of men into the kingdom of God<br />1b) referring to time of reaping, the final judgment, when the righteous are gathered into the kingdom of God and the wicked are cast into hell for ever<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:133, 332|<b>G2326</b><br />From G2325; <i>reaping</i>, that is, the <i>crop:</i> - harvest.<br />|2326|
θεριστής|qerist�j|heristgs|1) a reaper<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G2327</b><br />From G2325; a <i>harvester:</i> - reaper.<br />|2327|
θερμαίνομαι|qerma�nomai|hermainpmai|1) to make warm, to heat<br />2) to warm one's self<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2328</b><br />From G2329; to <i>heat</i> (oneself): - (be) warm (-ed, self).<br />|2328|
θέρμη|q�rmh|hermg|1) heat<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G2329</b><br />From the base of G2330; <i>warmth:</i> - heat.<br />|2329|
θέρος|q�roj|herps|1) summer<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G2330</b><br />From a primary word <span class="uni">θέρω</span> ther&ocirc; (to <i>heat</i>); properly <i>heat</i>, that is, <i>summer:</i> - summer.<br />|2330|
Θεσσαλονικεύς|Qessalonike�j|hessalpnikeus|1) a Thessalonians<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G2331</b><br />From G2332; a <i>Thessalonican</i>, that is, inhabitant of Thessalonice: - Thessalonian.<br />|2331|
Θεσσαλονίκη|Qessalon�kh|hessalpnikg|Thessalonica = "victory of falsity"<br />1) a famous and populous city, situated on the Thermaic Gulf, the capital of the second division of Macedonia and the residence of a Roman governor and quaestor<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G2332</b><br />From <span class="uni">Θεσσαλός</span> Thessalos (a <i>Thessalian</i>) and G3529; <i>Thessalonice</i>, a place in Asia Minor: - Thessalonica.<br />|2332|
Θευδᾶς|Qeud�j|heudas|Theudas = "God-given"<br />1) the name of an insurgent mentioned in Gamaliel's speech before the Jewish council, Act 5:35-39, at the time of the arraignment of the apostles. He appeared, according to Luke's account, at the head of about four hundred men. He was probably one of the insurrectionary chiefs or fanatics by whom the land was overrun in the last year of Herod's reign. Josephus speaks of a Theudas who played a similar part at the time of Claudius, about A.D. 44; but the Theudas mentioned by Luke must be a different person from the one spoken of by Josephus.<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G2333</b><br />Of uncertain origin; <i>Theudas</i>, as Israelite: - Theudas.<br />|2333|
θεωρέω|qewr�w|hezrez|1) to be a spectator, look at, behold<br />1a) to view attentively, take a view of, survey<br />1a1) to view mentally, consider<br />2) to see<br />2a) to perceive with the eyes, to enjoy the presence of one<br />2b) to discern, descry<br />2c) to ascertain, find out by seeing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:315, 706|<b>G2334</b><br />From a derivative of G2300 (perhaps by adverb of G3708); to <i>be a spectator</i> of, that is, <i>discern</i>, (literally, figuratively [<i>experience</i>] or intensively [<i>acknowledge</i>]): - behold, consider, look on, perceive, see. Compare G3700.<br />|2334|
θεωρία|qewr�a|hezria|1) a viewing, beholding<br />2) that which is viewed, a spectacle, sight<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G2335</b><br />From the same as G2334; <i>spectatorship</i>, that is, (concretely) a <i>spectacle:</i> - sight.<br />|2335|
θήκη|q�kh|hgkg|1) that which a thing is put or laid away, a receptacle, repository, chest, box<br />1a) used of the sheath of a sword<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G2336</b><br />From G5087; a <i>receptacle</i>, that is, <i>scabbard:</i> - sheath.<br />|2336|
θηλάζω|qhl�zw|hglafz|1) to give the breast, give suck, to suckle<br />2) to suck<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2337</b><br />From <span class="uni">θηλή</span> th&ecirc;l&ecirc; (the <i>nipple</i>); to <i>suckle</i>; by implication to <i>suck:</i> - (give) suck (-ling).<br />|2337|
θῆλυς|q�luj|hglus|1) of the female sex<br />2) a woman, a female<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G2338</b><br />From the same as G2337; <i>female:</i> - female, woman.<br />|2338|
θήρα|q�ra|hgra|1) a hunting of wild beasts to destroy them<br />2) metaphorically of preparing destruction for men<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G2339</b><br />From <span class="uni">θήρ</span> th&ecirc;r (a wild <i>animal</i>, as <i>game</i>); <i>hunting</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>destruction:</i> - trap.<br />|2339|
θηρεύω|qhre�w|hgreuz|1) to go a hunting, to hunt, to catch in hunting<br />2) metaphorically to lay wait for, strive to ensnare, catch artfully<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2340</b><br />From G2339; to <i>hunt</i> (an animal), that is, (figuratively) to <i>carp at:</i> - catch.<br />|2340|
θηριομαχέω|qhriomac�w|hgripmaxez|1) to fight with wild beasts<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2341</b><br />From a compound of G2342 and G3164; to <i>be a beast fighter</i> (in the gladiatorial show), that is, (figuratively) to <i>encounter</i> (furious men): - fight with wild beasts.<br />|2341|
θηρίον|qhr�on|hgripn|1) an animal<br />2) a wild animal, wild beast, beast<br />3) metaphorically a brutal, bestial man, savage, ferocious<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:133, 333|<b>G2342</b><br />Diminutive from the same as G2339; a <i>dangerous animal:</i> - (venomous, wild) beast.<br />|2342|
θησαυρίζω|qhsaur�zw|hgsaurifz|1) to gather and lay up, to heap up, store up<br />1a) to accumulate riches<br />1b) to keep in store, store up, reserve<br />2) metaphorically so to live from day to day as to increase either the bitterness or the happiness of one's consequent lot<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:138, 333|<b>G2343</b><br />From G2344; to <i>amass</i> or <i>reserve</i> (literally or figuratively): - lay up (treasure), (keep) in store, (heap) treasure (together, up).<br />|2343|
θησαυρός|qhsaur�j|hgsaurps|1) the place in which good and precious things are collected and laid up<br />1a) a casket, coffer, or other receptacle, in which valuables are kept<br />1b) a treasury<br />1c) storehouse, repository, magazine<br />2) the things laid up in a treasury, collected treasures<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:136, 333|<b>G2344</b><br />From G5087; a <i>deposit</i>, that is, <i>wealth</i> (literally or figuratively): - treasure.<br />|2344|
θιγγάνω|qigg�nw|hiccanz|1) to touch, handle<br />1a) to do violence to, injury<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2345</b><br />A prolonged form of an obsolete primary word <span class="uni">θίγω</span> thig&ocirc; (to <i>finger</i>); to <i>manipulate</i>, that is, <i>have to do with</i>; by implication to <i>injure:</i> - handle, touch.<br />|2345|
θλίβω|ql�bw|hlibz|1) to press (as grapes), press hard upon<br />2) a compressed way<br />2a) narrow straitened, contracted<br />3) metaphorically to trouble, afflict, distress<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:139, 334|<b>G2346</b><br />Akin to the base of G5147; to <i>crowd</i> (literally or figuratively): - afflict, narrow, throng, suffer tribulation, trouble.<br />|2346|
θλῖψις|ql�yij|hliyis|1) a pressing, pressing together, pressure<br />2) metaphorically oppression, affliction, tribulation, distress, straits<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:139, 334|<b>G2347</b><br />From G2346; <i>pressure</i> (literally or figuratively): - afflicted, (-tion), anguish, burdened, persecution, tribulation, trouble.<br />|2347|
θνῄσκω|qn�skw|hngskz|1) to die, to be dead<br />2) metaphorically to be spiritually dead<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:7, 312|<b>G2348</b><br />A strengthened form of a simpler primary word <span class="uni">θάνω</span> than&ocirc; (which is used for it only in certain tenses); to <i>die</i> (literally or figuratively): - be dead, die.<br />|2348|
θνητός|qnht�j|hngtps|1) liable to death, mortal<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:21, 312|<b>G2349</b><br />From G2348; <i>liable to die:</i> - mortal (-ity).<br />|2349|
θορυβέω|qorub�w|hprubez|1) to make a noise or uproar, be turbulent<br />2) to disturb, throw into confusion<br />2a) to be troubled in mind<br />2b) to wail tumultuously<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2350</b><br />From G2351; to <i>be in tumult</i>, that is, <i>disturb</i>, <i>clamor:</i> - make ado (a noise), trouble self, set on an uproar.<br />|2350|
θόρυβος|q�ruboj|hprubps|1) a noise, tumult, uproar<br />1a) of persons wailing<br />1b) of a clamorous and excited multitude<br />1c) of riotous persons<br />2) a tumult, as a breach of public order<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G2351</b><br />From the base of G2360; a <i>disturbance:</i> - tumult, uproar.<br />|2351|
θραύω|qra�w|hrauz|1) to break, break in pieces, shatter, smite through<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2352</b><br />A primary verb; to <i>crush</i>: - bruise. Compare G4486.<br />|2352|
θρέμμα|qr�mma|hremma|1) whatever is fed or nursed<br />1a) a ward, nursling, child<br />2) a flock, cattle, especially sheep and goats<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G2353</b><br />From G5142; <i>stock</i> (as <i>raised</i> on a farm): - cattle.<br />|2353|
θρηνέω|qrhn�w|hrgnez|1) to mourn, to lament<br />1a) of singers of dirges, [to wail]<br />2) to bewail, deplore<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:148, 335|<b>G2354</b><br />From G2355; to <i>bewail:</i> - lament, mourn.<br />|2354|
θρῆνος|qr�noj|hrgnps|1) a lamentation<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:148, 335|<b>G2355</b><br />From the base of G2360; <i>wailing:</i> - lamentation.<br />|2355|
θρησκεία|qrhske�a|hrgskeia|1) religious worship<br />1a) especially external, that which consists of ceremonies<br />1a1) religious discipline, religion<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:155, 337|<b>G2356</b><br />From a derivative of G2357; ceremonial <i>observance:</i> - religion, worshipping.<br />|2356|
θρησκός|qrhsk�j|hrgskps|1) fearing or worshipping God<br />2) to tremble<br />2a) trembling, fearful<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:155, 337|<b>G2357</b><br />Probably from the base of G2360; <i>ceremonious</i> in worship (as <i>demonstrative</i>), that is, <i>pious:</i> - religious.<br />|2357|
θριαμβεύω|qriambe�w|hriambeuz|1) to triumph, to celebrate a triumph<br />2) cause one to triumph<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:159, 337|<b>G2358</b><br />From a prolonged compound of the base of G2360 and a derivative of G680 (meaning a <i>noisy iambus</i>, sung in honor of Bacchus); to <i>make an acclamatory procession</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>conquer</i> or (by Hebraism) to <i>give victory:</i> - (cause) to triumph (over).<br />|2358|
θρίξ|qr�x|hrio|1) the hair of the head<br />2) the hair of animals<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G2359</b><br />Of uncertain derivation; <i>hair</i>: - hair. Compare G2864.<br />|2359|
θροέομαι|qro�omai|hrpepmai|1) to cry aloud, make a noise by outcry<br />1a) in the NT, to trouble, frighten<br />1b) to be troubled in mind, to be frightened, alarmed<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2360</b><br />From <span class="uni">θρέομαι</span> threomai (to <i>wail</i>); to <i>clamor</i>, that is, (by implication) to <i>frighten:</i> - trouble.<br />|2360|
θρόμβος|qr�mboj|hrpmbps|1) a large thick drop, especially of clotted blood<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G2361</b><br />Perhaps from G5142 (in the sense of <i>thickening</i>); a <i>clot:</i> - great drop.<br />|2361|
θρόνος|qr�noj|hrpnps|1) a throne seat<br />1a) a chair of state having a footstool<br />1b) assigned in the NT to kings, hence, kingly power or royalty<br />1b1) metaphorically to God, the governor of the world<br />1b2) to the Messiah, Christ, the partner and assistant in the divine administration<br />1b2a) hence divine power belonging to Christ<br />1b3) to judges, i.e. tribunal or bench<br />1b4) to elders<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:160, 338|<b>G2362</b><br />From <span class="uni">θράω</span> thra&ocirc; (to <i>sit</i>); a stately <i>seat</i> ("throne"); by implication <i>power</i> or (concretely) a <i>potentate:</i> - seat, throne.<br />|2362|
Θυάτιρα|Qu�tira|huatira|Thyatira = "odour of affliction"<br />1) a colony of Macedonia Greeks, situated between Sardis and Pergamos on the river Lycus; its inhabitants gained their living by traffic and the art of dyeing in purple<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G2363</b><br />Of uncertain derivation; <i>Thyatira</i>, a place in Asia Minor: - Thyatira.<br />|2363|
θυγάτηρ|qug�thr|hucatgr|1) a daughter<br />1a) a daughter of God<br />1a1) acceptable to God, rejoicing in God's peculiar care and protection<br />1b) with the name of a place, city, or region<br />1b1) denotes collectively all its inhabitants and citizens<br />1c) a female descendant<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G2364</b><br />Apparently a primary word (compare "daughter"); a <i>female child</i>, or (by Hebraism) <i>descendant</i> (or <i>inhabitant</i>): - daughter.<br />|2364|
θυγάτριον|qug�trion|hucatripn|1) a little daughter<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G2365</b><br />From G2364; a <i>daughterling:</i> - little (young) daughter.<br />|2365|
θύελλα|q�ella|huella|1) a sudden storm, tempest, whirlwind<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G2366</b><br />From G2380 (in the sense of <i>blowing</i>) a storm: - tempest.<br />|2366|
θύϊνος|qڎnoj|huinps|1) the citrus, an odoriferous North African tree used as incense, prized by the ancient Greeks and Romans on account of the beauty of its wood for various ornamental purposes<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G2367</b><br />From a derivative of G2380 (in the sense of <i>blowing</i>; denoting a certain <i>fragrant</i> tree); made of <i>citron</i> wood: - thyine.<br />|2367|
θυμίαμα|qum�ama|humiama|1) an aromatic substance burnt, incense<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G2368</b><br />From G2370; an <i>aroma</i>, that is, fragrant <i>powder</i> burnt in religious service; by implication the <i>burning</i> itself: - incense, odour.<br />|2368|
θυμιατήριον|qumiat�rion|humiatgripn|1) a utensil for fumigating or burning incense<br />2) an altar of incense<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G2369</b><br />From a derivative of G2370; a <i>place of fumigation</i>, that is, the <i>altar of incense</i> (in the Temple): - censer.<br />|2369|
θυμιάω|qumi�w|humiaz|1) to burn incense<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2370</b><br />From a derivative of G2380 (in the sense of <i>smoking</i>); to <i>fumigate</i>, that is, <i>offer</i> aromatic <i>fumes:</i> - burn incense.<br />|2370|
θυμομαχέω|qumomac�w|humpmaxez|1) to carry on war with great animosity<br />2) to be very angry, be exasperated<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2371</b><br />From a presumed compound of G2372 and G3164; to <i>be in a furious fight</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>be exasperated:</i> - be highly displeased.<br />|2371|
θυμός|qum�j|humps|1) passion, angry, heat, anger forthwith boiling up and soon subsiding again<br />2) glow, ardour, the wine of passion, inflaming wine (which either drives the drinker mad or kills him with its strength)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:167, 339|<b>G2372</b><br />From G2380; <i>passion</i> (as if <i>breathing</i> hard): - fierceness, indignation, wrath. Compare G5590.<br />|2372|
θυμόομαι|qum�omai|humppmai|1) to cause one to become incensed, to provoke to anger<br />2) to be wroth<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2373</b><br />From G2372; to <i>put in a passion</i>, that is, <i>enrage:</i> - be wroth.<br />|2373|
θύρα|q�ra|hura|1) a door<br />1a) the vestibule<br />1b) used of any opening like a door, an entrance, way or passage into<br />1c) in a parable or metaphor<br />1c1) the door through which sheep go in and out, the name of him who brings salvation to those who follow his guidance<br />1c2) "an open door" is used of the opportunity of doing something<br />1c3) the door of the kingdom of heaven (likened to a palace) denotes the conditions which must be complied with in order to be received into the kingdom of God<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:173, 340|<b>G2374</b><br />Apparently a primary word (compare "door"); a <i>portal</i> or entrance (the opening or the closure, literally or figuratively): - door, gate.<br />|2374|
