θυσιαστήριον|qusiast�rion|husiastgripn|1) the altar for slaying and burning of victims used of<br />1a) the altar of whole burnt offerings which stood in the court of the priests in the temple at Jerusalem<br />1b) the altar of incense which stood in the sanctuary or the Holy Place<br />1c) any other altar<br />1c1) metaphorically, the cross on which Christ suffered an expiatory death: to eat of this altar, i.e. to appropriate to one's self the fruits of Christ's expiatory death<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:180, 342|<b>G2379</b><br />From a derivative of G2378; a <i>place of sacrifice</i>, that is, an <i>altar</i> (specifically or generally, literally or figuratively): - altar.<br />|2379|
