Ἰούδας|'Io�daj|ipudas|Judah or Judas = "he shall be praised"<br />1) the fourth son of Jacob<br />2) an unknown ancestor of Christ<br />3) a man surnamed the Galilean, who at the time of the census of Quirinus, excited the revolt in Galilee, Act 5:37<br />4) a certain Jew of Damascus, Act 9:11<br />5) a prophet surnamed Barsabas, of the church at Jerusalem, Act 15:22,Act 15:27,Act 15:32<br />6) the apostle, Joh 14:22, who was surnamed Lebbaeus or Thaddaeus, and according to opinion wrote the Epistle of Jude.<br />7) the half-brother of Jesus, Mat 13:55<br />8) Judas Iscariot, the apostle who betrayed Jesus<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G2455</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H3063]; <i>Judas</i> (that is, <i>Jehudah</i>), the name of ten Israelites; also of the posterity of one of them and its region: - Juda (-h, -s); Jude.<br />|2455|
