καταλείπω|katale�pw|kataleiqz|1) to leave behind<br />1a) to depart from, leave<br />1a1) to be left<br />1b) to bid (one) to remain<br />1c) to forsake, leave to one's self a person or thing by ceasing to care for it, to abandon, leave in the lurch<br />1c1) to be abandoned, forsaken<br />1d) to cause to be left over, to reserve, to leave remaining<br />1e) like our "leave behind", it is used of one who on being called away cannot take another with him<br />1e1) especially of the dying (to leave behind)<br />1f) like our "leave", leave alone, disregard<br />1f1) of those who sail past a place without stopping<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:194, 523|<b>G2641</b><br />From G2596 and G3007; to <i>leave down</i>, that is, <i>behind</i>; by implication to <i>abandon</i>, <i>have remaining:</i> - forsake, leave, reserve.<br />|2641|
