καταναρκάω|katanark�w|katanarkaz|1) to cause to grow numb or torpid<br />2) to be torpid, inactive, to be to the detriment of one<br />3) to weigh heavily upon, be burdensome to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2655</b><br />From G2596 and <span class="uni">ναρκάω</span> narka&ocirc; (to <i>be numb</i>); to <i>grow utterly torpid</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>slothful</i> (figuratively <i>expensive</i>): - be burdensome (chargeable).<br />|2655|
κατανεύω|katane�w|kataneuz|1) to nod to, make a sign<br />2) to indicate to another by a nod or sign what one wishes him to do<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2656</b><br />From G2596 and G3506; to <i>nod down</i> (<i>towards</i>), that is, (by analogy) to <i>make signs</i> to: - beckon.<br />|2656|
κατανοέω|katano�w|katanpez|1) to perceive, remark, observe, understand<br />2) to consider attentively, fix one's eyes or mind upon<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:973, 636|<b>G2657</b><br />From G2596 and G3539; to <i>observe fully:</i> - behold, consider, discover, perceive.<br />|2657|
καταντάω|katant�w|katantaz|1) to come to, arrive<br />1a) to come to a place over against, opposite another<br />1b) metaphorically to attain to a thing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:623, 419|<b>G2658</b><br />From G2596 and a derivative of G473; to <i>meet against</i>, that is, <i>arrive</i> at (literally or figuratively): - attain, come.<br />|2658|
κατάνυξις|kat�nuxij|katanuois|1) a pricking, piercing<br />2) severe sorrow, extreme grief<br />3) insensibility or torpor of mind, such as extreme grief easily produces<br />3a) hence a "spirit of stupor", which renders their souls torpid so insensible that they are not affected at all by the offer made them of salvation through the Messiah<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:626, 419|<b>G2659</b><br />From G2660; a <i>prickling</i> (sensation, as of the limbs <i>asleep</i>), that is, (by implication [perhaps by some confusion with G3506 or even with G3571]) <i>stupor</i> (<i>lethargy</i>): - slumber.<br />|2659|
κατανύσσομαι|katan�ssomai|katanusspmai|1) to prick, pierce<br />2) metaphorically to pain the mind sharply, agitate it vehemently<br />2a) especially of the emotion of sorrow<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:626, 419|<b>G2660</b><br />From G2596 and G3572; to <i>pierce thoroughly</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>agitate</i> violently ("sting to the quick"): - prick.<br />|2660|
