καταπατέω|katapat�w|kataqatez|1) to tread down, trample under foot, to trample on<br />2) metaphorically to treat with rudeness and insult<br />2a) to spurn, treat with insulting neglect<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:940, 804|<b>G2662</b><br />From G2596 and G3961; to <i>trample down</i>; figuratively to <i>reject</i> with disdain: - trample, tread (down, underfoot).<br />|2662|
