καταπέτασμα|katap�tasma|kataqetasma|1) a veil spread out, a curtain<br />1a) the name given to the two curtains in the temple at Jerusalem, one of them at the entrance to the temple separated the Holy Place from the outer court, the other veiled the Holy of Holies from the Holy Place<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:628, 420|<b>G2665</b><br />From a compound of G2596 and a congener of G4072; something <i>spread thoroughly</i>, that is, (specifically) the door <i>screen</i> (to the Most Holy Place) in the Jewish Temple: - vail.<br />|2665|
καταπίνω|katap�nw|kataqinz|1) to drink down, swallow down<br />2) to devour<br />3) to swallow up, destroy<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:158, 841|<b>G2666</b><br />From G2596 and G4095; to <i>drink down</i>, that is, <i>gulp entire</i> (literally or figuratively): - devour, drown, swallow (up).<br />|2666|
καταπίπτω|katap�ptw|kataqiqtz|1) to fall down<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:169, 846|<b>G2667</b><br />From G2596 and G4098; to <i>fall down:</i> - fall (down).<br />|2667|
καταπλέω|katapl�w|kataqlez|1) to sail down from the deep sea to the land<br />2) to put in<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2668</b><br />From G2596 and G4126; to <i>sail down</i> upon a place, that is, to <i>land</i> at: - arrive.<br />|2668|
καταπονέω|katapon�w|kataqpnez|1) to tire down with toil, exhaust with labour<br />1a) to afflict or oppress with evils<br />1b) to make trouble for<br />1c) to treat roughly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2669</b><br />From G2596 and a derivative of G4192; to <i>labor down</i>, that is, <i>wear with toil</i> (figuratively <i>harass</i>): - oppress, vex.<br />|2669|
καταποντίζομαι|katapont�zomai|kataqpntifpmai|1) to plunge or sink into the sea<br />1a) to sink, to go down<br />1b) a grievous offender for the purpose of killing him, to drown<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2670</b><br />From G2596 and a derivative of the same as G4195; to <i>plunge down</i>, that is, <i>submerge:</i> - drown, sink.<br />|2670|
