κατεφίστημι|katef�sthmi|katevistgmi|1) to set up against<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2721</b><br />From G2596 and G2186; to <i>stand over against</i>, that is, <i>rush upon</i> (<i>assault</i>): - make insurrection against.<br />|2721|
κατέχω|kat�cw|katexz|1) to hold back, detain, retain<br />1a) from going away<br />1b) to restrain, hinder (the course or progress of)<br />1b1) that which hinders, Antichrist from making his appearance<br />1b2) to check a ship's headway, i.e. to hold or head the ship<br />1c) to hold fast, keep secure, keep firm possession of<br />2) to get possession of, take<br />2b) to possess<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:829, 286|<b>G2722</b><br />From G2596 and G2192; to <i>hold down</i> (<i>fast</i>), in various applications (literally or figuratively): - have, hold (fast), keep (in memory), let, X make toward, possess, retain, seize on, stay, take, withhold.<br />|2722|
