κατηχέω|kathc�w|katgxez|1) to sound towards, sound down upon, resound<br />1a) to charm with resounding sound, to fascinate<br />2) to teach orally, to instruct<br />3) to inform by word of mouth<br />3a) to be orally informed<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:638, 422|<b>G2727</b><br />From G2596 and G2279; to <i>sound down</i> into the ears, that is, (by implication) to <i>indoctrinate</i> ("catechize") or (generally) to <i>apprise</i> of: - inform, instruct, teach.<br />|2727|
