καυστηριάζω|kausthri�zw|kaustgriafz|1) to mark by branding, to brand, branded with their own consciences<br />1a) whose souls are branded with the marks of sin<br />1b) who carry about with them the perpetual consciousness of sin<br />2) seared<br />3) in a medical sense, to cauterise, remover by cautery<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:644,*|<b>G2743</b><br />From a derivative of G2545; to <i>brand</i> ("cauterize"), that is, (by implication) to <i>render unsensitive</i> (figuratively): - sear with a hot iron.<br />|2743|
καυχάομαι|kauc�omai|kauxapmai|1) to glory (whether with reason or without)<br />2) to glory on account of a thing<br />3) to glory in a thing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:645, 423|<b>G2744</b><br />From some (obsolete) base akin to that of <span class="uni">αὐχέω</span> auche&ocirc; (to <i>boast</i>) and G2172; to <i>vaunt</i> (in a good or a bad sense): - (make) boast, glory, joy, rejoice.<br />|2744|
