κεῖμαι|ke�mai|keimai|1) to lie<br />1a) of an infant<br />1b) of one buried<br />1c) of things that quietly cover some spot<br />1c1) of a city situated on a hill<br />1d) of things put or set in any place, in ref. to which we often use "to stand"<br />1d1) of vessels, of a throne, of the site of a city, of grain and other things laid up together, of a foundation<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) to be (by God's intent) set, i.e. destined, appointed<br />2b) of laws, to be made, laid down<br />2c) lies in the power of the evil one, i.e. is held in subjection by the devil<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:654, 425|<b>G2749</b><br />Middle voice of a primary verb; to <i>lie</i> outstretched (literally or figuratively): - be (appointed, laid up, made, set), lay, lie. Compare G5087.<br />|2749|
κειρία|keir�a|keiria|1) a band, either for bed-girth, or for tying up a corpse after it has been swathed in linen<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G2750</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; a <i>swathe</i>, that is, <i>winding sheet:</i> - graveclothes.<br />|2750|
κείρω|ke�rw|keirz|1) to sheer: a sheep<br />2) to get or let be shorn<br />3) of shearing or cutting short the hair of the head<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2751</b><br />A primary verb; to <i>shear:</i> - shear (-er).<br />|2751|
κέλευσμα|k�leusma|keleusma|1) an order, command, spec. a stimulating cry, either that by which animals are roused and urged on by man, as horses by charioteers, hounds by hunters, etc., or that by which a signal is given to men, e.g. to rowers by the master of a ship, to soldiers by a commander (with a loud summons, a trumpet call)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:656,*|<b>G2752</b><br />From G2753; a <i>cry</i> of incitement: - shout.<br />|2752|
κελεύω|kele�w|keleuz|1) to command, to order<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2753</b><br />From a primary word <span class="uni">κέλλω</span> kell&ocirc; (to <i>urge</i> on); "hail"; to <i>incite</i> by word, that is, <i>order:</i> - bid, (at, give) command (-ment).<br />|2753|
κενοδοξία|kenodox�a|kenpdpoia|1) vain glory, groundless, self esteem, empty pride<br />2) a vain opinion, error<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:662, 426|<b>G2754</b><br />From G2755; <i>empty glorying</i>, that is, <i>self conceit:</i> - vain-glory.<br />|2754|
