κινέω|kin�w|kinez|1) to cause to go, i.e. to move, set in motion<br />1a) to be moved, move: of that motion which is evident in life<br />1b) to move from a place, to remove<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) to move excite<br />2b) a riot, disturbance<br />2c) to throw into commotion<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:718, 435|<b>G2795</b><br />From <span class="uni">κίω</span> ki&ocirc; (poetic for [<span class="uni">εἶμι</span> eimi to <i>go</i>]); to <i>stir</i> (transitively), literally or figuratively: - (re-) move (-r), way.<br />|2795|
