Κνίδος|Kn�doj|knidps|Cnidus or Gnidus = "nettled"<br />1) a peninsula [now Cape Crio] and a city by the same name, situated at the extreme south west of the peninsula of Asia Minor, on a promontory now called Cape Crio, which projects between the islands of Cos and Rhodes<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G2834</b><br />Probably of foreign origin; <i>Cnidus</i>, a place in Asia Minor: - Cnidus.<br />|2834|
