κόκκος|k�kkoj|kpkkps|1) a grain<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:810, 450|<b>G2848</b><br />Apparently a primary word; a <i>kernel</i> of seed: - corn, grain.<br />|2848|
κολάζω|kol�zw|kplafz|1) to lop or prune, as trees and wings<br />2) to curb, check, restrain<br />3) to chastise, correct, punishment<br />4) to cause to be punished<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:814, 451|<b>G2849</b><br />From <span class="uni">κόλος</span> kolos (<i>dwarf</i>); properly to <i>curtail</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>chastise</i> (or <i>reserve</i> for infliction): - punish.<br />|2849|
κολακεία|kolake�a|kplakeia|1) flattery, flattering discourse<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:817, 451|<b>G2850</b><br />From a derivative of <span class="uni">κόλαξ</span> kolax (a <i>fawner</i>); <i>flattery:</i> - X flattering.<br />|2850|
