κολαφίζω|kolaf�zw|kplavifz|1) to strike with the fist, give one a blow with the fist<br />2) to maltreat, treat with violence and contumely<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:818, 451|<b>G2852</b><br />From a derivative of the base of G2849; to <i>rap</i> with the fist: - buffet.<br />|2852|
κολλάομαι|koll�omai|kpllapmai|1) to glue, to glue together, cement, fasten together<br />2) to join or fasten firmly together<br />3) to join one's self to, cleave to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:822, 452|<b>G2853</b><br />From <span class="uni">κόλλα</span> kolla ("glue"); to <i>glue</i>, that is, (passively or reflexively) to <i>stick</i> (figuratively): - cleave, join (self), keep company.<br />|2853|
κολλούριον|kollo�rion|kpllpuripn|1) a preparation composed of various materials and used as a remedy for tender eyelids<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G2854</b><br />Neuter of a presumed derivative of <span class="uni">κολλύρα</span> kollura (a <i>cake</i>; probably akin to the base of G2853); properly a <i>poultice</i> (as made of or in the form of <i>crackers</i>), that is, (by analogy) a <i>plaster:</i> - eyesalve.<br />|2854|
