κομίζω|kom�zw|kpmifz|1) to care for, take care of, provide for<br />2) to take up or carry away in order to care for and preserve<br />3) to carry away, bear off<br />4) to carry, bear, bring to, to carry away for one's self, to carry off what is one's own, to bring back<br />4a) to receive, obtain: the promised blessing<br />4b) to receive what was previously one's own, to get back, receive back, recover<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G2865</b><br />From a primary word <span class="uni">κολυμβος</span> kolumbos (to <i>tend</i>, that is, take care of); properly to <i>provide</i> for, that is, (by implication) to <i>carry</i> off (as if from harm; generally <i>obtain</i>): - bring, receive.<br />|2865|
