κτίζω|kt�zw|ktifz|1) to make habitable, to people, a place, region, island<br />1a) to found a city, colony, state<br />2) to create<br />2a) of God creating the worlds<br />2b) to form, shape, i.e. to completely change or transform<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:1000, 481|<b>G2936</b><br />Probably akin to G2932 (through the idea of the <i>proprietorship</i> of the <i>manufacturer</i>); to <i>fabricate</i>, that is, <i>found</i> (<i>form</i> originally): - create, Creator, make.<br />|2936|
