λατρεία|latre�a|latreia|1) service rendered for hire<br />1a) any service or ministration: the service of God<br />2) the service and worship of God according to the requirements of the Levitical law<br />3) to perform sacred services<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:58, 503|<b>G2999</b><br />From G3000; <i>ministration</i> of God, that is, <i>worship:</i> - (divine) service.<br />|2999|
λατρεύω|latre�w|latreuz|1) to serve for hire<br />2) to serve, minister to, either to the gods or men and used alike of slaves and freemen<br />2a) in the NT, to render religious service or homage, to worship<br />2b) to perform sacred services, to offer gifts, to worship God in the observance of the rites instituted for his worship<br />2b1) of priests, to officiate, to discharge the sacred office<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:58, 503|<b>G3000</b><br />From <span class="uni">λάτρις</span> latris (a hired <i>menial</i>); to <i>minister</i> (to God), that is, <i>render</i> religious <i>homage:</i> - serve, do the service, worship (-per).<br />|3000|
