λειτουργικός|leitourgik�j|leitpurcikps|1) relating to the performance of service, employed in ministering<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:231, 526|<b>G3010</b><br />From the same as G3008; <i>functional publicly</i> ("liturgic"), that is, <i>beneficent:</i> - ministering.<br />|3010|
λειτουργός|leitourg�j|leitpurcps|1) a public minister, a servant of the state<br />2) a minister, servant<br />2a) so of military labourers<br />2b) of the temple<br />2b1) of one busied with holy things<br />2b2) of a priest<br />2c) of the servants of a king<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:229, 526|<b>G3011</b><br />From a derivative of G2992 and G2041; a <i>public servant</i>, that is, a <i>functionary</i> in the Temple or Gospel, or (generally) a <i>worshipper</i> (of God) or <i>benefactor</i> (of man): - minister (-ed).<br />|3011|
λέντιον|l�ntion|lentipn|1) a linen cloth, towel<br />1a) of the towel or apron with which servants put on when about to work<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G3012</b><br />Of Latin origin; a "linen" cloth, that is, <i>apron:</i> - towel.<br />|3012|
