λιθόστρωτος|liq�strwton|lihpstrztpn|1) spread (paved with stones)<br />2) a mosaic or tessellated pavement<br />2a) of a place near the praetorium or palace of Jerusalem<br />2b) an apartment whose pavement consists of tessellated work<br />2c) of places in the outer courts of temple<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3038</b><br />From G3037 and a derivative of G4766; <i>stone strewed</i>, that is, a tessellated <i>mosaic</i> on which the Roman tribunal was placed: - Pavement.<br />|3038|
λικμάω|likm�w|likmaz|1) to winnow, cleanse away the chaff from the grain by winnowing<br />2) to scatter<br />3) to crush to pieces, grind to powder<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:280, 535|<b>G3039</b><br />From <span class="uni">λικμός</span> likmos, the equivalent. of <span class="uni">λίκνον</span> liknon (a winnowing <i>fan</i> or basket); to <i>winnow</i>, that is, (by analogy) to <i>triturate:</i> - grind to powder.<br />|3039|
