λιμός|lim�j|limps|1) scarcity of harvest, famine<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G3042</b><br />Probably from G3007 (through the idea of <i>destitution</i>); a <i>scarcity</i> of food: - dearth, famine, hunger.<br />|3042|
λίνον|l�non|linpn|1) linen clothing made from flax<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G3043</b><br />Probably a primary word; <i>flax</i>, that is, (by implication) "linen": - linen.<br />|3043|
Λίνος|L�noj|linps|Linus = "a net"<br />1) a Christian at Rome, known to Paul and to Timothy, 2Ti 4:21, who was the first bishop of Rome after the apostles (A.D. 64)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G3044</b><br />Perhaps from G3043; <i>Linus</i>, a Christian: - Linus.<br />|3044|
