μακροθυμέω|makroqum�w|makrphumez|1) to be of a long spirit, not to lose heart<br />1a) to persevere patiently and bravely in enduring misfortunes and troubles<br />1b) to be patient in bearing the offenses and injuries of others<br />1b1) to be mild and slow in avenging<br />1b2) to be longsuffering, slow to anger, slow to punish<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:374, 550|<b>G3114</b><br />From the same as G3116; to <i>be long spirited</i>, that is, (objectively) <i>forbearing</i> or (subjectively) <i>patient:</i> - bear (suffer) long, be longsuffering, have (long) patience, be patient, patiently endure.<br />|3114|
μακροθυμία|makroqum�a|makrphumia|1) patience, endurance, constancy, steadfastness, perseverance<br />2) patience, forbearance, longsuffering, slowness in avenging wrongs<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:374, 550|<b>G3115</b><br />From the same as G3116; <i>longanimity</i>, that is, (objectively) <i>forbearance</i> or (subjectively) <i>fortitude:</i> - longsuffering, patience.<br />|3115|
μακροθύμως|makroq�mwj|makrphumzs|1) with longanimity, i.e. patiently<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:387, 550|<b>G3116</b><br />Adverb of a compound of G3117 and G2372; <i>with long</i> (<i>enduring</i>) <i>temper</i>, that is, <i>leniently:</i> - patiently.<br />|3116|
μακρός|makr�j|makrps|1) long<br />1a) of place: remote, distant, far off<br />1b) of time: long, long lasting<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3117</b><br />From G3372; <i>long</i> (in place [<i>distant</i>] or time [neuter plural]): - far, long.<br />|3117|
μακροχρόνιος|makrocr�nioj|makrpxrpnips|1) long lived<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3118</b><br />From G3117 and G5550; <i>long timed</i>, that is, <i>long lived:</i> - live long.<br />|3118|
μαλακία|malak�a|malakia|1) softness<br />2) in the NT infirmity, debility, bodily weakness, sickness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:1091, 655|<b>G3119</b><br />From G3120; <i>softness</i>, that is, <i>enervation</i> (<i>debility</i>): - disease.<br />|3119|
μαλακός|malak�j|malakps|1) soft, soft to the touch<br />2) metaphorically in a bad sense<br />2a) effeminate<br />2a1) of a catamite<br />2a2) of a boy kept for homosexual relations with a man<br />2a3) of a male who submits his body to unnatural lewdness<br />2a4) of a male prostitute<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3120</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; <i>soft</i>, that is, <i>fine</i> (clothing); figuratively a <i>catamite:</i> - effeminate, soft.<br />|3120|
Μαλελεήλ|Malele�l|malelegl|Maleleel or Mahalaleel = "praise of God"<br />1) the fourth in descent from Adam, son of Cainan<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G3121</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H4111]; <i>Maleleel</i> (that is, <i>Mahalalel</i>), an antediluvian: - Maleleel.<br />|3121|
μάλιστα|m�lista|malista|1) especially, chiefly, most of all, above all<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverbial superlative|<b>G3122</b><br />Neuter plural of the superlative of an apparently primary adverb <span class="uni">μάλα</span> mala (<i>very</i>); (adverb) <i>most</i> (<i>in the greatest degree</i>) or <i>particularly:</i> - chiefly, most of all, (e-) specially.<br />|3122|
μᾶλλον|m�llon|mallpn|1) more, to a greater degree, rather<br />1a) much, by far<br />1b) rather, sooner<br />1c) more willingly, more readily, sooner<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverbial comparative|<b>G3123</b><br />Neuter of the comparative of the same as G3122; (adverb) <i>more</i> (<i>in a greater degree</i>) or <i>rather:</i> - + better, X far, (the) more (and more), (so) much (the more), rather.<br />|3123|
