μάμμη|m�mmh|mammg|1) mother (the name infants use in addressing their mother)<br />2) grandmother<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G3125</b><br />Of natural origin ["mammy"]; a <i>grandmother:</i> - grandmother.<br />|3125|
μαμωνᾶς|mamwn�j|mamznas|1) mammon<br />2) treasure<br />3) riches (where it is personified and opposed to God)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:388, 552|<b>G3126</b><br />Of Chaldee origin (<i>confidence</i>, that is, figuratively <i>wealth</i>, personified); <i>mammonas</i>, that is, <i>avarice</i> (deified): - mammon.<br />|3126|
