μανθάνω|manq�nw|manhanz|1) to learn, be appraised<br />1a) to increase one's knowledge, to be increased in knowledge<br />1b) to hear, be informed<br />1c) to learn by use and practice<br />1c1) to be in the habit of, accustomed to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:390, 552|<b>G3129</b><br />Prolonged from a primary verb, another form of which, <span class="uni">μαθέω</span> mathe&ocirc;, is used as an alternate in certain tenses; to <i>learn</i> (in any way): - learn, understand.<br />|3129|
