μάννα|m�nna|manna|manna = "what is it"<br />1) the food that nourished the Israelites for forty years in the wilderness<br />2) of the manna was kept in the ark of the covenant<br />3) symbolically, that which is kept in the heavenly temple for the food of angels and the blessed<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:462, 563|<b>G3131</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H4478]; <i>manna</i> (that is, <i>man</i>), an edible gum: - manna.<br />|3131|
μαντεύομαι|mante�omai|manteupmai|1) to act as a seer<br />1a) deliver an oracle, prophesy, divine<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3132</b><br />From a derivative of G3105 (meaning a <i>prophet</i>, as supposed to <i>rave</i> through <i>inspiration</i>); to <i>divine</i>, that is, <i>utter spells</i> (under pretence of foretelling): - by soothsaying.<br />|3132|
μαραίνομαι|mara�nomai|marainpmai|1) to extinguish (a flame, fire, light, etc.)<br />2) to render arid, make to waste away, consume away, perish<br />3) to have a miserable end<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3133</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; to <i>extinguish</i> (as fire), that is, (figuratively and passively) to <i>pass away:</i> - fade away.<br />|3133|
μαρανα-θα|marana-qa|maranaha|1) our Lord cometh or will come<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> interjection<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:466, 563|<b>G3134</b><br />Of Chaldee origin (meaning <i>our Lord has come</i>); <i>maranatha</i>, that is, an exclamation of the approaching <i>divine judgment:</i> - Maran-atha.<br />|3134|
