μαρτυρέω|martur�w|marturez|1) to be a witness, to bear witness, i.e. to affirm that one has seen or heard or experienced something, or that he knows it because taught by divine revelation or inspiration<br />1a) to give (not to keep back) testimony<br />1b) to utter honourable testimony, give a good report<br />1c) conjure, implore<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:474, 564|<b>G3140</b><br />From G3144; to <i>be a witness</i>, that is, <i>testify</i> (literally or figuratively): - charge, give [evidence], bear record, have (obtain, of) good (honest) report, be well reported of, testify, give (have) testimony, (be, bear, give, obtain) witness.<br />|3140|
μαρτυρία|martur�a|marturia|1) a testifying<br />1a) the office committed to the prophets of testifying concerning future events<br />2) what one testifies, testimony, i.e. before a judge<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:474, 564|<b>G3141</b><br />From G3144; <i>evidence</i> given (judicially or generally): - record, report, testimony, witness.<br />|3141|
μαρτύριον|mart�rion|marturipn|1) testimony<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:474, 564|<b>G3142</b><br />Neuter of a presumed derivative of G3144; something <i>evidential</i>, that is, (generally) <i>evidence</i> given or (specifically) the <i>Decalogue</i> (in the sacred Tabernacle): - to be testified, testimony, witness.<br />|3142|
μαρτύρομαι|mart�romai|marturpmai|1) to cite a witness, bring forward a witness, call to witness<br />1a) to affirm be appeal to God, to declare solemnly, protest<br />2) to conjure, beseech as in God's name, exhort solemnly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:510, 564|<b>G3143</b><br />Middle voice from G3144; to <i>be adduced</i> as <i>a witness</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>obtest</i> (in affirmation or exhortation): - take to record, testify.<br />|3143|
μάρτυς|m�rtuj|martus|1) a witness<br />1a) in a legal sense<br />1b) an historical sense<br />1b1) one who is a spectator of anything, e.g. of a contest<br />1c) in an ethical sense<br />1c1) those who after his example have proved the strength and genuineness of their faith in Christ by undergoing a violent death<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:474, 564|<b>G3144</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; a <i>witness</i> (literally [judicially] or figuratively [generally]); by analogy a "martyr": - martyr, record, witness.<br />|3144|
