Μαθθίας|Maqq�aj|mahhias|Matthias = "gift of God"<br />1) the apostle elected to fill the place of the traitor Judas<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G3159</b><br />Apparently a shortened form of G3161; <i>Matthias</i> (that is, <i>Mattithjah</i>), an Israelite: - Matthias.<br />|3159|
Ματταθά|Mattaq�|mattaha|Mattatha = "givingness"<br />1) an ancestor of Christ<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G3160</b><br />Probably a shortened form of G3161 (compare [H4992]); <i>Mattatha</i> (that is, <i>Mattithjah</i>), an Israelite: - Mattatha.<br />|3160|
Ματταθίας|Mattaq�aj|mattahias|Mattathias = "gift of Jehovah"<br />1) the son of Amos, in the genealogy of Christ<br />2) Mattathias was the son of Semei in the genealogy of Christ<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G3161</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H4993]; <i>Mattathias</i> (that is, <i>Mattithjah</i>), an Israelite and Christian: - Mattathias.<br />|3161|
μάχαιρα|m�caira|maxaira|1) a large knife, used for killing animals and cutting up flesh<br />2) a small sword, as distinguished from a large sword<br />2a) curved sword, for a cutting stroke<br />2b) a straight sword, for thrusting<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:524, 572|<b>G3162</b><br />Probably feminine of a presumed derivative of G3163; a <i>knife</i>, that is, <i>dirk</i>; figuratively <i>war</i>, judicial <i>punishment:</i> - sword.<br />|3162|
μάχη|m�ch|maxg|1) a fight or combat<br />1a) of those in arms, a battle<br />1b) of persons at variance, disputants etc., strife, contention<br />1c) a quarrel<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:527, 573|<b>G3163</b><br />From G3164; a <i>battle</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>controversy:</i> - fighting, strive, striving.<br />|3163|
