αὐχέω|a�c�w|auxez|1) to be grandiloquent<br />2) to boast great things, to bear one's self loftily in speech or action<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3166</b><br />From a compound of G3173 and <span class="uni">αὐχέω</span> auche&ocirc; (to <i>boast</i>; akin to G837 and G2744); to <i>talk big</i>, that is, <i>be grandiloquent</i> (<i>arrogant</i>, <i>egotistic</i>): - boast great things.<br />|3166|
μεγαλεῖος|megale�on|mecaleipn|1) magnificent, excellent, splendid, wonderful<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:541, 573|<b>G3167</b><br />From G3173; <i>magnificent</i>, that is, (neuter plural as noun) a conspicuous <i>favor</i>, or (subjectively) <i>perfection:</i> - great things, wonderful works.<br />|3167|
μεγαλειότης|megalei�thj|mecaleiptgs|1) greatness, magnificence<br />1a) of the majesty of God<br />1b) of the visible splendour of the divine majesty as it appeared in the transfiguration of Christ<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:541, 573|<b>G3168</b><br />From G3167; <i>superbness</i>, that is, <i>glory</i> or <i>splendor:</i> - magnificence, majesty, mighty power.<br />|3168|
μεγαλοπρεπής|megaloprep�j|mecalpqreqgs|1) befitting a great man, magnificent, splendid<br />2) full of majesty, majestic<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:542, 573|<b>G3169</b><br />From G3173 and G4241; <i>befitting greatness</i> or <i>magnificence</i> (<i>majestic</i>): - excellent.<br />|3169|
μεγαλύνω|megal�nw|mecalunz|1) to make great, magnify<br />1a) metaphorically to make conspicuous<br />2) to deem or declare great<br />2a) to esteem highly, to extol, laud, celebrate<br />3) to get glory and praise<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:543, 573|<b>G3170</b><br />From G3173; to <i>make</i> (or <i>declare</i>) <i>great</i>, that is, <i>increase</i> or (figuratively) <i>extol:</i> - enlarge, magnify, shew great.<br />|3170|
μεγάλως|meg�lwj|mecalzs|1) greatly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3171</b><br />Adverb from G3173; <i>much:</i> - greatly.<br />|3171|
μεγαλωσύνη|megalws�nh|mecalzsung|1) majesty<br />1a) of the majesty of God<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:544, 573|<b>G3172</b><br />From G3173; <i>greatness</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>divinity</i> (often <i>God</i> himself): - majesty.<br />|3172|
μέγας|m�gaj|mecas|1) great<br />1a) of the external form or sensible appearance of things (or of persons)<br />1a1) in particular, of space and its dimensions, as respects<br />1a1a) mass and weight: great<br />1a1b) compass and extent: large, spacious<br />1a1c) measure and height: long<br />1a1d) stature and age: great, old<br />1b) of number and quantity: numerous, large, abundant<br />1c) of age: the elder<br />1d) used of intensity and its degrees: with great effort, of the affections and emotions of the mind, of natural events powerfully affecting the senses: violent, mighty, strong<br />2) predicated of rank, as belonging to<br />2a) persons, eminent for ability, virtue, authority, power<br />2b) things esteemed highly for their importance: of great moment, of great weight, importance<br />2c) a thing to be highly esteemed for its excellence: excellent<br />3) splendid, prepared on a grand scale, stately<br />4) great things<br />4a) of God's preeminent blessings<br />4b) of things which overstep the province of a created being, proud (presumptuous) things, full of arrogance, derogatory to the majesty of God<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:529, 573|<b>G3173</b><br />Including the prolonged forms, femine <span class="uni">μεγάλη</span> megal&ecirc;, plural <span class="uni">μέγάλοι</span> megaloi, etc.; compare also G3176, G3187], <i>big</i> (literally or figuratively, in a very wide application): - (+ fear) exceedingly, great (-est), high, large, loud, mighty, + (be) sore (afraid), strong, X to years.<br />|3173|
μέγεθος|m�geqoj|mecehps|1) greatness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:544, 573|<b>G3174</b><br />From G3173; <i>magnitude</i> (figuratively): - greatness.<br />|3174|
μεγιστάν|megist�n|mecistan|1) the grandees, magnates, nobles, chief men<br />1a) of a city or a people<br />1b) of the associates or courtiers of a king<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G3175</b><br />Plural from G3176; <i>grandees:</i> - great men, lords.<br />|3175|
μέγιστος|m�gistoj|mecistps|1) greatest, very great<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3176</b><br />Superlative of G3173; <i>greatest</i> or <i>very great:</i> - exceeding great.<br />|3176|
μεθερμηνεύω|meqermhne�w|mehermgneuz|1) to translate into the language of one with whom I wish to communicate, to interpret<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3177</b><br />From G3326 and G2059; to <i>explain over</i>, that is, <i>translate:</i> - (by) interpret (-ation).<br />|3177|
μέθη|m�qh|mehg|1) intoxication<br />2) drunkenness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:545, 576|<b>G3178</b><br />Apparently a primary word; an <i>intoxicant</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>intoxication:</i> - drunkenness.<br />|3178|
μεθίστημι|meq�sthmi|mehistgmi|1) to transpose, transfer, remove from one place to another<br />1a) of change of situation or place<br />1b) to remove from the office of a steward<br />1c) to depart from life, to die<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3179</b><br />From G3326 and G2476; (second form used at 1Co 13:2) to <i>transfer</i>, that is, <i>carry away</i>, <i>depose</i> or (figuratively) <i>exchange</i>, <i>seduce:</i> - put out, remove, translate, turn away.<br />|3179|
μεθοδεία|meqode�a|mehpdeia|1) cunning arts, deceit, craft, trickery<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:102, 666|<b>G3180</b><br />From a compound of G3326 and G3593 [compare "method"]; <i>traveling over</i>, that is, <i>travesty</i>, (<i>trickery</i>): - wile, lie in wait.<br />|3180|
μεθοριος|meqorioj|mehprips|1) a border, frontier<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G3181</b><br />From G3326 and G3725; <i>bounded alongside</i>, that is, <i>contiguous</i> (neuter plural as noun, <i>frontier</i>): - border.<br />|3181|
μεθύσκομαι|meq�skomai|mehuskpmai|1) to intoxicate, make drunk<br />2) to get drunk, become intoxicated<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:545,*|<b>G3182</b><br />A prolonged (transitive) form of G3184; to <i>intoxicate:</i> - be drunk (-en).<br />|3182|
μέθυσος|m�qusoj|mehusps|1) drunken, intoxicated<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:545, 576|<b>G3183</b><br />From G3184; <i>tipsy</i>, that is, (as noun) a <i>sot:</i> - drunkard.<br />|3183|
μεθύω|meq�w|mehuz|1) to be drunken<br />2) metaphorically of one who has shed blood or murdered profusely<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:545, 576|<b>G3184</b><br />From another form of G3178; to <i>drink</i> to <i>intoxication</i>, that is, <i>get drunk:</i> - drink well, make (be) drunk (-en).<br />|3184|
