μέλας|m�laj|melas|1) black<br />2) black ink<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:549, 577|<b>G3189</b><br />Apparently a primary word; <i>black:</i> - black.<br />|3189|
Μελεά|Mele�|melea|Melea = "my dear friend: object of care"<br />1) the son of Joseph in the genealogy of Christ<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G3190</b><br />Of uncertain origin; <i>Meleas</i>, an Israelite: - Meleas.<br />|3190|
μελετάω|melet�w|meletaz|1) to care for, attend to carefully, practise<br />2) to meditate, i.e. to devise, contrive<br />2a) used of the Greeks of the meditative pondering and the practice of orators and rhetoricians<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3191</b><br />From a presumed derivative of G3199; to <i>take care of</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>revolve</i> in the mind: - imagine, (pre-) meditate.<br />|3191|
μέλι|m�li|meli|1) honey<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:552, 577|<b>G3192</b><br />Apparently a primary word; <i>honey:</i> - honey.<br />|3192|
μελισσιος|melissioj|melissips|1) of bees, made by bees<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3193</b><br />From G3192; <i>relating to honey</i>, that is, <i>bee</i> (comb): - honeycomb.<br />|3193|
Μελίτη|Mel�th|melitg|Melita = "honey"<br />1) the name of an island in the Mediterranean, lying between Africa and Sicily, now called Malta<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G3194</b><br />Of uncertain origin; <i>Melita</i>, an island in the Mediterranean: - Melita.<br />|3194|
μέλλω|m�llw|mellz|1) to be about<br />1a) to be on the point of doing or suffering something<br />1b) to intend, have in mind, think to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3195</b><br />A strengthened form of G3199 (through the idea of <i>expectation</i>); to <i>intend</i>, that is, <i>be about</i> to be, do, or suffer something (of persons or things, especially events; in the sense of <i>purpose</i>, <i>duty</i>, <i>necessity</i>, <i>probability</i>, <i>possibility</i>, or <i>hesitation</i>): - about, after that, be (almost), (that which is, things, + which was for) to come, intend, was to (be), mean, mind, be at the point, (be) ready, + return, shall (begin), (which, that) should (after, afterwards, hereafter) tarry, which was for, will, would, be yet.<br />|3195|
μέλος|m�loj|melps|1) a member, limb: a member of the human body<br />1a) of bodies given up to criminal intercourse, because they are as it were members belonging to the harlot's body<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:555, 577|<b>G3196</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; a <i>limb</i> or <i>part</i> of the body: - member.<br />|3196|
Μελχί|Melc�|melxi|1) the son of Janna in the genealogy of Christ<br />2) Melchi was the son of Addi in the genealogy of Christ<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G3197</b><br />Of Hebrew origin ([H4428] with pronominal suffix, <i>my king</i>); <i>Melchi</i> (that is, <i>Malki</i>), the name of two Israelites: - Melchi.<br />|3197|
Μελχισέδεκ|Melcis�dek|melxisedek|Melchizedek = "king of righteousness"<br />1) the king of Salem and priest of the most high God, who lived in the days of Abraham<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:568,*|<b>G3198</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H4442]; <i>Melchisedek</i> (that is, <i>Malkitsedek</i>), a patriarch: - Melchisedec.<br />|3198|
μέλει|m�lei|melei|1) to care about<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3199</b><br />A primary verb; to <i>be of interest</i> to, that is, to <i>concern</i> (only third person singular present indicative used impersonally <i>it matters</i>): - (take) care.<br />|3199|
μεμβράνα|membr�na|membrana|1) parchment, made first of dressed skins at Pergamos, hence its name<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G3200</b><br />Of Latin origin ("membrane"); a (written) sheep <i>skin:</i> - parchment.<br />|3200|
μέμφομαι|m�mfomai|memvpmai|1) to blame, find fault<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:571, 580|<b>G3201</b><br />Middle voice of an apparently primary verb; to <i>blame:</i> - find fault.<br />|3201|
μεμψίμοιρος|memy�moiroj|memyimpirps|1) complaining of one's lot, querulous, discontented<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:571, 580|<b>G3202</b><br />From a presumed derivative of G3201 and <span class="uni">μοῖρα</span> moira (<i>fate</i>; akin to the base of G3313); <i>blaming fate</i>, that is, <i>querulous</i> (<i>discontented</i>): - complainer.<br />|3202|
μέν|m�n|men|1) truly, certainly, surely, indeed<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> particle|<b>G3303</b><br />A primary particle; properly indicative of <i>affirmation</i> or <i>concession</i> (<i>in fact</i>); usually followed by a <i>contrasted</i> clause with G1161 (<i>this</i> one, the <i>former</i>, etc.: - even, indeed, so, some, truly, verily. Often compounded with other particles in an <i>intensive</i> or <i>asseverative</i> sense.<br />|3303|
μενοῦν|meno�n|menpun|1) nay surely, nay rather<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> particle|<b>G3304</b><br />From G3303 and G3767 and G1065; <i>so then at least:</i> - nay but, yea doubtless (rather, verily).<br />|3304|
μέντοι|m�ntoi|mentpi|1) but yet, nevertheless, howbeit<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> particle|<b>G3305</b><br />From G3303 and G5104; <i>indeed though</i>, that is, <i>however:</i> - also, but, howbeit, nevertheless, yet.<br />|3305|
μένω|m�nw|menz|1) to remain, abide<br />1a) in reference to place<br />1a1) to sojourn, tarry<br />1a2) not to depart<br />1a2a) to continue to be present<br />1a2b) to be held, kept, continually<br />1b) in reference to time<br />1b1) to continue to be, not to perish, to last, endure<br />1b1a) of persons, to survive, live<br />1c) in reference to state or condition<br />1c1) to remain as one, not to become another or different<br />2) to wait for, await one<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:574, 581|<b>G3306</b><br />A primary verb; to <i>stay</i> (in a given place, state, relation or expectancy): - abide, continue, dwell, endure, be present, remain, stand, tarry (for), X thine own.<br />|3306|
μερίζω|mer�zw|merifz|1) to divide<br />1a) to separate into parts, cut into pieces<br />1a1) to divide into parties, i.e. be split into factions<br />1b) to distribute<br />1b1) a thing among people<br />1b2) bestow, impart<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3307</b><br />From G3313; to <i>part</i>, that is, (literally) to <i>apportion</i>, bestow, share, or (figuratively) to <i>disunite</i>, <i>differ:</i> - deal, be difference between, distribute, divide, give part.<br />|3307|
μέριμνα|m�rimna|merimna|1) care, anxiety<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:589, 584|<b>G3308</b><br />From G3307 (through the idea of <i>distraction</i>); <i>solicitude:</i> - care.<br />|3308|
μεριμνάω|merimn�w|merimnaz|1) to be anxious<br />1a) to be troubled with cares<br />2) to care for, look out for (a thing)<br />2a) to seek to promote one's interests<br />2b) caring or providing for<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:589, 584|<b>G3309</b><br />From G3308; to <i>be anxious</i> about: - (be, have) care (-ful), take thought.<br />|3309|
μερίς|mer�j|meris|1) a part as distinct from the whole<br />2) an assigned part, a portion, share<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G3310</b><br />Feminine of G3313; a <i>portion</i>, that is, <i>province</i>, <i>share</i> or (abstractly) <i>participation:</i> - part (X -akers).<br />|3310|
μερισμός|merism�j|merismps|1) a division, partition<br />1a) distribution (of various kinds)<br />2) a separation<br />2a) so far as to cleave asunder or separate<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G3311</b><br />From G3307; a <i>separation</i> or <i>distribution:</i> - dividing asunder, gift.<br />|3311|
μεριστής|merist�j|meristgs|1) a divider<br />1a) of an inheritance<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G3312</b><br />From G3307; an <i>apportioner</i> (<i>administrator</i>): - divider.<br />|3312|
μέρος|m�roj|merps|1) a part<br />1a) a part due or assigned to one<br />1b) lot, destiny<br />2) one of the constituent parts of a whole<br />2a) in part, partly, in a measure, to some degree, as respects a part, severally, individually<br />2b) any particular, in regard to this, in this respect<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:594, 585|<b>G3313</b><br />From an obsolete but more primary form of <span class="uni">μείρομαι</span> meiromai (to <i>get</i> as a <i>section</i> or <i>allotment</i>); a <i>division</i> or <i>share</i> (literally or figuratively, in a wide application): - behalf, coast, course, craft, particular (+ -ly), part (+ -ly), piece, portion, respect, side, some sort (-what).<br />|3313|
μεσημβρία|meshmbr�a|mesgmbria|1) as respects to time: noon<br />2) as respects to locality<br />2a) the south<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G3314</b><br />From G3319 and G2250; <i>midday</i>; by implication the <i>south:</i> - noon, south.<br />|3314|
μεσιτεύω|mesite�w|mesiteuz|1) to act as a mediator between litigating or covenanting parties<br />1a) to accomplish something by interposing between two parties<br />1b) to mediate<br />2) act as a sponsor or surety<br />2a) to pledge one's self, give surety<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:598, 585|<b>G3315</b><br />From G3316; to <i>interpose</i> (as arbiter), that is, (by implication) to <i>ratify</i> (as surety): - confirm.<br />|3315|
μεσίτης|mes�thj|mesitgs|1) one who intervenes between two, either in order to make or restore peace and friendship, or form a compact, or for ratifying a covenant<br />2) a medium of communication, arbitrator<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:598, 585|<b>G3316</b><br />From G3319; a <i>go between</i>, that is, (simply) an <i>internunciator</i>, or (by implication) a <i>reconciler</i> (<i>intercessor</i>): - mediator.<br />|3316|
μεσονύκτιον|meson�ktion|mespnuktipn|1) midnight<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G3317</b><br />Neuter of a compound of G3319 and G3571; <i>midnight</i> (especially as a watch): - midnight.<br />|3317|
Μεσοποταμία|Mesopotam�a|mespqptamia|Mesopotamia = "between two rivers"<br />1) the entire country between the two rivers, the Tigris and the Euphrates<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G3318</b><br />From G3319 and G4215; <i>Mesopotamia</i> (as lying between the Euphrates and the Tigris; compare [H763]), a region of Asia: - Mesopotamia.<br />|3318|
μέσος|m�soj|mesps|1) middle<br />2) the midst<br />3) in the midst of, amongst<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3319</b><br />From G3326; <i>middle</i> (as adjective or [neuter] noun): - among, X before them, between, + forth, mid [-day, -night], midst, way.<br />|3319|
μεσότοιχον|mes�toicon|mesptpixpn|1) a partition wall<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:625, 589|<b>G3320</b><br />From G3319 and G5109; a <i>partition</i> (figuratively): - middle wall.<br />|3320|
μεσουράνημα|mesour�nhma|mespurangma|1) mid-heaven<br />2) the highest point in the heavens, which the sun occupies at noon, where what is done can be seen and heard by all<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G3321</b><br />From a presumed compound of G3319 and G3772; <i>mid-sky:</i> - midst of heaven.<br />|3321|
μεσόω|mes�w|mespz|1) to be in the middle, be midway<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3322</b><br />From G3319; to <i>form</i> the <i>middle</i>, that is, (in point of time), to <i>be half way</i> over: - be about the midst.<br />|3322|
Μεσσίας|Mess�aj|messias|Messias = "anointed"<br />1) the Greek form of Messiah<br />2) a name of Christ<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:493, 1322|<b>G3323</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H4899]; the <i>Messias</i> (that is, <i>Mashiach</i>), or Christ: - Messias.<br />|3323|
μεστός|mest�j|mestps|1) full<br />1a) in reference to persons, whose minds are as it were filled with thoughts and emotions, either good or bad<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3324</b><br />Of uncertain derivative; <i>replete</i> (literally or figuratively): - full.<br />|3324|
μεστόω|mest�w|mestpz|1) to fill, be full<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3325</b><br />From G3324; to <i>replenish</i>, that is, (by implication) to <i>intoxicate:</i> - fill.<br />|3325|
μετά|met�|meta|1) with, after, behind<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> preposition<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:766, 1102|<b>G3326</b><br />A primary preposition (often used adverbially); properly denoting <i>accompaniment</i>; "amid" (local or causal); modified variously according to the case (genitive case <i>association</i>, or accusative case <i>succession</i>) with which it is joined; occupying an intermediate position between G575 or G1537 and G1519 or G4314; less intimate than G1722, and less close than G4862)<i>:</i> - after (-ward),X that he again, against, among, X and, + follow, hence, hereafter, in, of, (up-) on, + our, X and setting, since, (un-) to, + together, when, with (+ -out). Often used in composition, in substantially the same relations of <i>participation</i> or <i>proximity</i>, and <i>transfer</i> or <i>sequence</i>.<br />|3326|
μεταβαίνω|metaba�nw|metabainz|1) to pass over from one place to another, to remove, depart<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:523, 90|<b>G3327</b><br />From G3326 and the base of G939; to <i>change place:</i> - depart, go, pass, remove.<br />|3327|
μεταβάλλομαι|metab�llomai|metaballpmai|1) to turn around, to turn about<br />2) to turn one's self about, or transform one's self<br />3) to change one's opinion<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3328</b><br />From G3326 and G906; to <i>throw over</i>, that is, (middle voice, figuratively) to <i>turn about</i> in opinion: - change mind.<br />|3328|
μετάγω|met�gw|metacz|1) to transfer, lead over<br />2) to direct<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3329</b><br />From G3326 and G71; to <i>lead over</i>, that is, <i>transfer</i> (<i>direct</i>): - turn about.<br />|3329|
μεταδίδωμι|metad�dwmi|metadidzmi|1) to impart<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3330</b><br />From G3326 and G1325; to <i>give over</i>, that is, <i>share:</i> - give, impart.<br />|3330|
μετάθεσις|met�qesij|metahesis|1) transfer: from one place to another<br />2) to change<br />2a) of things instituted or established<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:161, 1176|<b>G3331</b><br />From G3346; <i>transposition</i>, that is, <i>transferral</i> (to heaven), <i>disestablishment</i> (of a law): - change, removing, translation.<br />|3331|
μεταίρω|meta�rw|metairz|1) to lift up and remove from one place to another, to transfer<br />2) to go away, depart<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3332</b><br />From G3326 and G142; to <i>betake</i> oneself, that is, <i>remove</i> (locally): - depart.<br />|3332|
μετακαλέομαι|metakal�omai|metakalepmai|1) to call from one place to another, to summon<br />2) to call one's self<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:496, 394|<b>G3333</b><br />From G3326 and G2564; to <i>call elsewhere</i>, that is, <i>summon:</i> - call (for, hither).<br />|3333|
μετακινέω|metakin�w|metakinez|1) to move from a place, to move away<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:720, 435|<b>G3334</b><br />From G3326 and G2795; to <i>stir</i> to a place <i>elsewhere</i>, that is, <i>remove</i> (figuratively): - move away.<br />|3334|
μεταλαμβάνω|metalamb�nw|metalambanz|1) to be or to be made a partner<br />2) to partake of, take [some] food<br />3) of a thing, to get, find (a whole)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:10, 495|<b>G3335</b><br />From G3326 and G2983; to <i>participate</i>; generally to <i>accept</i> (and use): - eat, have, be partaker, receive, take.<br />|3335|
μετάλημψις|met�lhmyij|metalgmyis|1) a taking, participation<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:10, 495|<b>G3336</b><br />From G3335; <i>participation:</i> - taking.<br />|3336|
μεταλλάσσω|metall�ssw|metallassz|1) to exchange, change<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:259, 40|<b>G3337</b><br />From G3326 and G236; to <i>exchange:</i> - change.<br />|3337|
μεταμέλομαι|metam�lomai|metamelpmai|1) it is a care to one afterwards<br />1a) it repents one, to repent one's self<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:626, 589|<b>G3338</b><br />From G3326 and the middle of G3199; to <i>care afterwards</i>, that is, <i>regret:</i> - repent (self).<br />|3338|
μεταμορφόομαι|metamorf�omai|metamprvppmai|1) to change into another form, to transform, to transfigure<br />1a) Christ appearance was changed and was resplendent with divine brightness on the mount of transfiguration<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:755, 607|<b>G3339</b><br />From G3326 and G3445; to <i>transform</i> (literally or figuratively "metamorphose"): - change, transfigure, transform.<br />|3339|
μετανοέω|metano�w|metanpez|1) to change one's mind, i.e. to repent<br />2) to change one's mind for better, heartily to amend with abhorrence of one's past sins<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:975, 636|<b>G3340</b><br />From G3326 and G3539; to <i>think differently</i> or <i>afterwards</i>, that is, <i>reconsider</i> (morally to <i>feel compunction</i>): - repent.<br />|3340|
μετάνοια|met�noia|metanpia|1) a change of mind, as it appears to one who repents, of a purpose he has formed or of something he has done<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:975, 636|<b>G3341</b><br />From G3340; (subjectively) <i>compunction</i> (for guilt, including <i>reformation</i>); by implication <i>reversal</i> (of [another's] decision): - repentance.<br />|3341|
μεταξύ|metax�|metaou|1) between<br />1a) meanwhile, in the mean time<br />2) after, afterwards<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3342</b><br />From G3326 and a form of G4862; <i>betwixt</i> (of place or person); (of time) as adjective <i>intervening</i>, or (by implication) <i>adjoining:</i> - between, mean while, next.<br />|3342|
μεταπέμπομαι|metap�mpomai|metaqemqpmai|1) to send one after another<br />2) like our send after, i.e. to send for<br />3) to send after for one's self, cause to be sent<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3343</b><br />From G3326 and G3992; to <i>send</i> from <i>elsewhere</i>, that is, (middle voice) to <i>summon</i> or <i>invite:</i> - call (send) for.<br />|3343|
μεταστρέφω|metastr�fw|metastrevz|1) to turn around, turn around<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:729, 1093|<b>G3344</b><br />From G3326 and G4762; to <i>turn across</i>, that is, <i>transmute</i> or (figuratively) <i>corrupt:</i> - pervert, turn.<br />|3344|
μετασχηματίζω|metaschmat�zw|metasxgmatifz|1) to change the figure of, to transform<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:957, 1129|<b>G3345</b><br />From G3326 and a derivative of G4976; to <i>transfigure</i> or <i>disguise</i>; figuratively to <i>apply</i> (by accommodation): - transfer, transform (self).<br />|3345|
μετατίθημι|metat�qhmi|metatihgmi|1) to transpose (two things, one of which is put in place of the other)<br />1a) to transfer<br />1b) to change<br />1c) to transfer one's self or suffer one's self to be transferred<br />1c1) to go or pass over<br />1c2) to fall away or desert from one person or thing to another<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:161, 1176|<b>G3346</b><br />From G3326 and G5087; to <i>transfer</i>, that is, (literally) <i>transport</i>, (by implication) <i>exchange</i>, (reflexively) <i>change sides</i>, or (figuratively) <i>pervert:</i> - carry over, change, remove, translate, turn.<br />|3346|
μετέπειτα|met�peita|meteqeita|1) afterwards, after that<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3347</b><br />From G3326 and G1899; <i>thereafter:</i> - afterward.<br />|3347|
μετέχω|met�cw|metexz|1) to be or become partaker<br />2) to partake<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:830, 286|<b>G3348</b><br />From G3326 and G2192; to <i>share</i> or <i>participate</i>; by implication <i>belong</i> to, <i>eat</i> (or <i>drink</i>): - be partaker, pertain, take part, use.<br />|3348|
μετεωρίζομαι|metewr�zomai|metezrifpmai|1) to rise up on high<br />1a) to put a ship [out to sea] up upon the deep<br />1b) to raise up fortifications<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) to lift up one's soul, raise his spirits<br />2a1) to buoy up with hope<br />2a2) to inflate with pride<br />2a3) to be elated<br />2a4) to take one airs, be puffed up with pride<br />2b) by a metaphor taken from ships that are tossed about on the deep by winds and waves<br />2b1) to cause one to waver or fluctuate in the mind<br />2b2) to agitate or harass with cares<br />2b3) to make anxious<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:630,*|<b>G3349</b><br />From a compound of G3326 and a collateral form of G142 or perhaps rather of G109 (compare "meteor"); to <i>raise in mid-air</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>suspend</i> (passively <i>fluctuate</i> or <i>be anxious</i>): - be of doubtful mind.<br />|3349|
μετοικεσία|metoikes�a|metpikesia|1) removal from one abode to another, especially a forced removal<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G3350</b><br />From a derivative of a compound of G3326 and G3624; a <i>change of abode</i>, that is, (specifically) <i>expatriation:</i> - X brought, carried (-ying) away (in-) to.<br />|3350|
μετοικίζω|metoik�zw|metpikifz|1) to transfer settlers<br />2) to cause to remove into another land<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3351</b><br />From the same as G3350; to <i>transfer</i> as a <i>settler</i> or <i>captive</i>, that is, <i>colonize</i> or <i>exile:</i> - carry away, remove into.<br />|3351|
μετοχή|metoc�|metpxg|1) a sharing, communion, fellowship<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:830, 286|<b>G3352</b><br />From G3348; <i>participation</i>, that is, <i>intercourse:</i> - fellowship.<br />|3352|
μέτοχος|m�tocoj|metpxps|1) sharing in, partaking<br />2) a partner (in a work, office, dignity)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:830, 286|<b>G3353</b><br />From G3348; <i>participant</i>, that is, (as noun) a <i>sharer</i>; by implication an <i>associate:</i> - fellow, partaker, partner.<br />|3353|
μετρέω|metr�w|metrez|1) to measure, to measure out or off<br />1a) any space or distance with a measurer's reed or rule<br />1b) metaphorically to judge according to any rule or standard, to estimate<br />2) to measure out, mete out to, i.e. to give by measure<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:632, 590|<b>G3354</b><br />From G3358; to <i>measure</i> (that is, ascertain in size by a fixed standard); by implication to <i>admeasure</i> (that is, allot by rule); figuratively to <i>estimate:</i> - measure, mete.<br />|3354|
μετρητής|metrht�j|metrgtgs|1) a measurer, the name of a utensil known as a amphora, which is a species of measure used for liquids and containing somewhat less the nine English gallons or about (40 l)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G3355</b><br />From G3354; a <i>measurer</i>, that is, (specifically) a certain standard <i>measure</i> of capacity for liquids: - firkin.<br />|3355|
μετριοπαθέω|metriopaq�w|metripqahez|1) to be affected moderately or in due measure<br />2) to preserve moderation in the passions, especially anger or grief<br />2a) of one who is not unduly disturbed by the errors, faults, sins of others, but bears them gently<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:938, 798|<b>G3356</b><br />From a compound of the base of G3357 and G3806; to <i>be moderate in passion</i>, that is, <i>gentle</i> (to <i>treat indulgently</i>): - have compassion.<br />|3356|
μετρίως|metr�wj|metrizs|1) in due measure<br />2) moderately, exceedingly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3357</b><br />Adverb from a derivative of G3358; <i>moderately</i>, that is, <i>slightly:</i> - a little.<br />|3357|
μέτρον|m�tron|metrpn|1) measure, an instrument for measuring<br />1a) a vessel for receiving and determining the quantity of things, whether dry or liquid<br />1b) a graduated staff for measuring, a measuring rod<br />1c) proverbially, the rule or standard of judgment<br />2) determined extent, portion measured off, measure or limit<br />2a) the required measure, the due, fit, measure<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:632, 590|<b>G3358</b><br />An apparently primary word; a <i>measure</i> ("metre"), literally or figuratively; by implication a limited <i>portion</i> (<i>degree</i>): - measure.<br />|3358|
μέτωπον|m�twpon|metzqpn|1) the space between the eyes, the forehead<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:635, 591|<b>G3359</b><br />From G3326 and <span class="uni">ὤψ; &ocirc;ps</span> (the <i>face</i>); the <i>forehead</i> (as <i>opposite</i> the <i>countenance</i>): - forehead.<br />|3359|
μέχρι(ς)|m�cri|mexri|1) as far as, until<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> particle|<b>G3360</b><br />From G3372; as <i>far as</i>, that is, <i>up to</i> a certain point (as preposition of extent [denoting the <i>terminus</i>, whereas G891 refers especially to the <i>space</i> of time or place intervening] or conjugation): - till, (un-) to, until.<br />|3360|
μή|m�|mg|1) no, not lest<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> particle|<b>G3361</b><br />A primary particle of qualified <i>negation</i> (whereas G3756 expresses an absolute denial); (adverbially) <i>not</i>, (conjugationally) <i>lest</i>; also (as interrogitive implying a <i>negative</i> answer [whereas G3756 expects an <i>affirmative</i> one]); <i>whether</i>: - any, but, (that), X forbear, + God forbid, + lack, lest, neither, never, no (X wise in), none, nor, [can-] not, nothing, that not, un [-taken], without. Often used in compounds in substantially the same relations. See also G3362, G3363, G3364, G3372, G3373, G3375, G3378.<br />|3361|
μηδαμῶς|mhdam�j|mgdamzs|1) by no means<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3365</b><br />Adverb from a compound of G3361 and <span class="uni">ἀμός</span> amos (<i>somebody</i>); <i>by no means:</i> - not so.<br />|3365|
μηδέ|mhd�|mgde|1) and not, but not, nor, not<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> particle|<b>G3366</b><br />From G3361 and G1161; <i>but not</i>, <i>not even</i>; in a continued negation, <i>nor:</i> - neither, nor (yet), (no) not (once, so much as).<br />|3366|
μηδείς|mhde�j|mgdeis|1) nobody, no one, nothing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3367</b><br />The masculine, feminine irregular (second form) and neuter (third form) from G3361 and G1520; <i>not even one</i> (man, woman, thing): - any (man, thing), no (man), none, not (at all, any man, a whit), nothing, + without delay.<br />|3367|
μηδέποτε|mhd�pote|mgdeqpte|1) never<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3368</b><br />From G3366 and G4218; <i>not even ever:</i> - never.<br />|3368|
μηδέπω|mhd�pw|mgdeqz|1) not yet<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3369</b><br />From G3366 and G4452; <i>not even yet:</i> - not yet.<br />|3369|
Μῆδος|M�doj|mgdps|Mede or Media = "middle land"<br />1) a Mede, a native or inhabitant of Media, a well known region of Asia whose chief city was Ecbatana<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G3370</b><br />Of foreign origin (compare [H4074]); a <i>Median</i>, or inhabitant of Media: - Mede.<br />|3370|
μηκέτι|mhk�ti|mgketi|1) no longer, no more, not hereafter<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3371</b><br />From G3361 and G2089; <i>no further:</i> - any longer, (not) henceforth, hereafter, no henceforward (longer, more, soon), not any more.<br />|3371|
μῆκος|m�koj|mgkps|1) length<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G3372</b><br />Probably akin to G3173; <i>length</i> (literally or figuratively): - length.<br />|3372|
μηκύνομαι|mhk�nomai|mgkunpmai|1) to make long, to lengthen<br />2) in the Bible twice of plants, to cause to grow, increase<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3373</b><br />From G3372; to <i>lengthen</i>, that is, (middle voice) to <i>enlarge:</i> - grow up.<br />|3373|
μηλωτή|mhlwt�|mglztg|1) a sheepskin<br />2) an outer robe or mantle since most mantles were made of skins<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:637, 591|<b>G3374</b><br />From <span class="uni">μῆλον</span> m&ecirc;lon (a <i>sheep</i>); a <i>sheep skin:</i> - sheepskin.<br />|3374|
μήν|m�n|mgn|1) a month<br />2) the time of the new moon, new moon (the first day of each month, when the new moon appeared was a festival among the Hebrews)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:638, 591|<b>G3376</b><br />A primary word; a <i>month:</i> - month.<br />|3376|
μηνύω|mhn�w|mgnuz|1) to disclose or make known something secret<br />1a) in a forensic sense, to inform, report<br />2) to declare, tell, make known<br />3) to indicate, intimate<br />3a) of a teacher<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3377</b><br />Probably from the same base as G3145 and G3415 (that is, <span class="uni">μάω</span> ma&ocirc; [to <i>strive</i>]); to <i>disclose</i> (through the idea of mental <i>effort</i> and thus calling to <i>mind</i>), that is, <i>report</i>, <i>declare</i>, <i>intimate:</i> - shew, tell.<br />|3377|
μήποτε|m�pote|mgqpte|1) that ... not, lest, whether perhaps, whether or not, in no way, perhaps<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> conjunction|<b>G3379</b><br />From G3361 and G4218; <i>not ever</i>; also <i>if</i> (or <i>lest</i>) <i>ever</i> (or <i>perhaps</i>): - if peradventure, lest (at any time, haply), not at all, whether or not.<br />|3379|
μήπω|m�pw|mgqz|1) not yet<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3380</b><br />From G3361 and G4452; <i>not yet:</i> - not yet.<br />|3380|
μήπως|m�pwj|mgqzs|1) lest, lest somehow, that perhaps<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> conjunction|<b>G3381</b><br />From G3361 and G4458; <i>lest somehow:</i> - lest (by any means, by some means, haply, perhaps).<br />|3381|
μηρός|mhr�j|mgrps|1) thigh<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G3382</b><br />Perhaps a primary word; a <i>thigh:</i> - thigh.<br />|3382|
μήτε|m�te|mgte|1) and not, neither ... nor, not so<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> conjunction|<b>G3383</b><br />From G3361 and G5037; <i>not too</i>, that is, (in continued negation) <i>neither</i> or <i>nor</i>; also, <i>not even:</i> - neither, (n-) or, so much as.<br />|3383|
μήτηρ|m�thr|mgtgr|1) a mother<br />2) metaphorically the source of something, the motherland<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:642, 592|<b>G3384</b><br />Apparently a primary word; a "mother" (literally or figuratively, immediate or remote): - mother.<br />|3384|
μήτι|m�ti|mgti|1) whether, at all, perchance<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> particle|<b>G3385</b><br />From G3361 and the neuter of G5100; <i>whether at all</i>: - not [the particle usually not expressed, except by the form of the question].<br />|3385|
μήτιγε|m�tige|mgtice|1) to say nothing of, not to mention<br />1a) much less<br />1b) much more, much rather<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> particle|<b>G3386</b><br />From G3385 and G1065; <i>not at all then</i>, that is, <i>not to say</i> (<i>the rather still</i>): - how much more.<br />|3386|
μητις|mhtij|mgtis|1) let no one<br />2) hath any one<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> pronoun|<b>G3387</b><br />From G3361 and G5100; <i>whether any</i>: - any [sometimes unexpressed except by the simple interrogative form of the sentence].<br />|3387|
μήτρα|m�tra|mgtra|1) the womb<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G3388</b><br />From G3384; the <i>matrix:</i> - womb.<br />|3388|
μητρολῴας|mhtrol�aj|mgtrplzas|1) matricide, the murderer of a mother<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G3389</b><br />From G3384 and the base of G257; a <i>mother thresher</i>, that is, <i>matricide:</i> - murderer of mothers.<br />|3389|
μιαίνω|mia�nw|miainz|1) to dye with another colour, to stain<br />2) to defile, pollute, sully, contaminate, soil<br />2a) to defile with sins<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:644, 593|<b>G3392</b><br />Perhaps a primary verb; to <i>sully</i> or <i>taint</i>, that is, <i>contaminate</i> (ceremonially or morally): - defile.<br />|3392|
μίασμα|m�asma|miasma|1) that which defiles, defilement<br />2) metaphorically, vices the foulness of which contaminates one in his intercourse with the ungodly mass of mankind<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:646, 593|<b>G3393</b><br />From G3392 ("miasma"); (morally) <i>foulness</i> (properly the effect): - pollution.<br />|3393|
μιασμός|miasm�j|miasmps|1) the act of defiling, defilement, pollution<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:647, 593|<b>G3394</b><br />From G3392; (morally) <i>contamination</i> (properly the act): - uncleanness.<br />|3394|
μίγμα|m�gma|micma|1) that which has been produced by a mixing, a mixture<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G3395</b><br />From G3396; a <i>compound:</i> - mixture.<br />|3395|
μίγνυμι|m�gnumi|micnumi|1) to mix, mingle<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3396</b><br />A primary verb; to <i>mix:</i> - mingle.<br />|3396|
μικρός|mikr�j|mikrps|1) small, little<br />1a) of size: hence of stature, of length<br />1b) of space<br />1c) of age: less by birth, younger<br />1d) of time: short, brief, a little while, how little!<br />1e) of quantity: i.e. number, amount<br />1f) of rank or influence<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:648, 593|<b>G3398</b><br />Apparently a primary word, including the comparative (second form); <i>small</i> (in size, quantity, number or (figuratively) dignity): - least, less, little, small.<br />|3398|
Μίλητος|M�lhtoj|milgtps|Miletus = "pure white fine wool"<br />1) a maritime city, now nearly 10 miles (16 km), from the coast of Caria or Ionia, near the mouth of the Maeander and 35 miles (55 km) from Ephesus. It was the mother of about eighty colonies, the the birth place of Thales, Anaximander, and other famous men.<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G3399</b><br />Of uncertain origin; <i>Miletus</i>, a city of Asia Minor: - Miletus.<br />|3399|
