νίπτω|n�ptw|niqtz|1) to wash<br />2) to wash one's self<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:946, 635|<b>G3538</b><br />To <i>cleanse</i> (especially the hands or the feet or the face); ceremonially to <i>perform ablution</i>: - wash. Compare G3068.<br />|3538|
νοέω|no�w|npez|1) to perceive with the mind, to understand, to have understanding<br />2) to think upon, heed, ponder, consider<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:948, 636|<b>G3539</b><br />From G3563; to <i>exercise</i> the <i>mind</i> (<i>observe</i>), that is, (figuratively) to <i>comprehend</i>, <i>heed:</i> - consider, perceive, think, understand.<br />|3539|
