νόμισμα|n�misma|npmisma|1) anything received and sanctioned by usage or law<br />2) money, (current) coin, legal tender<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G3546</b><br />From G3543; <i>what is reckoned</i> as of value (after the Latin <i>numisma</i>), that is, current <i>coin:</i> - money.<br />|3546|
νομοδιδάσκαλος|nomodid�skaloj|npmpdidaskalps|1) a teacher and interpreter of the law: among the Jews<br />1a) of those who among Christians went about as champions and interpreters of the Mosaic law<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:159, 161|<b>G3547</b><br />From G3551 and G1320; an <i>expounder of</i> the (Jewish) <i>law</i>, that is, a <i>Rabbi:</i> - doctor (teacher) of the law.<br />|3547|
νομοθεσία|nomoqes�a|npmphesia|1) law giving, legislation<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:1089, 646|<b>G3548</b><br />From G3550; <i>legislation</i> (specifically the <i>institution of</i> the Mosaic <i>code</i>): - giving of the law.<br />|3548|
νομοθετέομαι|nomoqet�omai|npmphetepmai|1) to enact laws<br />1a) laws are enacted or prescribed for one, to be legislated for, furnished with laws<br />2) to sanction by law, enact<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:1090, 646|<b>G3549</b><br />From G3550; to <i>legislate</i>, that is, (passively) to <i>have</i> (the Mosaic) <i>enactments</i> injoined, <i>be sanctioned</i> (by them): - establish, receive the law.<br />|3549|
