ὀπτάνομαι|�pt�nomai|pqtanpmai|1) to look at, behold<br />2) to allow one's self to be seen, to appear<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:315, 706|<b>G3700</b><br />The first a (middle voice) prolonged form of the second (primary) which is used for it in certain tenses; and both as alternates of G3708; to <i>gaze</i> (that is, with wide open eyes, as at something remarkable; and thus differing from G991, which denotes simply <i>voluntary</i> observation; and from G1492, which expresses merely mechanical, passive or casual vision; while G2300, and still more emphatically its intensive G2334, signifies an earnest but more continued <i>inspection</i>; and G4648 a watching <i>from a distance</i>): - appear, look, see, shew self.<br />|3700|
ὀπτασία|�ptas�a|pqtasia|1) the act of exhibiting one's self to view<br />2) a sight, a vision, an appearance presented to one whether asleep or awake<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:372, 706|<b>G3701</b><br />From a presumed derivative of G3700; <i>visuality</i>, that is, (concretely) an <i>apparition:</i> - vision.<br />|3701|
ὀπτός|�pt�j|pqtps|1) cooked, broiled<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3702</b><br />From an obsolete verb akin to <span class="uni">ἕψω; heps&ocirc;</span> (to "<i>steep</i>"); <i>cooked</i>, that is, <i>roasted:</i> - broiled.<br />|3702|
ὀπώρα|�p�ra|pqzra|1) the season which succeeds summer, from the rising of Sirius to that of Arcturus, i.e. from late summer, early autumn, our dog days<br />2) ripe fruits (of trees)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G3703</b><br />Apparently from the base of G3796 and G5610; properly <i>even tide</i> of the (summer) season (<i>dog days</i>), that is, (by implication) <i>ripe</i> fruit: - fruit.<br />|3703|
ὅπως|�pwj|pqzs|1) how, that<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> particle|<b>G3704</b><br />From G3739 nad G4459; <i>what</i> (-ever) <i>how</i>, that is, <i>in</i> the <i>manner that</i> (as adverb or conjugation of coincidence, intentional or actual): - because, how, (so) that, to, when.<br />|3704|
ὅραμα|�rama|prama|1) that which is seen, spectacle<br />2) a sight divinely granted in an ecstasy or in a sleep, a vision<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:371, 706|<b>G3705</b><br />From G3708; <i>something gazed at</i>, that is, a <i>spectacle</i> (especially supernatural): - sight, vision.<br />|3705|
ὅρασις|�rasij|prasis|1) the act of seeing<br />1a) the sense of sight, the eyes<br />2) appearance, visible form<br />3) a vision<br />3a) an appearance divinely granted in an ecstasy or dream<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:370, 706|<b>G3706</b><br />From G3708; the act of <i>gazing</i>, that is, (external) an <i>aspect</i> or (internal) an inspired <i>appearance:</i> - sight, vision.<br />|3706|
ὁρατός|�rat�j|pratps|1) visible, open to view<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:368, 706|<b>G3707</b><br />From G3708; <i>gazed at</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>capable of being seen:</i> - visible.<br />|3707|
ὁράω|�r�w|praz|1) to see with the eyes<br />2) to see with the mind, to perceive, know<br />3) to see, i.e. become acquainted with by experience, to experience<br />4) to see, to look to<br />4a) to take heed, beware<br />4b) to care for, pay heed to<br />5) I was seen, showed myself, appeared<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:315, 706|<b>G3708</b><br />Properly to <i>stare</i> at (compare G3700), that is, (by implication) to <i>discern</i> clearly (physically or mentally); by extension to <i>attend</i> to; by Hebraism to <i>experience</i>; passively to <i>appear:</i> - behold, perceive, see, take heed.<br />|3708|
ὀργή|�rg�|prcg|1) anger, the natural disposition, temper, character<br />2) movement or agitation of the soul, impulse, desire, any violent emotion, but especially anger<br />3) anger, wrath, indignation<br />4) anger exhibited in punishment, hence used for punishment itself<br />4a) of punishments inflicted by magistrates<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:382, 716|<b>G3709</b><br />From G3713; properly <i>desire</i> (as a <i>reaching</i> forth or <i>excitement</i> of the mind), that is, (by analogy) violent <i>passion</i> (<i>ire</i>, or [justifiable] <i>abhorrence</i>); by implication <i>punishment:</i> - anger, indignation, vengeance, wrath.<br />|3709|
ὀργίζομαι|�rg�zomai|prcifpmai|1) to provoke, to arouse to anger<br />2) to be provoked to anger, be angry, be wroth<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:100, 835<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:100, 835<br /><b>A Related Word by Thayer's/Strong's Number: </b>from G3709<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:382,*|<b>G3710</b><br />From G3709; to <i>provoke</i> or <i>enrage</i>, that is, (passively) <i>become exasperated:</i> - be angry (wroth).<br />|3710|
ὀργίλος|�rg�loj|prcilps|1) prone to anger, irascible<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:382, 716|<b>G3711</b><br />From G3709; <i>irascible:</i> - soon angry.<br />|3711|
ὀργυιά|�rgui�|prcuia|1) fathom, the distance across the breast from the tip of one middle finger to the tip of the other when the arms are outstretched, 5 to 6 feet (2 m)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G3712</b><br />From G3713; a <i>stretch</i> of the arms, that is, a <i>fathom:</i> - fathom.<br />|3712|
ὀρέγομαι|�r�gomai|precpmai|1) to stretch one's self out in order to touch or to grasp something, to reach after or desire something<br />2) to give one's self up to the love of money<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:447, 727|<b>G3713</b><br />Middle voice of apparently a prolonged form of an obsolete primary (compare G3735); to <i>stretch</i> oneself, that is, <i>reach</i> out after (<i>long</i> for): - covet after, desire.<br />|3713|
ὀρεινή|�rein�|preing|1) mountainous, hilly<br />2) the mountain district, hill country<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3714</b><br />From G3735; <i>mountainous</i>, that is, (feminine by implication of G5561) the <i>Highlands</i> (of Judaea): - hill country.<br />|3714|
ὄρεξις|�rexij|preois|1) desire, longing, craving for<br />2) eager desire, lust, appetite<br />2a) used both in a good and a bad sense, as well of natural and lawful and even of proper cravings (of appetite for food), also of corrupt and unlawful desires<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:447, 727|<b>G3715</b><br />From G3713; <i>excitement</i> of the mind, that is, <i>longing</i> after: - lust.<br />|3715|
ὀρθοποδέω|�rqopod�w|prhpqpdez|1) to walk in a straight course<br />2) metaphorically to act uprightly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:451, 727|<b>G3716</b><br />From a compound of G3717 and G4228; to <i>be straight footed</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>go directly</i> forward: - walk uprightly.<br />|3716|
ὀρθός|�rq�j|prhps|1) straight, erect<br />1a) upright<br />1b) straight, not crooked<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:449, 727|<b>G3717</b><br />Probably from the base of G3735; <i>right</i> (as <i>rising</i>), that is, (perpendicularly) <i>erect</i> (figuratively <i>honest</i>), or (horizontally) <i>level</i> or <i>direct:</i> - straight, upright.<br />|3717|
ὀρθοτομέω|�rqotom�w|prhptpmez|1) to cut straight, to cut straight ways<br />1a) to proceed on straight paths, hold a straight course, equiv. to doing right<br />2) to make straight and smooth, to handle aright, to teach the truth directly and correctly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:111, 1169|<b>G3718</b><br />From a compound of G3717 and the base of G5114; to <i>make</i> a <i>straight cut</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>dissect</i> (<i>expound</i>) <i>correctly</i> (the divine message): - rightly divide.<br />|3718|
ὀρθρίζω|�rqr�zw|prhrifz|1) to rise early in the morning<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3719</b><br />From G3722; to <i>use</i> the <i>dawn</i>, that is, (by implication) to <i>repair betimes:</i> - come early in the morning.<br />|3719|
ὀρθρινός|�rqrin�j|prhrinps|1) early<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3720</b><br />From G3722; <i>relating to</i> the <i>dawn</i>, that is, <i>matutinal</i> (as an epithet of Venus, especially brilliant in the early day): - morning.<br />|3720|
ὄρθριος|�rqrioj|prhrips|1) early<br />2) rising at the first dawn or very early in the morning<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G3721</b><br />From G3722; <i>in</i> the <i>dawn</i>, that is, up <i>at day break:</i> - early.<br />|3721|
ὄρθρος|�rqroj|prhrps|1) daybreak, dawn<br />2) at early dawn, at daybreak, early in the morning<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G3722</b><br />From the same as G3735; <i>dawn</i> (as <i>sun rise</i>, <i>rising</i> of light); by extension <i>morn:</i> - early in the morning.<br />|3722|
ὀρθῶς|�rq�j|prhzs|1) rightly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3723</b><br />Adverb from G3717; <i>in a straight</i> manner, that is, (figuratively) <i>correctly</i> (also morally): - plain, right (-ly).<br />|3723|
ὁρίζω|�r�zw|prifz|1) to define<br />1a) to mark out the boundaries or limits (of any place or thing)<br />1b1) that which has been determined, acc. to appointment, decree<br />1b2) to ordain, determine, appoint<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:452, 728|<b>G3724</b><br />From G3725; to <i>mark</i> out or <i>bound</i> ("horizon"), that is, (figuratively) to <i>appoint</i>, <i>decree</i>, <i>specify:</i> - declare, determine, limit, ordain.<br />|3724|
ὅριον|�rion|pripn|1) boundaries<br />1a) for a region, district, land, territory<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G3725</b><br />Neuter of a derivative of an apparently primary word <span class="uni">ὅρος</span> horos (a <i>bound</i> or <i>limit</i>); a <i>boundary</i> line, that is, (by implication) a <i>frontier</i> (<i>region</i>): - border, coast.<br />|3725|
ὁρκίζω|�rk�zw|prkifz|1) to force to take an oath, to administer an oath to<br />2) to adjure (solemnly implore)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:462, 729|<b>G3726</b><br />From G3727; to <i>put on oath</i>, that is, <i>make swear</i>; by analogy to solemnly <i>enjoin:</i> - adjure, charge.<br />|3726|
ὅρκος|�rkoj|prkps|1) that which has been pledged or promised with an oath<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:457, 729|<b>G3727</b><br />From <span class="uni">ἕρκος</span> herkos (a <i>fence</i>; perhaps akin to G3725); a <i>limit</i>, that is, (sacred) <i>restraint</i> (specifically <i>oath</i>): - oath.<br />|3727|
ὁρκωμοσία|�rkwmos�a|prkzmpsia|1) affirmation made on oath, the taking of an oath, an oath<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:463, 729|<b>G3728</b><br />From a compound of G3727 and a derivative of G3660; <i>asseveration on oath:</i> - oath.<br />|3728|
ὁρμάω|�rm�w|prmaz|1) to set in rapid motion, stir up, incite, urge on<br />2) to start forward impetuously, to rush<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:467, 730|<b>G3729</b><br />From G3730; to <i>start</i>, <i>spur</i> or <i>urge</i> on, that is, (reflexively) to <i>dash</i> or <i>plunge:</i> - run (violently), rush.<br />|3729|
