ὁροθεσία|�roqes�a|prphesia|1) a setting of boundaries, laying down limits<br />2) a definite limit, bounds<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G3734</b><br />From a compound of the base of G3725 and a derivative of G5087; a <i>limit placing</i>, that is, (concretely) <i>boundary line:</i> - bound.<br />|3734|
ὄρος|�roj|prps|1) a mountain<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:475, 732|<b>G3735</b><br />Probably a from an obsolete word <span class="uni">ὄρω</span> or&ocirc; (to <i>rise</i> or "rear"; perhaps akin to G142; compare G3733); a <i>mountain</i> (as <i>lifting</i> itself above the plain): - hill, mount (-ain).<br />|3735|
