ὀρφανός|�rfan�j|prvanps|1) bereft (of a father, of parents)<br />1a) of those bereft of a teacher, guide, guardian<br />1b) orphaned<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:487, 734|<b>G3737</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; <i>bereaved</i> ("orphan"), that is, <i>parentless:</i> - comfortless, fatherless.<br />|3737|
ὀρχέομαι|�rc�omai|prxepmai|1) to dance<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3738</b><br />Middle voice from<span class="uni">όρχος</span> orchos (a <i>row</i> or <i>ring</i>); to <i>dance</i> (from the <i>ranklike</i> or <i>regular</i> motion): - dance.<br />|3738|
