παντοκράτωρ|pantokr�twr|qantpkratzr|1) he who holds sway over all things<br />2) the ruler of all<br />3) almighty: God<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:914, 466|<b>G3841</b><br />From G3956 and G2904; the <i>all ruling</i>, that is, <i>God</i> (as absolute and universal <i>sovereign</i>): - Almighty, Omnipotent.<br />|3841|
πάντοτε|p�ntote|qantpte|1) at all times, always, ever<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3842</b><br />From G3956 and G3753; <i>every when</i>, that is, <i>at all</i> times: - always (-s), ever (-more).<br />|3842|
πάντως|p�ntwj|qantzs|1) altogether<br />1a) in any and every way, by all means<br />1b) doubtless, surely, certainly<br />1c) in no wise, not at all<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G3843</b><br />From G3956; <i>entirely</i>; specifically <i>at all events</i>, (with negative following) <i>in</i> no <i>event:</i> - by all means, altogether, at all, needs, no doubt, in [no] wise, surely.<br />|3843|
παρά|par�|qara|1) from, of at, by, besides, near<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> preposition<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:727, 771|<b>G3844</b><br />A primary preposition; properly <i>near</i>, that is, (with genitive case) <i>from beside</i> (literally or figuratively), (with dative case) <i>at</i> (or <i>in</i>) the <i>vicinity</i> of (objectively or subjectively), (with accusative case) to the <i>proximity</i> with (local [especially <i>beyond</i> or <i>opposed</i> to] or causal [<i>on account</i> of]). In compounds it retains the same variety of application: - above, against, among, at, before, by, contrary to, X friend, from, + give [such things as they], + that [she] had, X his, in, more than, nigh unto, (out) of, past, save, side . . . by, in the sight of, than, [there-] fore, with. In compounds it retains the same variety of application.<br />|3844|
παραβαίνω|paraba�nw|qarabainz|1) to go by the side of<br />2) to go past or pass over without touching a thing<br />3) to overstep, neglect, violate, transgress<br />4) so to go past as to turn aside from<br />4a) to depart, leave, be turned from<br />5) one who abandons his trust<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:736, 772|<b>G3845</b><br />From G3844 and the base of G939; to <i>go contrary to</i>, that is, <i>violate</i> a command: - (by) transgress (-ion).<br />|3845|
παραβάλλω|parab�llw|qaraballz|1) to throw before, cast to (as fodder for horses)<br />2) to put one thing by the side of another for the sake of comparison, to compare, liken<br />3) to put one's self, betake one's self into a place or to a person<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G3846</b><br />From G3844 and G906; to <i>throw alongside</i>, that is, (reflexively) to <i>reach</i> a place, or (figuratively) to <i>liken:</i> - arrive, compare.<br />|3846|
παράβασις|par�basij|qarabasis|1) a going over<br />2) metaphorically a disregarding, violating<br />2a) of the Mosaic law<br />2b) the breach of a definite, promulgated, ratified law<br />2c) to create transgressions, i.e. that sins might take on the character of transgressions, and thereby the consciousness of sin be intensified and the desire for redemption be aroused<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:739, 772|<b>G3847</b><br />From G3845; <i>violation:</i> - breaking, transgression.<br />|3847|
