πεντηκοστή|penthkost�|qentgkpstg|Pentecost = "the fiftieth day"<br />1) the second of the three great Jewish feasts, celebrated at Jerusalem yearly, the seventh week after the Passover, in grateful recognition of the completed harvest<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:44, 826|<b>G4005</b><br />Feminine of G4004; <i>fiftieth</i> (G2250 being implied) from Passover, that is, the festival of "pentecost": - Pentecost.<br />|4005|
