Πέργαμος|P�rgamoj|qercamps|Pergamos = "height or elevation"<br />1) a city of Mysia Minor, in Asia Minor, the seat of the dynasties of Attalus and Eumenes, famous for its temple of Aesculapius and the invention and manufacture of parchment. The river Selinus flowed through it and the Cetius ran past it. It was the birthplace of the physician Galen, and had a great royal library. It had a Christian church.<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G4010</b><br />From G4444; <i>fortified</i>; <i>Pergamus</i>, a place in Asia Minor: - Pergamos.<br />|4010|
Πέργη|P�rgh|qercg|Perga = "earthy"<br />1) a town in Pamphylia, on the river Cestius, at a distance of 7 miles<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G4011</b><br />Probably from the same as G4010; a <i>tower</i>; <i>Perga</i>, a place in Asia Minor: - Perga.<br />|4011|
περί|per�|qeri|1) about, concerning, on account of, because of, around, near<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> preposition<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:53, 827|<b>G4012</b><br />From the base of G4008; properly <i>through</i> (all <i>over</i>), that is, <i>around</i>; figuratively <i>with respect</i> to; used in various applications, of place, cause or time (with the genitive case denoting the <i>subject</i> or <i>occasion</i> or <i>superlative</i> point; with the accusative case the <i>locality</i>, <i>circuit</i>, <i>matter</i>, <i>circumstance</i> or general <i>period</i>): - (there-) about, above, against, at, on behalf of, X and his company, which concern, (as) concerning, for, X how it will go with, ([there-, where-]) of, on, over, pertaining (to), for sake, X (e-) state, (as) touching, [where-] by (in), with. In compounds it retains substantially the same meaning of circuit (<i>around</i>), excess (<i>beyond</i>), or completeness (<i>through</i>).<br />|4012|
περιάγω|peri�gw|qeriacz|1) to lead around, to lead about with one's self<br />2) to go about, walk about<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4013</b><br />From G4012 and G71; to <i>take around</i> (as a companion); reflexively to <i>walk around:</i> - compass, go (round) about, lead about.<br />|4013|
περιαιρέω|periair�w|qeriairez|1) to take away that which surrounds or envelopes a thing<br />2) metaphorically to take away altogether or entirely<br />2a) the guilt of sin, to expiate perfectly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4014</b><br />From G4012 and G138 (including its alternate); to <i>remove</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>unveil</i>, <i>cast off</i> (anchor); figuratively to <i>expiate:</i> - take away (up).<br />|4014|
περιαστράπτω|periastr�ptw|qeriastraqtz|1) to flash around, shine about<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4015</b><br />From G4012 and G797; to <i>flash</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>envelop in light:</i> - shine round (about).<br />|4015|
περιβάλλω|perib�llw|qeriballz|1) to throw around, to put around<br />1a) to surround a city with a bank (palisade)<br />1b) of garments, to clothe one<br />1b1) to put a thing on one<br />1b2) to clothe one with a thing<br />1c) to put on or clothe one's self<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4016</b><br />From G4012 and G906; to <i>throw</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>invest</i> (with a palisade or with clothing): - array, cast about, clothe (-d me), put on.<br />|4016|
περιβλέπομαι|peribl�pomai|qeribleqpmai|1) to look around<br />2) to look around about one's self<br />3) to look round on one (i.e. to look for one's self at one near by)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4017</b><br />From G4012 and G991; to <i>look</i> all <i>around:</i> - look (round) about (on).<br />|4017|
περιβόλαιον|perib�laion|qeribplaipn|1) a covering thrown around, a wrapper<br />1a) a mantle<br />1b) a veil<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G4018</b><br />Neuter of a presumed derivative of G4016; something <i>thrown around</i> one, that is, a <i>mantle</i>, <i>veil:</i> - covering, vesture.<br />|4018|
περιδέω|perid�w|qeridez|1) to bind around, tie over<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4019</b><br />From G4012 and G1210; to <i>bind around</i> one, that is, <i>enwrap:</i> - bind about.<br />|4019|
περιεργάζομαι|perierg�zomai|qeriercafpmai|1) to bustle about uselessly, to busy one's self about trifling, needless, useless matters<br />1a) used apparently of a person officiously inquisitive about other's affairs<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4020</b><br />From G4012 and G2038; to <i>work</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>bustle about</i> (<i>meddle</i>): - be a busybody.<br />|4020|
περίεργος|per�ergoj|qeriercps|1) busy about trifles and neglectful of important matters<br />1a) especially busy about other folks' affairs, a busybody<br />1b) of things: impertinent and superfluous<br />1b1) of magic arts<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4021</b><br />From G4012 and G2041; <i>working all around</i>, that is, <i>officious</i> (<i>meddlesome</i>, neuter plural <i>magic</i>): - busybody, curious arts.<br />|4021|
περιέρχομαι|peri�rcomai|qerierxpmai|1) to go about<br />1a) of strollers<br />1b) of wanderers<br />1c) of navigators (making a circuit)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:682, 257|<b>G4022</b><br />From G4012 and G2064 (including its alternate); to <i>come</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>stroll</i>, <i>vacillate</i>, <i>veer:</i> - fetch a compass, vagabond, wandering about.<br />|4022|
περιέχω|peri�cw|qeriexz|1) to surround, encompass<br />1a) to contain: of the subject-matter, contents, of a writing<br />1b) to take possession of, to seize<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4023</b><br />From G4012 and G2192; to <i>hold</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>include</i>, <i>clasp</i> (figuratively): - + astonished, contain, after [this manner].<br />|4023|
περιζώννυμι|periz�nnumi|qerifznnumi|1) to fasten garments with a girdle or belt<br />2) to gird one's self<br />3) metaphorically with truth as a girdle<br />3a) to equip one's self with knowledge of the truth<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:302, 702|<b>G4024</b><br />From G4012 and G2224; to <i>gird</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, (middle or passive voice) to <i>fasten on one's belt</i> (literally or figuratively): - gird (about, self).<br />|4024|
περίθεσις|per�qesij|qerihesis|1) the act of putting around<br />2) the adornment consisting of the golden ornaments wont to be placed around the head or the body<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4025</b><br />From G4060; a <i>putting</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>decorating</i> oneself with: - wearing.<br />|4025|
περιΐστημι|peri�sthmi|qeriistgmi|1) to place around one<br />2) to stand around<br />2a) to turn one's self about for the purpose of avoiding something<br />2b) to avoid, shun<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4026</b><br />From G4012 and G2476; to <i>stand</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, (near) to <i>be a bystander</i>, or (aloof) to <i>keep away</i> from: - avoid, shun, stand by (round about).<br />|4026|
περικάθαρμα|perik�qarma|qerikaharma|1) off scouring, refuse<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) the most abject and despicable men<br />2b) the price of expiation or redemption, because the Greeks used to apply the term "katharmata" to victims sacrificed to make expiation for the people, and even to criminals who were maintained at the public expense, that on the outbreak of a pestilence or other calamity they might be offered as sacrifices to make expiation for the state<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:430, 381|<b>G4027</b><br />From a compound of G4012 and G2508; something <i>cleaned</i> off all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>refuse</i> (figuratively): - filth.<br />|4027|
περικαλύπτω|perikal�ptw|qerikaluqtz|1) to cover all around, to cover up, cover over<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4028</b><br />From G4012 and G2572; to <i>cover</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>entirely</i> (the face, a surface): - blindfold, cover, overlay.<br />|4028|
περίκειμαι|per�keimai|qerikeimai|1) to lie around<br />2) to be compassed with, have round one<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:656, 425|<b>G4029</b><br />From G4012 and G2749; to <i>lie</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>inclose</i>, <i>encircle</i>, <i>hamper</i> (literally or figuratively): - be bound (compassed) with, hang about.<br />|4029|
περικεφαλαία|perikefala�a|qerikevalaia|1) a helmet<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) the protection of the soul which consists in (the hope of) salvation<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:314, 702|<b>G4030</b><br />Feminine of a compound of G4012 and G2776; <i>encirclement of</i> the <i>head</i>, that is, a <i>helmet:</i> - helmet.<br />|4030|
