περιπατέω|peripat�w|qeriqatez|1) to walk<br />1a) to make one's way, progress; to make due use of opportunities<br />1b) Hebrew for, to live<br />1b1) to regulate one's life<br />1b2) to conduct one's self<br />1b3) to pass one's life<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:940, 804|<b>G4043</b><br />From G4012 and G3961; to <i>tread</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>walk</i> at large (especially as proof of ability); figuratively to <i>live</i>, <i>deport oneself</i>, <i>follow</i> (as a companion or votary): - go, be occupied with, walk (about).<br />|4043|
περιπείρω|peripe�rw|qeriqeirz|1) to pierce through<br />2) metaphorically to torture one's soul with sorrows<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4044</b><br />From G4012 and the base of G4008; to <i>penetrate entirely</i>, that is, <i>transfix</i> (figuratively): - pierce through.<br />|4044|
περιπίπτω|perip�ptw|qeriqiqtz|1) so to fall into as to be encompassed<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:173, 846|<b>G4045</b><br />From G4012 and G4098; to <i>fall</i> into something that is all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>light among</i> or <i>upon</i>, <i>be surrounded with:</i> - fall among (into).<br />|4045|
περιποιέομαι|peripoi�omai|qeriqpiepmai|1) to make to remain over<br />2) to reserve, to leave or keep safe, lay by<br />3) to make to remain for one's self<br />4) to preserve for one's self<br />5) to get for one's self, purchase<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4046</b><br />Middle voice from G4012 and G4160; to <i>make around oneself</i>, that is, <i>acquire</i> (<i>buy</i>): - purchase.<br />|4046|
περιποίησις|peripo�hsij|qeriqpigsis|1) a preserving, a preservation<br />2) possession, one's own property<br />3) an obtaining<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4047</b><br />From G4046; <i>acquisition</i> (the act or the thing); by extension <i>preservation:</i> - obtain (-ing), peculiar, purchased, possession, saving.<br />|4047|
περιρήγνυμι|perir�gnumi|qerirgcnumi|1) to break off on all sides, break off all around<br />2) to rend or tear off all around<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4048</b><br />From G4012 and G4486; to <i>tear</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, <i>completely away:</i> - rend off.<br />|4048|
περισπάομαι|perisp�omai|qerisqapmai|1) to draw around, to draw away, distract<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) to be driven about mentally, to be distracted<br />2b) to be over-occupied, too busy, about a thing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4049</b><br />From G4012 and G4685; to <i>drag</i> all <i>around</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>distract</i> (with care): - cumber.<br />|4049|
