πλείων|ple�wn|qleizn|1) greater in quantity<br />1a) the more part, very many<br />2) greater in quality, superior, more excellent<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4119</b><br />Comparative of G4183; <i>more</i> in quantity, number, or quality; also (in plural) the <i>major portion:</i> - X above, + exceed, more excellent, further, (very) great (-er), long (-er), (very) many, greater (more) part, + yet but.<br />|4119|
πλέκω|pl�kw|qlekz|1) to plait, braid, weave together<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4120</b><br />A primary word; to <i>twine</i> or <i>braid:</i> - plait.<br />|4120|
πλεονάζω|pleon�zw|qlepnafz|1) to superabound<br />1a) of things<br />1a1) to exist in abundance<br />1a2) to increase<br />1a3) be augmented<br />2) to make to increase: one in a thing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:263, 864|<b>G4121</b><br />From G4119; to <i>do</i>, <i>make</i> or <i>be more</i>, that is, <i>increase</i> (transitively or intransitively); by extension to <i>superabound:</i> - abound, abundant, make to increase, have over.<br />|4121|
πλεονεκτέω|pleonekt�w|qlepnektez|1) to have more, or a greater part or share<br />1a) to be superior, excel, surpass, have an advantage over<br />2) to gain or take advantage of another, to overreach<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:266, 864|<b>G4122</b><br />From G4123; to <i>be covetous</i>, that is, (by implication) to <i>over reach:</i> - get an advantage, defraud, make a gain.<br />|4122|
πλεονέκτης|pleon�kthj|qlepnektgs|1) one eager to have more, especially what belongs to others<br />2) greedy of gain, covetous<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:266, 864|<b>G4123</b><br />From G4119 and G2192; <i>holding</i> (<i>desiring</i>) <i>more</i>, that is, <i>eager for gain</i> (<i>avaricious</i>, hence a <i>defrauder</i>): - covetous.<br />|4123|
πλεονεξία|pleonex�a|qlepneoia|1) greedy desire to have more, covetousness, avarice<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:266, 864|<b>G4124</b><br />From G4123; <i>avarice</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>fraudulency</i>, <i>extortion:</i> - covetous (-ness) practices, greediness.<br />|4124|
πλευρά|pleur�|qleura|1) the side of the body<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4125</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; a <i>rib</i>, that is, (by extension) <i>side:</i> - side.<br />|4125|
πλέω|pl�w|qlez|1) to sail, navigate, travel by ship<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4126</b><br />The first is another form for the second which is used as an alternate in certain tenses; probably a form of G4150 (through the idea of <i>plunging</i> through the water); to <i>pass</i> in a vessel: - sail. See also G4130.<br />|4126|
πληγή|plhg�|qlgcg|1) a blow, stripe, a wound<br />2) a public calamity, heavy affliction, plague<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4127</b><br />From G4141; a <i>stroke</i>; by implication a <i>wound</i>; figuratively a <i>calamity:</i> - plague, stripe, wound (-ed).<br />|4127|
πλῆθος|pl�qoj|qlghps|1) a multitude<br />1a) a great number, of men or things<br />1b) the whole number, the whole multitude, the assemblage<br />1b1) the multitude of the people<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:274, 866|<b>G4128</b><br />From G4130; a <i>fulness</i>, that is, a <i>large number</i>, <i>throng</i>, <i>populace:</i> - bundle, company, multitude.<br />|4128|
πληθύνω|plhq�nw|qlghunz|1) to increase, to multiply<br />1a) to be increased, (be multiplied) multiply<br />2) to be increased, to multiply<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:279, 866|<b>G4129</b><br />From another form of G4128; to <i>increase</i> (transitively or intransitively): - abound, multiply.<br />|4129|
πίμπλημι|p�mplhmi|qimqlgmi|1) to fill<br />2) to be fulfilled, to be filled<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:128,*|<b>G4130</b><br />A prolonged form of a primary word <span class="uni">πλέω</span> ple&ocirc; (which appears only as an alternate in certain tenses and in the reduplicated form of <span class="uni">πίμπλημι</span> pimpl&ecirc;mi to "<i>fill</i>" (literally or figuratively [<i>imbue</i>, <i>influence</i>, <i>supply</i>]); specifically to <i>fulfil</i> (time): - accomplish, full (. . . come), furnish.<br />|4130|
πλήκτης|pl�kthj|qlgktgs|1) bruiser, ready for a blow<br />2) a pugnacious, contentious, quarrelsome person<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G4131</b><br />From G4141; a <i>smiter</i>, that is, <i>pugnacious</i> (<i>quarrelsome</i>): - striker.<br />|4131|
πλήμμυρα|pl�mmura|qlgmmura|1) a flood, whether of sea or of a river<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4132</b><br />Prolongation from G4130; <i>flood tide</i>, that is, (by analogy) a <i>freshet:</i> - flood.<br />|4132|
πλήν|pl�n|qlgn|1) moreover, besides, but, nevertheless<br />2) besides, except, but<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4133</b><br />From G4119; <i>moreover</i> (<i>besides</i>), that is, <i>albeit</i>, <i>save that</i>, <i>rather</i>, <i>yet:</i> - but (rather), except, nevertheless, notwithstanding, save, than.<br />|4133|
πλήρης|pl�rhj|qlgrgs|1) full, i.e. filled up (as opposed to empty)<br />1a) of hollow vessels<br />1b) of a surface, covered in every part<br />1c) of the soul, thoroughly permeated with<br />2) full, i.e. complete<br />2a) lacking nothing, perfect<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:283, 867|<b>G4134</b><br />From G4130; <i>replete</i>, or <i>covered</i> over; by analogy <i>complete:</i> - full.<br />|4134|
πληροφορέω|plhrofor�w|qlgrpvprez|1) to bear or bring full, to make full<br />1a) to cause a thing to be shown to the full<br />1a1) to fulfil the ministry in every part<br />1b) to carry through to the end, accomplish<br />1b1) things that have been accomplished<br />1c) to fill one with any thought, conviction, or inclination<br />1c1) to make one certain, to persuade, convince one<br />1c2) to be persuaded, persuaded, fully convinced or assured<br />1c3) to render inclined or bent on<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:309, 867|<b>G4135</b><br />From G4134 and G5409; to <i>carry</i> out <i>fully</i> (in evidence), that is, <i>completely assure</i> (or <i>convince</i>), <i>entirely accomplish:</i> - most surely believe, fully know (persuade), make full proof of.<br />|4135|
πληροφορία|plhrofor�a|qlgrpvpria|1) full assurance, most certain confidence<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:310, 867|<b>G4136</b><br />From G4135; <i>entire confidence:</i> - (full) assurance.<br />|4136|
πληρόω|plhr�w|qlgrpz|1) to make full, to fill up, i.e. to fill to the full<br />1a) to cause to abound, to furnish or supply liberally<br />1a1) I abound, I am liberally supplied<br />2) to render full, i.e. to complete<br />2a) to fill to the top: so that nothing shall be wanting to full measure, fill to the brim<br />2b) to consummate: a number<br />2b1) to make complete in every particular, to render perfect<br />2b2) to carry through to the end, to accomplish, carry out, (some undertaking)<br />2c) to carry into effect, bring to realisation, realise<br />2c1) of matters of duty: to perform, execute<br />2c2) of sayings, promises, prophecies, to bring to pass, ratify, accomplish<br />2c3) to fulfil, i.e. to cause God's will (as made known in the law) to be obeyed as it should be, and God's promises (given through the prophets) to receive fulfilment<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:286, 867|<b>G4137</b><br />From G4134; to <i>make replete</i>, that is, (literally) to <i>cram</i> (a net), <i>level</i> up (a hollow), or (figuratively) to <i>furnish</i> (or <i>imbue</i>, <i>diffuse</i>, <i>influence</i>), <i>satisfy</i>, <i>execute</i> (an office), <i>finish</i> (a period or task), <i>verify</i> (or <i>coincide</i> with a prediction), etc.: - accomplish, X after, (be) complete, end, expire, fill (up), fulfil, (be, make) full (come), fully preach, perfect, supply.<br />|4137|
πλήρωμα|pl�rwma|qlgrzma|1) that which is (has been) filled<br />1a) a ship inasmuch as it is filled (i.e. manned) with sailors, rowers, and soldiers<br />1b) in the NT, the body of believers, as that which is filled with the presence, power, agency, riches of God and of Christ<br />2) that which fills or with which a thing is filled<br />2a) of those things which a ship is filled, freight and merchandise, sailors, oarsmen, soldiers<br />2b) completeness or fulness of time<br />3) fulness, abundance<br />4) a fulfilling, keeping<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:298, 867|<b>G4138</b><br />From G4137; <i>repletion</i> or <i>completion</i>, that is, (subjectively) what <i>fills</i> (as contents, supplement, copiousness, multitude), or (objectively) what is <i>filled</i> (as container, performance, period): - which is put in to fill up, piece that filled up, fulfilling, full, fulness.<br />|4138|
πλησίον|plhs�on|qlgsipn|1) a neighbour<br />1a) a friend<br />1b) any other person, and where two are concerned, the other (thy fellow man, thy neighbour), according to the Jews, any member of the Hebrew nation and commonwealth<br />1c) according to Christ, any other man irrespective of nation or religion with whom we live or whom we chance to meet<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:311, 872|<b>G4139</b><br />Neuter of a derivative of <span class="uni">πέλας</span> pelas (<i>near</i>); (adverb) <i>close</i> by; as noun, a <i>neighbor</i>, that is, <i>fellow</i> (as man, countryman, Christian or friend): - near, neighbour.<br />|4139|
πλησμονή|plhsmon�|qlgsmpng|1) repletion, satiety, for the satisfying of the flesh, to satiate the desires of the flesh<br />1a) indulgence of the flesh<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:131, 840|<b>G4140</b><br />From a presumed derivative of G4130; a <i>filling</i> up, that is, (figuratively) <i>gratification:</i> - satisfying.<br />|4140|
πλήσσω|pl�ssw|qlgssz|1) to strike, smite<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4141</b><br />Apparently another form of G4111 (through the idea of <i>flattening</i> out); to <i>pound</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>inflict</i> with (calamity): - smite. Compare G5180.<br />|4141|
πλοιάριον|ploi�rion|qlpiaripn|1) a small vessel, a boat<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G4142</b><br />Neuter of a presumed derivative of G4143; a <i>boat:</i> - boat, little (small) ship.<br />|4142|
πλοῖον|plo�on|qlpipn|1) a ship<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G4143</b><br />From G4126; a <i>sailer</i>, that is, <i>vessel:</i> - ship (-ping).<br />|4143|
πλοῦς|plo�j|qlpus|1) a voyage<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G4144</b><br />From G4126; a <i>sail</i>, that is, <i>navigation:</i> - course, sailing, voyage.<br />|4144|
πλούσιος|plo�sioj|qlpusips|1) wealthy, abounding in material resources<br />2) metaphorically abounding, abundantly supplied<br />2a) abounding (rich) in Christian virtues and eternal possessions<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:318, 873|<b>G4145</b><br />From G4149; <i>wealthy</i>; figuratively <i>abounding</i> with: - rich.<br />|4145|
πλουσίως|plous�wj|qlpusizs|1) abundantly, richly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4146</b><br />From G4145; <i>copiously:</i> - abundantly, richly.<br />|4146|
πλουτέω|plout�w|qlputez|1) to be rich, to have abundance<br />1a) of outward possessions<br />2) metaphorically to be richly supplied<br />2a) is affluent in resources so that he can give blessings of salvation to all<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:318, 873|<b>G4147</b><br />From G4148; to <i>be</i> (or <i>become</i>) <i>wealthy</i> (literally or figuratively): - be increased with goods, (be made, wax) rich.<br />|4147|
πλουτίζω|plout�zw|qlputifz|1) to make rich, enrich<br />1a) of spiritual riches<br />2) to be richly furnished<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:318, 873|<b>G4148</b><br />From G4149; to <i>make wealthy</i> (figuratively): - en- (make) rich.<br />|4148|
πλοῦτος|plo�toj|qlputps|1) riches, wealth<br />1a) abundance of external possessions<br />1b) fulness, abundance, plenitude<br />1c) a good, i.e. that with which one is enriched<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:318, 873|<b>G4149</b><br />From the base of G4130; <i>wealth</i> (as <i>fulness</i>), that is, (literally) <i>money</i>, <i>possessions</i>, or (figuratively) <i>abundance</i>, <i>richness</i>, (specifically) valuable <i>bestowment:</i> - riches.<br />|4149|
πλύνω|pl�nw|qlunz|1) to wash: with reference to clothing<br />1a) use figuratively of those who by faith so appropriate the results of Christ's expiation as to be regarded by God as pure and sinless<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4150</b><br />A prolonged form of an obsolete <span class="uni">πλύω</span> plu&ocirc; <i>ploo'-o</i> (to "<i>flow</i>"); to "<i>plunge</i>", that is, <i>launder</i> clothing: - wash. Compare G3068, G3538.<br />|4150|
πνεῦμα|pne�ma|qneuma|1) the third person of the triune God, the Holy Spirit, coequal, coeternal with the Father and the Son<br />1a) sometimes referred to in a way which emphasises his personality and character (the Holy Spirit)<br />1b) sometimes referred to in a way which emphasises his work and power (the Spirit of Truth)<br />1c) never referred to as a depersonalised force<br />2) the spirit, i.e. the vital principal by which the body is animated<br />2a) the rational spirit, the power by which the human being feels, thinks, decides<br />2b) the soul<br />3) a spirit, i.e. a simple essence, devoid of all or at least all grosser matter, and possessed of the power of knowing, desiring, deciding, and acting<br />3a) a life giving spirit<br />3b) a human soul that has left the body<br />3c) a spirit higher than man but lower than God, i.e. an angel<br />3c1) used of demons, or evil spirits, who were conceived as inhabiting the bodies of men<br />3c2) the spiritual nature of Christ, higher than the highest angels and equal to God, the divine nature of Christ<br />4) the disposition or influence which fills and governs the soul of any one<br />4a) the efficient source of any power, affection, emotion, desire, etc.<br />5) a movement of air (a gentle blast)<br />5a) of the wind, hence the wind itself<br />5b) breath of nostrils or mouth<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:332, 876|<b>G4151</b><br />From G4154; a <i>current</i> of air, that is, <i>breath</i> (<i>blast</i>) or a <i>breeze</i>; by analogy or figuratively a <i>spirit</i>, that is, (human) the rational <i>soul</i>, (by implication) <i>vital principle</i>, mental <i>disposition</i>, etc., or (superhuman) an <i>angel</i>, <i>daemon</i>, or (divine) God, Christ's <i>spirit</i>, the Holy <i>spirit</i>: - ghost, life, spirit (-ual, -ually), mind. Compare G5590.<br />|4151|
πνευματικός|pneumatik�j|qneumatikps|1) relating to the human spirit, or rational soul, as part of the man which is akin to God and serves as his instrument or organ<br />1a) that which possesses the nature of the rational soul<br />2) belonging to a spirit, or a being higher than man but inferior to God<br />3) belonging to the Divine Spirit<br />3a) of God the Holy Spirit<br />3b) one who is filled with and governed by the Spirit of God<br />4) pertaining to the wind or breath; windy, exposed to the wind, blowing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:332, 876|<b>G4152</b><br />From G4151; <i>non-carnal</i>, that is, (humanly) <i>ethereal</i> (as opposed to gross), or (daemoniacally) a <i>spirit</i> (concretely), or (divinely) <i>supernatural</i>, <i>regenerate</i>, <i>religious</i>: - spiritual. Compare G5591.<br />|4152|
πνευματικῶς|pneumatik�j|qneumatikzs|1) spiritually: i.e. by the aid of the Holy Spirit<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4153</b><br />Adverb from G4152; <i>non-physically</i>, that is, <i>divinely</i>, <i>figuratively:</i> - spiritually.<br />|4153|
πνέω|pn�w|qnez|1) to breathe, to blow<br />1a) of the wind<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:452, 876|<b>G4154</b><br />A primary word; to <i>breathe</i> hard, that is, <i>breeze</i>: - blow. Compare G5594.<br />|4154|
πνίγω|pn�gw|qnicz|1) to choke, strangle<br />1a) of thorns crowding out the seed in the field and hindering its growth<br />2) to wring one's neck, throttle<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:455, 895|<b>G4155</b><br />Strengthened from G4154; to <i>wheeze</i>, that is, (causative by implication) to <i>throttle</i> or <i>strangle</i> (<i>drown</i>): - choke, take by the throat.<br />|4155|
πνικτός|pnikt�j|qniktps|1) suffocate, strangled<br />1a) what is strangled, i.e. an animal deprived of life without the shedding of blood<br />1b) of cooking: our "smothered" as a culinary term<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:455, 895|<b>G4156</b><br />From G4155; <i>throttled</i>, that is, (neuter concretely) an animal <i>choked</i> to death (not bled): - strangled.<br />|4156|
πνοή|pno�|qnpg|1) breath, breath of life<br />2) wind<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:453, 876|<b>G4157</b><br />From G4154; <i>respiration</i>, a <i>breeze:</i> - breath, wind.<br />|4157|
ποδήρης|pod�rhj|qpdgrgs|1) reaching to the feet<br />2) a garment reaching to the ankles, coming down to the feet<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4158</b><br />From G4228 and another element of uncertain affinity; a <i>dress</i> (G2066 implied) <i>reaching</i> the <i>ankles:</i> - garment down to the foot.<br />|4158|
πόθεν|p�qen|qphen|1) of place: from where, from what condition<br />2) of origin or source: from what author or giver<br />3) of cause: how is that?, how can that be?<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4159</b><br />From the base of G4213 with enclitic adverb of origin; <i>from which</i> (as interrogitive) or <i>what</i> (as relative) place, state, source or cause: - whence.<br />|4159|
ποιέω|poi�w|qpiez|1) to make<br />1a) with the names of things made, to produce, construct, form, fashion, etc.<br />1b) to be the authors of, the cause<br />1c) to make ready, to prepare<br />1d) to produce, bear, shoot forth<br />1e) to acquire, to provide a thing for one's self<br />1f) to make a thing out of something<br />1g) to (make, i.e.) render one anything<br />1g1) to (make, i.e.) constitute or appoint one anything, to appoint or ordain one that<br />1g2) to (make, i.e.) declare one anything<br />1h) to put one forth, to lead him out<br />1i) to make one do something<br />1i1) cause one to<br />1j) to be the authors of a thing (to cause, bring about)<br />2) to do<br />2a) to act rightly, do well<br />2a1) to carry out, to execute<br />2b) to do a thing unto one<br />2b1) to do to one<br />2c) with designation of time: to pass, spend<br />2d) to celebrate, keep<br />2d1) to make ready, and so at the same time to institute, the celebration of the passover<br />2e) to perform: to a promise<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:458, 895|<b>G4160</b><br />Apparently a prolonged form of an obsolete primary; to <i>make</i> or <i>do</i> (in a very wide application, more or less direct): - abide, + agree, appoint, X avenge, + band together, be, bear, + bewray, bring (forth), cast out, cause, commit, + content, continue, deal, + without any delay, (would) do (-ing), execute, exercise, fulfil, gain, give, have, hold, X journeying, keep, + lay wait, + lighten the ship, make, X mean, + none of these things move me, observe, ordain, perform, provide, + have purged, purpose, put, + raising up, X secure, shew, X shoot out, spend, take, tarry, + transgress the law, work, yield. Compare G4238.<br />|4160|
ποίημα|po�hma|qpigma|1) that which has been made<br />2) a work<br />2a) of the works of God as creator<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:458, 895|<b>G4161</b><br />From G4160; a <i>product</i>, that is, <i>fabric</i> (literally or figuratively): - thing that is made, workmanship.<br />|4161|
ποίησις|po�hsij|qpigsis|1) a making<br />2) a doing or performing<br />2a) in his doing, i.e. in the obedience he renders to the law<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:458, 895|<b>G4162</b><br />From G4160; <i>action</i>, that is, <i>performance</i> (of the law): - deed.<br />|4162|
ποιητής|poiht�j|qpigtgs|1) a maker, a producer, author<br />2) a doer, performer<br />2a) one who obeys or fulfils the law<br />3) a poet<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:458, 895|<b>G4163</b><br />From G4160; a <i>performer</i>; specifically a "poet": - doer, poet.<br />|4163|
ποικίλος|poik�loj|qpikilps|1) a various colours, variegated<br />2) of various sorts<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:484, 901|<b>G4164</b><br />Of uncertain derivation; <i>motley</i>, that is, <i>various</i> in character: - divers, manifold.<br />|4164|
ποιμαίνω|poima�nw|qpimainz|1) to feed, to tend a flock, keep sheep<br />1a) to rule, govern<br />1a1) of rulers<br />1a2) to furnish pasture for food<br />1a3) to nourish<br />1a4) to cherish one's body, to serve the body<br />1a5) to supply the requisites for the soul's need<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:485, 901|<b>G4165</b><br />From G4166; to <i>tend</i> as a shepherd (or figuratively <i>superviser</i>): - feed (cattle), rule.<br />|4165|
ποιμήν|poim�n|qpimgn|1) a herdsman, especially a shepherd<br />1a) in the parable, he to whose care and control others have committed themselves, and whose precepts they follow<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) the presiding officer, manager, director, of any assembly: so of Christ the Head of the church<br />2a1) of the overseers of the Christian assemblies<br />2a2) of kings and princes<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:485, 901|<b>G4166</b><br />Of uncertain affinity; a <i>shepherd</i> (literally or figuratively): - shepherd, pastor.<br />|4166|
ποίμνη|po�mnh|qpimng|1) a flock (especially) of sheep<br />1a) of Christ's flock, i.e. the body of those who follow Jesus as their guide and keeper<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:499, 901|<b>G4167</b><br />Contracted from G4165; a <i>flock</i> (literally or figuratively): - flock, fold.<br />|4167|
ποίμνιον|po�mnion|qpimnipn|1) a flock (especially) of sheep<br />2) a group of Christ's disciples<br />3) bodies of Christian (churches) presided over by elders<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:499, 901|<b>G4168</b><br />Neuter of a presumed derivative of G4167; a <i>flock</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>group</i> (of believers): - flock.<br />|4168|
ποῖος|po�oj|qpips|1) of what sort or nature<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> pronoun|<b>G4169</b><br />From the base of G4226 and G3634; individualizing interrogitive (of character) <i>what</i> sort of, or (of number) <i>which</i> one: - what (manner of), which.<br />|4169|
πολεμέω|polem�w|qplemez|1) to war, carry on war<br />2) to fight<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:502, 904|<b>G4170</b><br />From G4171; to <i>be</i> (engaged) in <i>warfare</i>, that is, to <i>battle</i> (literally or figuratively): - fight, (make) war.<br />|4170|
πόλεμος|p�lemoj|qplemps|1) a war<br />2) a fight, a battle<br />3) a dispute, strife, quarrel<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:502, 904|<b>G4171</b><br />From <span class="uni">πέλομαι</span> pelomai (to <i>bustle</i>); <i>warfare</i> (literally or figuratively; a single encounter or a series): - battle, fight, war.<br />|4171|
πόλις|p�lij|qplis|1) a city<br />1a) one's native city, the city in which one lives<br />1b) the heavenly Jerusalem<br />1b1) the abode of the blessed in heaven<br />1b2) of the visible capital in the heavenly kingdom, to come down to earth after the renovation of the world by fire<br />1c) the inhabitants of a city<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:516, 906|<b>G4172</b><br />Probably from the same as G4171, or perhaps from G4183; a <i>town</i> (properly with walls, of greater or less size): - city.<br />|4172|
πολιτάρχης|polit�rchj|qplitarxgs|1) a ruler of a city or citizens<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G4173</b><br />From G4172 and G757; a <i>town officer</i>, that is, <i>magistrate:</i> - ruler of the city.<br />|4173|
πολιτεία|polite�a|qpliteia|1) the administration of civil affairs<br />2) a state or commonwealth<br />3) citizenship, the rights of a citizen<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:516, 906|<b>G4174</b><br />From G4177 ("polity"); <i>citizenship</i>; concretely a <i>community:</i> - commonwealth, freedom.<br />|4174|
πολίτευμα|pol�teuma|qpliteuma|1) the administration of civil affairs or of a commonwealth<br />2) the constitution of a commonwealth, form of government and the laws by which it is administered<br />3) a state, commonwealth<br />3a) the commonwealth of citizens<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:516, 906|<b>G4175</b><br />From G4176; a <i>community</i>, that is, (abstractly) <i>citizenship</i> (figuratively): - conversation.<br />|4175|
πολιτεύομαι|polite�omai|qpliteupmai|1) to be a citizen<br />2) to administer civil affairs, manage the state<br />3) to make or create a citizen<br />3a) to be a citizen<br />3b) to behave as a citizen<br />3b1) to avail one's self of or recognise the laws<br />3b2) to conduct one's self as pledged to some law of life<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:516, 906|<b>G4176</b><br />Middle voice of a derivative of G4177; to <i>behave</i> as a citizen (figuratively): - let conversation be, live.<br />|4176|
πολίτης|pol�thj|qplitgs|1) a citizen<br />1a) the inhabitant of any city or country<br />1b) the association of another in citizenship<br />1b1) a fellow citizen, fellow countryman<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:516, 906|<b>G4177</b><br />From G4172; a <i>townsman:</i> - citizen.<br />|4177|
πολλάκις|poll�kij|qpllakis|1) often, frequently<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4178</b><br />Multiplicative adverb from G4183; <i>many times</i>, that is, <i>frequently:</i> - oft (-en, -en-times, -times).<br />|4178|
πολλαπλασίων|pollaplas�wn|qpllaqlasizn|1) manifold, much, more<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4179</b><br />From G4183 and probably a derivative of G4120; <i>manifold</i>, that is, (neuter as noun) <i>very much more:</i> - manifold more.<br />|4179|
πολυλογία|polulog�a|qplulpcia|1) much speaking<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:545, 911|<b>G4180</b><br />From a compound of G4183 and G3056; <i>loquacity</i>, that is, <i>prolixity:</i> - much speaking.<br />|4180|
πολυμερῶς|polumer�j|qplumerzs|1) by many portions, by many times and in many ways<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4181</b><br />Adverb from a compound of G4183 and G3313; <i>in many portions</i>, that is, <i>variously</i> as to time and agency (<i>piecemeal</i>): - at sundry times.<br />|4181|
πολυποίκιλος|polupo�kiloj|qpluqpikilps|1) much variegated, marked with a great variety of colours<br />1a1) of cloth or a painting<br />2) much varied, manifold<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:485, 901|<b>G4182</b><br />From G4183 and G4164; <i>much variegated</i>, that is, <i>multifarious:</i> - manifold.<br />|4182|
πολύς|pol�j|qplus|1) many, much, large<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4183</b><br />Including the forms from the alternate "pollos"; (singular) <i>much</i> (in any respect) or (plural) <i>many</i>; neuter (singular) as adverb <i>largely</i>; neuter (plural) as adverb or noun <i>often</i>, <i>mostly</i>, <i>largely</i>: - abundant, + altogether, common, + far (passed, spent), (+ be of a) great (age, deal, -ly, while), long, many, much, oft (-en [-times]), plenteous, sore, straitly. Compare G4118, G4119.<br />|4183|
πολύσπλαγχνος|pol�splagcnoj|qplusqlacxnps|1) full of pity, very kind<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:548, 1067|<b>G4184</b><br />From G4183 and G4698 (figuratively), <i>extremely compassionate:</i> - very pitiful.<br />|4184|
πολυτελής|polutel�j|qplutelgs|1) precious<br />1a) requiring very great outlay, very costly<br />1b) excellent, of surpassing value<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4185</b><br />From G4183 and G5056; <i>extremely expensive:</i> - costly, very precious, of great price.<br />|4185|
πολύτιμος|pol�timoj|qplutimps|1) very valuable, of great price<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4186</b><br />From G4183 and G5092; <i>extremely valuable:</i> - very costly, of great price.<br />|4186|
πολυτρόπως|polutr�pwj|qplutrpqzs|1) in many manners<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4187</b><br />Adverb from a compound of G4183 and G5158; <i>in many ways</i>, that is, <i>variously</i> as to method or form: - in divers manners.<br />|4187|
πόμα|p�ma|qpma|1) drink<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:145, 840|<b>G4188</b><br />From the alternate of G4095; a <i>beverage:</i> - drink.<br />|4188|
πονηρία|ponhr�a|qpngria|1) depravity, iniquity, wickedness<br />2) malice<br />3) evil purposes and desires<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:562, 912|<b>G4189</b><br />From G4190; <i>depravity</i>, that is, (specifically) <i>malice</i>; plural (concretely) <i>plots</i>, <i>sins:</i> - iniquity, wickedness.<br />|4189|
πονηρός|ponhr�j|qpngrps|1) full of labours, annoyances, hardships<br />1a) pressed and harassed by labours<br />1b) bringing toils, annoyances, perils; of a time full of peril to Christian faith and steadfastness; causing pain and trouble<br />2) bad, of a bad nature or condition<br />2a) in a physical sense: diseased or blind<br />2b) in an ethical sense: evil wicked, bad<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:546, 912|<b>G4190</b><br />From a derivative of G4192; <i>hurtful</i>, that is, <i>evil</i> (properly in effect or influence, and thus differing from G2556, which refers rather to <i>essential</i> character, as well as from G4550, which indicates <i>degeneracy</i> from original virtue); figuratively <i>calamitous</i>; also (passively) <i>ill</i>, that is, <i>diseased</i>; but especially (morally) <i>culpable</i>, that is, <i>derelict</i>, <i>vicious</i>, <i>facinorous</i>; neuter (singular) <i>mischief</i>, <i>malice</i>, or (plural) <i>guilt</i>; masculine (singular) the <i>devil</i>, or (plural) <i>sinners</i>: - bad, evil, grievous, harm, lewd, malicious, wicked (-ness). See also G4191.<br />|4190|
πονηροτερος|ponhroteroj|qpngrpterps|1) more evil<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4191</b><br />Comparative of G4190; <i>more evil:</i> - more wicked.<br />|4191|
πόνος|p�noj|qpnps|1) great trouble, intense desire<br />2) pain<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G4192</b><br />From the base of G3993; <i>toil</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>anguish:</i> - pain.<br />|4192|
Ποντικός|Pontik�j|qpntikps|1) belonging to Pontus, born in Pontus<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4193</b><br />From G4195; a <i>Pontican</i>, that is, native of Pontus: - born in Pontus.<br />|4193|
Πόντιος|P�ntioj|qpntips|Pontius [Pilate] = "of the sea"<br />1) the sixth Roman procurator of Judah who crucified Christ<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G4194</b><br />Of Latin origin; apparently <i>bridged</i>; <i>Pontius</i>, a Roman: - Pontius.<br />|4194|
Πόντος|P�ntoj|qpntps|Pontus = "the sea"<br />1) a region of eastern Asia Minor, bounded by the Euxine Sea, Armenia, Cappadocia, Galatia, Paphlagonia<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G4195</b><br />A <i>sea</i>; <i>Pontus</i>, a region of Asia Minor: - Pontus.<br />|4195|
Πόπλιος|P�plioj|qpqlips|Publius = "popular"<br />1) the chief magistrate of the island of Melita<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G4196</b><br />Of Latin origin; apparently "popular"; <i>Poplius</i> (that is, <i>Publius</i>), a Roman: - Publius.<br />|4196|
πορεία|pore�a|qpreia|1) a journey<br />2) a going, that is: purpose, pursuit, undertaking<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4197</b><br />From G4198; <i>travel</i> (by land); figuratively (plural) <i>proceedings</i>, that is, <i>career:</i> - journey [-ing], ways.<br />|4197|
πορεύομαι|pore�omai|qpreupmai|1) to lead over, carry over, transfer<br />1a) to pursue the journey on which one has entered, to continue on one's journey<br />1b) to depart from life<br />1c) to follow one, that is: become his adherent<br />1c1) to lead or order one's life<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:566, 915|<b>G4198</b><br />Middle voice from a derivative of the same as G3984; to <i>traverse</i>, that is, <i>travel</i> (literally or figuratively; especially to <i>remove</i> [figuratively <i>die</i>], <i>live</i>, etc.): - depart, go (away, forth, one's way, up), (make a, take a) journey, walk.<br />|4198|
πορθέω|porq�w|qprhez|1) to destroy, overthrow<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4199</b><br />Prolonged version of <span class="uni">πέρθω</span> porth&ocirc; (to <i>sack</i>); to <i>ravage</i> (figuratively): - destroy, waste.<br />|4199|
πορισμός|porism�j|qprismps|1) acquisition, gain<br />2) source of gain<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G4200</b><br />From a derivative of <span class="uni">πόρος</span> poros (a <i>way</i>, that is, <i>means</i>); <i>furnishing</i> (<i>procuring</i>), that is, (by implication) <i>money getting</i> (<i>acquisition</i>): - gain.<br />|4200|
Πόρκιος|P�rkioj|qprkips|Porcius [Festus] = "swinish"<br />1) the successor of Felix as procurator of Judea<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G4201</b><br />Of Latin origin; apparently <i>swinish</i>; <i>Porcius</i>, a Roman: - Porcius.<br />|4201|
πορνεία|porne�a|qprneia|1) illicit sexual intercourse<br />1a) adultery, fornication, homosexuality, lesbianism, intercourse with animals etc.<br />1b) sexual intercourse with close relatives; Lev. 18<br />1c) sexual intercourse with a divorced man or woman; Mar 10:11,Mar 10:12<br />2) metaphorically the worship of idols<br />2a) of the defilement of idolatry, as incurred by eating the sacrifices offered to idols<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:579, 918|<b>G4202</b><br />From G4203; <i>harlotry</i> (including <i>adultery</i> and <i>incest</i>); figuratively <i>idolatry:</i> - fornication.<br />|4202|
πορνεύω|porne�w|qprneuz|1) to prostitute one's body to the lust of another<br />2) to give one's self to unlawful sexual intercourse<br />2a) to commit fornication<br />3) metaphorically to be given to idolatry, to worship idols<br />3a) to permit one's self to be drawn away by another into idolatry<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:579, 918|<b>G4203</b><br />From G4204; to <i>act</i> the <i>harlot</i>, that is, (literally) <i>indulge</i> unlawful <i>lust</i> (of either sex), or (figuratively) <i>practise idolatry:</i> - commit (fornication).<br />|4203|
πόρνη|p�rnh|qprng|1) a woman who sells her body for sexual uses<br />1a) a prostitute, a harlot, one who yields herself to defilement for the sake of gain<br />1b) any woman indulging in unlawful sexual intercourse, whether for gain or for lust<br />2) metaphorically an idolatress<br />2a) of "Babylon," i.e. Rome, the chief seat of idolatry<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:579, 918|<b>G4204</b><br />Feminine of G4205; a <i>strumpet</i>; figuratively an <i>idolater:</i> - harlot, whore.<br />|4204|
πόρνος|p�rnoj|qprnps|1) a man who prostitutes his body to another's lust for hire<br />2) a male prostitute<br />3) a man who indulges in unlawful sexual intercourse, a fornicator<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:579, 918|<b>G4205</b><br />From <span class="uni">πέρνημι</span> pern&ecirc;mi (to <i>sell</i>; akin to the base of G4097); a (male) <i>prostitute</i> (as <i>venal</i>), that is, (by analogy) a <i>debauchee</i> (<i>libertine</i>): - fornicator, whoremonger.<br />|4205|
πόρρω|p�rrw|qprrz|1) far, at a distance, a great way off<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4206</b><br />Adverb from G4253; <i>forwards</i>, that is, <i>at a distance</i>: - far, a great way off. See also G4207.<br />|4206|
πόρρωθεν|p�rrwqen|qprrzhen|1) from afar, afar off<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4207</b><br />From G4206 with adverbial enclitic of source; <i>from far</i>, or (by implication) <i>at a distance</i>, that is, <i>distantly:</i> - afar off.<br />|4207|
πορρώτερον|porr�teron|qprrzterpn|1) further<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4208</b><br />Adverb comparative of G4206; <i>farther</i>, that is, <i>a greater distance:</i> - further.<br />|4208|
πορφύρα|porf�ra|qprvura|1) the purple fish, a species of shell fish or mussel<br />2) a fabric coloured with purple dye, a garment made from purple cloth<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4209</b><br />Of Latin origin; the "purple" mussel, that is, (by implication) the <i>red blue</i> color itself, and finally, a garment dyed with it: - purple.<br />|4209|
πορφυροῦς|porfuro�j|qprvurpus|1) purple, dyed in purple, made of purple fabric<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4210</b><br />From G4209; <i>purpureal</i>, that is, <i>bluish red:</i> - purple.<br />|4210|
πορφυρόπωλις|porfur�pwlij|qprvurpqzlis|1) a female seller of purple or of fabric dyed in purple<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4211</b><br />Feminine of a compound of G4209 and G4453; a <i>female trader in purple</i> cloth: - seller of purple.<br />|4211|
ποσάκις|pos�kij|qpsakis|1) how often<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4212</b><br />Multiplicative from G4214; <i>how many times:</i> - how oft (-en).<br />|4212|
πόσις|p�sij|qpsis|1) a drinking, drink<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:145, 841|<b>G4213</b><br />From the alternate of G4095; a <i>drinking</i> (the act), that is, (concretely) a <i>draught:</i> - drink.<br />|4213|
πόσος|p�soj|qpsps|1) how great<br />2) how much<br />3) how many<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> pronoun|<b>G4214</b><br />From an obsolete "pos" (<i>who</i>, <i>what</i>) and G3739; interrogitive pronoun (of amount) <i>how much</i> (<i>large</i>, <i>long</i> or [plural] <i>many</i>): - how great (long, many), what.<br />|4214|
ποταμός|potam�j|qptamps|1) a stream, a river<br />2) a torrent<br />3) floods<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:595, 921|<b>G4215</b><br />Probably from a derivative of the alternate of G4095 (compare G4224); a <i>current</i>, <i>brook</i> or <i>freshet</i> (as <i>drinkable</i>), that is, <i>running water:</i> - flood, river, stream, water.<br />|4215|
ποταμοφόρητος|potamof�rhtoj|qptampvprgtps|1) carried away by a stream (i.e. overwhelmed, drowned in the waters)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:607, 921|<b>G4216</b><br />From G4215 and a derivative of G5409; <i>river borne</i>, that is, <i>overwhelmed by a stream:</i> - carried away of the flood.<br />|4216|
ποταπός|potap�j|qptaqps|1) from what country, nation or tribe<br />2) of what sort or quality (what manner of)<br />2a) of persons<br />2b) of things<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4217</b><br />Apparently from G4219 and the base of G4226; interrogitive <i>whatever</i>, that is, of <i>what possible</i> sort: - what (manner of).<br />|4217|
ποτέ|pot�|qpte|1) once, i.e. formerly, aforetime, at some time<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> particle|<b>G4218</b><br />From the base of G4225 and G5037; indefinite adverb, at <i>some time</i>, <i>ever:</i> - afore- (any, some-) time (-s), at length (the last), (+ n-) ever, in the old time, in time past, once, when.<br />|4218|
πότερον|p�teron|qpterpn|1) which of two<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> conjunction|<b>G4220</b><br />Neuter of a comparative of the base of G4226; interrogitive as adverb, <i>which</i> (of two), that is, <i>is it</i> this or that: - whether.<br />|4220|
ποτήριον|pot�rion|qptgripn|1) a cup, a drinking vessel<br />2) metaphorically one's lot or experience, whether joyous or adverse, divine appointments, whether favourable or unfavourable, are likened to a cup which God presents one to drink: so of prosperity and adversity<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:148, 841|<b>G4221</b><br />Neuter of a derivative of the alternate of G4095; a <i>drinking vessel</i>; by extension the contents thereof, that is, a <i>cupful</i> (<i>draught</i>); figuratively a <i>lot</i> or <i>fate:</i> - cup.<br />|4221|
ποτίζω|pot�zw|qptifz|1) to give to drink, to furnish drink<br />2) to water, irrigate (plants, fields etc.)<br />3) metaphorically to imbue, saturate one's mind<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:159, 841|<b>G4222</b><br />From a derivative of the alternate of G4095; to <i>furnish drink</i>, <i>irrigate:</i> - give (make) to drink, feed, water.<br />|4222|
Ποτίολοι|Pot�oloi|qptiplpi|Puteoli = "sulphurous springs"<br />1) a city of Campania, in Italy, situated on the Bay of Naples<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G4223</b><br />Of Latin origin; <i>little wells</i>, that is, <i>mineral springs</i>; <i>Potioli</i> (that is, <i>Puteoli</i>), a place in Italy: - Puteoli.<br />|4223|
πότος|p�toj|qptps|1) a drinking, carousing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:145, 841|<b>G4224</b><br />From the alternate of G4095; a <i>drinking bout</i> or <i>carousal:</i> - banqueting.<br />|4224|
ποῦ|po�|qpu|1) somewhere<br />2) nearly<br />3) with numerals: somewhere about, about<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4226</b><br />Genitive case of <span class="uni">πός</span> pos, an interrogitive pronoun, (<i>what</i>) otherwise obsolete (perhaps the same as G4225 used with the rising slide of inquiry); as adverb of place; <i>at</i> (by implication <i>to</i>) <i>what</i> locality: - where, whither.<br />|4226|
Πούδης|Po�dhj|qpudgs|Pudens = "modest"<br />1) a Christian friend of Timothy at Rome, and may have been one of the seventy disciples<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G4227</b><br />Of Latin origin; <i>modest</i>; <i>Pudes</i> (that is, <i>Pudens</i>), a Christian: - Pudens.<br />|4227|
πούς|po�j|qpus|1) a foot, both of men or beast<br />1a) often in the orient, one put his foot on vanquished<br />1b) of disciples listening to their teacher's instruction are said to be at his feet<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:624, 925|<b>G4228</b><br />A primary word; a "foot" (figuratively or literally): - foot (-stool).<br />|4228|
πρᾶγμα|pr�gma|qracma|1) that which has been done, a deed, an accomplished fact<br />2) what is done or being accomplished<br />2a) spec. business, a commercial transaction<br />3) a matter, question, affair<br />3a) spec. in a forensic sense, a matter at law, case, suit<br />4) that which is or exists, a thing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:638, 927|<b>G4229</b><br />From G4238; a <i>deed</i>; by implication an <i>affair</i>; by extension an <i>object</i> (material): - business, matter, thing, work.<br />|4229|
πραγματεία|pragmate�a|qracmateia|1) prosecution of any affair<br />1a) business, occupation<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:640, 927|<b>G4230</b><br />From G4231; a <i>transaction</i>, that is, <i>negotiation:</i> - affair.<br />|4230|
πραγματεύομαι|pragmate�omai|qracmateupmai|1) to be occupied in anything<br />2) to carry on a business<br />3) to carry on the business of a banker or a trader<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:641, 927|<b>G4231</b><br />From G4229; to <i>busy oneself</i> with, that is, to <i>trade:</i> - occupy.<br />|4231|
πραιτώριον|prait�rion|qraitzripn|1) "head-quarters" in a Roman camp, the tent of the commander-in-chief<br />2) the palace in which the governor or procurator of a province resided, to which use the Romans were accustomed to appropriate the palaces already existing, and formerly dwelt in by kings or princes; at Jerusalem it was a magnificent palace which Herod the Great had built for himself, and which the Roman procurators seemed to have occupied whenever they came from Caesarea to Jerusalem to transact public business<br />3) the camp of the Praetorian soldiers established by Tiberius<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G4232</b><br />Of Latin origin; the <i>praetorium</i> or governor's <i>court room</i> (sometimes including the whole <i>edifice</i> and <i>camp</i>): - (common, judgment) hall (of judgment), palace, praetorium.<br />|4232|
πράκτωρ|pr�ktwr|qraktzr|1) one who does anything, a doer<br />2) one who does the work of inflicting punishment or taking vengeance<br />2a) the avenger of murder<br />2b) the exactor of a monetary fine<br />2c) an officer of justice of the lower order whose business it is to inflict punishment<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:642, 927|<b>G4233</b><br />From a derivative of G4238; a <i>practiser</i>, that is, (specifically) an official <i>collector:</i> - officer.<br />|4233|
πρᾶξις|pr�xij|qraois|1) a doing, a mode of acting, a deal, a transaction<br />1a) the doings of the apostles<br />1b) in a bad sense, wicked deed, crime, wicked doings (our practices, i.e. trickery)<br />2) a thing to be done, business<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:642, 927|<b>G4234</b><br />From G4238; <i>practice</i>, that is, (concretely) an <i>act</i>; by extension a <i>function:</i> - deed, office, work.<br />|4234|
πρᾷος|pr�oj|qraps|1) gentle, mild, meek<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4235</b><br />A form of G4239, used in certain parts; <i>gentle</i>, that is, <i>humble:</i> - meek.<br />|4235|
πραϋπάθεια|pra�p�qeia|qrauqaheia|1) gentleness, mildness, meekness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4236</b><br />From G4235; <i>gentleness</i>; by implication <i>humility:</i> - meekness.<br />|4236|
πρασιά|prasi�|qrasia|1) a plot of ground, a garden bed<br />2) Hebrew idiom, i.e. they reclined in ranks or divisions, so that several ranks formed, as it were separate plots<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4237</b><br />Perhaps from <span class="uni">πράσον</span> prason (a <i>leek</i>, and so an <i>onion patch</i>); a garden <i>plot</i>, that is, (by implication of regular <i>beds</i>) a <i>row</i> (repeated in plural by Hebraism to indicate an arrangement): - in ranks.<br />|4237|
πράσσω|pr�ssw|qrassz|1) to exercise, practise, to be busy with, carry on<br />1a) to undertake, to do<br />2) to accomplish, perform<br />2a) to commit, perpetrate<br />3) to manage public affairs, transact public business<br />3a) to exact tribute, revenue, debts<br />4) to act<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:632, 927|<b>G4238</b><br />A primary verb; to "practise", that is, <i>perform repeatedly</i> or <i>habitually</i> (thus differing from G4160, which properly refers to a <i>single</i> act); by implication to <i>execute</i>, <i>accomplish</i>, etc.; specifically to <i>collect</i> (dues), <i>fare</i> (personally): - commit, deeds, do, exact, keep, require, use arts.<br />|4238|
πραΰς|pra�j|qraus|1) mildness of disposition, gentleness of spirit, meekness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:645, 929|<b>G4239</b><br />Apparently a primary word; <i>mild</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>humble:</i> - meek. See also G4235.<br />|4239|
πραΰτης|pra�thj|qrautgs|1) mildness of disposition, gentleness of spirit, meekness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:645, 929|<b>G4240</b><br />From G4239; <i>mildness</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>humility:</i> - meekness.<br />|4240|
πρέπω|pr�pw|qreqz|1) to stand out, to be conspicuous, to be eminent<br />2) to be becoming, seemly, fit<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4241</b><br />Apparently a primary verb; to <i>tower</i> up (<i>be conspicuous</i>), that is, (by implication) to <i>be suitable</i> or <i>proper</i> (third person singular present indicative, often used impersonally, it is <i>fit</i> or <i>right</i>): - become, comely.<br />|4241|
πρεσβεία|presbe�a|qresbeia|1) age, dignity, right of the first born<br />2) the business normally intrusted to elders, spec. the office of an ambassador, an embassy<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4242</b><br />From G4243; <i>seniority</i> (<i>eldership</i>), that is, (by implication) an <i>embassy</i> (concretely <i>ambassadors</i>): - ambassage, message.<br />|4242|
πρεσβεύω|presbe�w|qresbeuz|1) to be older, prior by birth or in age<br />2) to be an ambassador, act as an ambassador<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:681, 931|<b>G4243</b><br />From the base of G4245; to be a <i>senior</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>act as a representative</i> (figuratively <i>preacher</i>): - be an ambassador.<br />|4243|
πρεσβυτέριον|presbut�rion|qresbuteripn|1) body of elders, presbytery, senate, council<br />1a) of the Jewish elders<br />1b) of the elders of any body (assembly) of Christians<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:651, 931|<b>G4244</b><br />Neuter of a presumed derivative of G4245; the <i>order of elders</i>, that is, (specifically) Israelite <i>Sanhedrim</i> or Christian "presbytery": - (estate of) elder (-s), presbytery.<br />|4244|
πρεσβύτερος|presb�teroj|qresbuterps|1) elder, of age<br />1a) the elder of two people<br />1b) advanced in life, an elder, a senior<br />1b1) forefathers<br />2) a term of rank or office<br />2a) among the Jews<br />2a1) members of the great council or Sanhedrin (because in early times the rulers of the people, judges, etc., were selected from elderly men)<br />2a2) of those who in separate cities managed public affairs and administered justice<br />2b) among the Christians, those who presided over the assemblies (or churches) The NT uses the term bishop, elders, and presbyters interchangeably<br />2c) the twenty four members of the heavenly Sanhedrin or court seated on thrones around the throne of God<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:651, 931|<b>G4245</b><br />Comparative of <span class="uni">πρέσβυς</span> presbus (<i>elderly</i>); <i>older</i>; as noun, a <i>senior</i>; specifically an Israelite <i>Sanhedrist</i> (also figuratively, member of the celestial council) or Christian "presbyter": - elder (-est), old.<br />|4245|
πρεσβύτης|presb�thj|qresbutgs|1) an old man, an aged man<br />2) ambassador<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:683, 931|<b>G4246</b><br />From the same as G4245; an <i>old man:</i> - aged (man), old man.<br />|4246|
πρεσβῦτις|presb�tij|qresbutis|1) an aged woman<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4247</b><br />Feminine of G4246; an <i>old woman:</i> - aged woman.<br />|4247|
πρηνής|prhn�j|qrgngs|1) headlong<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4248</b><br />From G4253; <i>leaning</i> (<i>falling</i>) <i>forward</i> ("prone"), that is, <i>head foremost:</i> - headlong.<br />|4248|
πρίζω|pr�zw|qrifz|1) to saw, to cut in two with a saw<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4249</b><br />A strengthened form of a primary word <span class="uni">πρίω</span> pri&ocirc;, (to <i>saw</i>); to <i>saw</i> in two: - saw asunder.<br />|4249|
πρίν|pr�n|qrin|1) before, formerly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4250</b><br />Adverb from G4253; <i>prior</i>, <i>sooner:</i> - before (that), ere.<br />|4250|
Πρίσκα|Pr�ska|qriska|Priscilla = "ancient"<br />1) a Christian woman, the wife of Aquila<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper feminine|<b>G4251</b><br />Of Latin origin; feminine of <i>Priscus</i>, <i>ancient</i>; <i>Priska</i>, a Christian woman: - Prisca. See also G4252.<br />|4251|
Πρίσκιλλα|Prisk�lla|qriskilla|Priscilla = "ancient"<br />1) a Christian woman, the wife of Aquila<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper feminine|<b>G4252</b><br />Diminutive of G4251; <i>Priscilla</i> (that is, <i>little Prisca</i>), a Christian woman: - Priscilla.<br />|4252|
πρό|pro|qrp|1) before<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> preposition<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:683, 935|<b>G4253</b><br />A primary preposition; "fore", that is, <i>in front of</i>, <i>prior</i> (figuratively <i>superior</i>) <i>to</i>. In compounds it retains the same significations: - above, ago, before, or ever. In compounds it retains the same significations.<br />|4253|
προάγω|pro�gw|qrpacz|1) to lead forward, lead forth<br />1a) one from a place in which he has lain hidden from view, as from a prison<br />1b) in a forensic sense, to bring one forth to trial<br />2) to go before<br />2a) preceding, prior in time, previous<br />2b) to proceed, go forward<br />2b1) in a bad sense, to go further than is right. or proper<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:130, 20|<b>G4254</b><br />From G4253 and G71; to <i>lead forward</i> (magisterially); intransitively to <i>precede</i> (in place or time [participle <i>previous</i>]): - bring (forth, out), go before.<br />|4254|
προαιρέομαι|proair�omai|qrpairepmai|1) to bring forward, bring forth from one's stores<br />2) to bring forth for one's self, to choose for one's self before another, to prefer<br />3) to purpose<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4255</b><br />From G4253 and G138; to <i>choose</i> for oneself <i>before</i> another thing (<i>prefer</i>), that is, (by implication) to <i>propose</i> (<i>intend</i>): - purpose.<br />|4255|
προαιτιάομαι|proaiti�omai|qrpaitiapmai|1) to bring a charge against previously (i.e. in what has previously been said)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4256</b><br />From G4253 and a derivative of G156; to <i>accuse already</i>, that is, <i>previously charge:</i> - prove before.<br />|4256|
προακούω|proako�w|qrpakpuz|1) to hear before<br />1a) the hoped for salvation before its realisation<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4257</b><br />From G4253 and G191; to <i>hear already</i>, that is, <i>anticipate:</i> - hear before.<br />|4257|
προαμαρτάνω|proamart�nw|qrpamartanz|1) to sin before<br />1a) of those who before receiving baptism had been guilty of the vices especially common among the Gentiles<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4258</b><br />From G4253 and G264; to <i>sin previously</i> (to conversion): - sin already, heretofore sin.<br />|4258|
προαύλιον|proa�lion|qrpaulipn|1) fore-court, porch<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G4259</b><br />Neuter of a presumed compound of G4253 and G833; a <i>fore-court</i>, that is, <i>vestibule</i> (<i>alley way</i>): - porch.<br />|4259|
προβαίνω|proba�nw|qrpbainz|1) to go forwards, go on<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4260</b><br />From G4253 and the base of G939; to <i>walk forward</i>, that is, <i>advance</i> (literally or in years): - + be of a great age, go farther (on), be well stricken.<br />|4260|
προβάλλω|prob�llw|qrpballz|1) to throw forward<br />1a) of trees, to shoot forth, put out leaves<br />1b) to germinate<br />1c) to push forward, thrust forward, put forward<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4261</b><br />From G4253 and G906; to <i>throw forward</i>, that is, <i>push to the front</i>, <i>germinate:</i> - put forward, shoot forth.<br />|4261|
προβατικός|probatik�j|qrpbatikps|1) pertaining to sheep<br />2) the sheep gate<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4262</b><br />From G4263; <i>relating to sheep</i>, that is, (a <i>gate</i>) through which they were led into Jerusalem: - sheep (market).<br />|4262|
πρόβατον|pr�baton|qrpbatpn|1) any four footed, tame animal accustomed to graze, small cattle<br />1a) a sheep, and so always in the NT<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:689, 936|<b>G4263</b><br />Properly the neuter of a presumed derivative of G4260; <i>something that walks forward</i> (a <i>quadruped</i>), that is, (specifically) a <i>sheep</i> (literally or figuratively): - sheep ([-fold]).<br />|4263|
προβιβάζω|probib�zw|qrpbibafz|1) to cause to go forward, to lean forward, to bring forward, drag forward<br />2) metaphorically to incite, instigate, urge, forward, set on<br />2a) to induce by persuasion<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4264</b><br />From G4253 and a reduplicated form of G971; to <i>force forward</i>, that is, <i>bring to the front</i>, <i>instigate:</i> - draw, before instruct.<br />|4264|
προβλέπομαι|probl�pomai|qrpbleqpmai|1) to foresee<br />2) to provide<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4265</b><br />From G4253 and G991; to <i>look</i> out <i>beforehand</i>, that is, <i>furnish in advance:</i> - provide.<br />|4265|
προγίνομαι|prog�nomai|qrpcinpmai|1) to arise or come before, happen before<br />1a) of sins committed previously<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4266</b><br />From G4253 and G1096; to <i>be already</i>, that is, <i>have previously transpired:</i> - be past.<br />|4266|
προγινώσκω|progin�skw|qrpcinzskz|1) to have knowledge before hand<br />2) to foreknow<br />2a) of those whom God elected to salvation<br />3) to predestinate<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:715, 119|<b>G4267</b><br />From G4253 and G1097; to <i>know beforehand</i>, that is, <i>foresee:</i> - foreknow (ordain), know (before).<br />|4267|
πρόγνωσις|pr�gnwsij|qrpcnzsis|1) foreknowledge<br />2) forethought, pre-arrangement<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:715, 119|<b>G4268</b><br />From G4267; <i>forethought:</i> - foreknowledge.<br />|4268|
πρόγονος|pr�gonoj|qrpcpnps|1) born before, older<br />1a) of ancestors<br />1b) of a mother<br />1c) of grandparents<br />1d) of great-grand parents (if they are still alive)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4269</b><br />From G4266; an <i>ancestor</i>, (<i>grand-</i>) <i>parent:</i> - forefather, parent.<br />|4269|
προγράφω|progr�fw|qrpcravz|1) to write before (of time)<br />1a) of old set forth or designated before hand (in the scriptures of the OT)<br />2) to depict or portray openly<br />2a) to write before the eyes of all who can read<br />2b) to depict, portray, paint, before the eyes<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:770, 128|<b>G4270</b><br />From G4253 and G1125; to <i>write previously</i>; figuratively to <i>announce</i>, <i>prescribe:</i> - before ordain, evidently set forth, write (afore, aforetime).<br />|4270|
πρόδηλος|pr�dhloj|qrpdglps|1) openly evident, known to all, manifest<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4271</b><br />From G4253 and G1212; <i>plain before</i> all men, that is, <i>obvious:</i> - evident, manifest (open) beforehand.<br />|4271|
προδίδωμι|prod�dwmi|qrpdidzmi|1) to give before, give first<br />2) to betray<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4272</b><br />From G4253 and G1325; to <i>give before</i> the other party has given: - first give.<br />|4272|
προδότης|prod�thj|qrpdptgs|1) a betrayer, traitor<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G4273</b><br />From G4272 (in the sense of <i>giving forward</i> into another's [the enemy's] hands); a <i>surrender:</i> - betrayer, traitor.<br />|4273|
πρόδρομος|pr�dromoj|qrpdrpmps|1) a forerunner<br />1a) especially one who is sent before to take observations or act as a spy, a scout, a light armed soldier<br />1b) one who comes in advance to a place where the rest are to follow<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:235, 1189|<b>G4274</b><br />From the alternate of G4390; a <i>runner ahead</i>, that is, <i>scout</i> (figuratively <i>precursor</i>): - forerunner.<br />|4274|
προελπίζω|proelp�zw|qrpelqifz|1) to hope before<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:534, 229|<b>G4276</b><br />From G4253 and G1679; to <i>hope in advance</i> of other confirmation: - first trust.<br />|4276|
προεπω|proepw|qrpeqz|1) to say before<br />1a) to say in what precedes, to say above<br />1b) to say before, i.e. heretofore, formerly<br />1c) to say beforehand, i.e. before the event: prophecies<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4277</b><br />From G4253 and G2036; to <i>say already</i>, to <i>predict</i>: - forewarn, say (speak, tell) before. Compare G4280.<br />|4277|
προενάρχομαι|proen�rcomai|qrpenarxpmai|1) to make a beginning before<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4278</b><br />From G4253 and G1728; to <i>commence already:</i> - begin (before).<br />|4278|
προεπαγγέλλομαι|proepagg�llomai|qrpeqaccellpmai|1) to announce before<br />2) to promise before<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:586, 240|<b>G4279</b><br />Middle voice from G4253 and G1861; to <i>promise of old:</i> - promise before.<br />|4279|
προερεω|proerew|qrperez|1) to say before<br />1a) to say in what precedes, to say above<br />1b) to say before, i.e. heretofore, formerly<br />1c) to say beforehand, i.e. before the event: prophecies<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4280</b><br />From G4253 and G2046; used as alternate of G4277; to <i>say already</i>, <i>predict:</i> - foretell, say (speak, tell) before.<br />|4280|
προέρχομαι|pro�rcomai|qrperxpmai|1) to go forward, go on<br />2) to go before<br />2a) to go before, precede<br />2b) to go before, in the advance of another<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4281</b><br />From G4253 and G2064 (including its alternate); to <i>go onward</i>, <i>precede</i> (in place or time): - go before (farther, forward), outgo, pass on.<br />|4281|
προετοιμάζω|proetoim�zw|qrpetpimafz|1) to prepare before, to make ready beforehand<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:704, 266|<b>G4282</b><br />From G4253 and G2090; to <i>fit</i> up <i>in advance</i> (literally or figuratively): - ordain before, prepare afore.<br />|4282|
προευαγγελίζομαι|proeuaggel�zomai|qrpeuaccelifpmai|1) to announce or promise glad tidings beforehand<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:737, 267|<b>G4283</b><br />Middle voice from G4253 and G2097; to <i>announce</i> glad news <i>in advance:</i> - preach before the gospel.<br />|4283|
προέχομαι|pro�comai|qrpexpmai|1) to have before or in advance of another, to have pre-eminence over another, to excel, surpass<br />2) to surpass in excellencies which can be passed to one's credit<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:692, 937|<b>G4284</b><br />Middle voice from G4253 and G2192; to <i>hold</i> oneself <i>before</i> others, that is, (figuratively) to <i>excel:</i> - be better.<br />|4284|
προηγέομαι|prohg�omai|qrpgcepmai|1) to go before and show the way, to go before and lead, to go before as a leader<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:908, 303|<b>G4285</b><br />From G4253 and G2233; to <i>lead the way</i> for others, that is, <i>show deference:</i> - prefer.<br />|4285|
πρόθεσις|pr�qesij|qrphesis|1) a setting forth of a thing, placing of it in view, the shewbread<br />1a) twelve loaves of wheaten bread, corresponding to the number of the tribes of Israel, which loaves were offered to God every Sabbath, and separated into two rows, lay for seven days upon a table placed in the sanctuary or front portion of the tabernacle, and afterwards of the temple<br />2) a purpose<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:164, 1176|<b>G4286</b><br />From G4388; a <i>setting forth</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>proposal</i> (<i>intention</i>); specifically the <i>show</i> bread (in the Temple) as <i>exposed</i> before God: - purpose, shew [-bread].<br />|4286|
προθεσμία|proqesm�a|qrphesmia|1) set beforehand, appointed or determined beforehand, prearranged<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4287</b><br />From G4253 and a derivative of G5087; <i>fixed beforehand</i>, that is, (feminine with G2250 implied) a <i>designated</i> day: - time appointed.<br />|4287|
προθυμία|proqum�a|qrphumia|1) zeal, spirit, eagerness<br />2) inclination, readiness of mind<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:697, 937|<b>G4288</b><br />From G4289; <i>predisposition</i>, that is, <i>alacrity:</i> - forwardness of mind, readiness (of mind), ready (willing) mind.<br />|4288|
πρόθυμος|pr�qumoj|qrphumps|1) ready, willing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:694, 937|<b>G4289</b><br />From G4253 and G2372; <i>forward</i> in <i>spirit</i>, that is, <i>predisposed</i>; neuter (as noun) <i>alacrity:</i> - ready, willing.<br />|4289|
προθύμως|proq�mwj|qrphumzs|1) willingly, with alacrity<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G4290</b><br />Adverb from G4289; <i>with alacrity:</i> - willingly.<br />|4290|
προΐστημι|pro�sthmi|qrpistgmi|1) to set or place before<br />1a) to set over<br />1b) to be over, to superintend, preside over<br />1c) to be a protector or guardian<br />1c1) to give aid<br />1d) to care for, give attention to<br />1d1) profess honest occupations<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:700,*|<b>G4291</b><br />From G4253 and G2476; to <i>stand before</i>, that is, (in rank) to <i>preside</i>, or (by implication) to <i>practise:</i> - maintain, be over, rule.<br />|4291|
προκαλέομαι|prokal�omai|qrpkalepmai|1) to call forth<br />2) to call forth to one's self<br />2a) especially to challenge to a combat or contest with one<br />3) to provoke, to irritate<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:496,*|<b>G4292</b><br />Middle voice from G4253 and G2564; to <i>call forth to oneself</i> (<i>challenge</i>), that is, (by implication) to <i>irritate:</i> - provoke.<br />|4292|
προκαταγγέλλω|prokatagg�llw|qrpkataccellz|1) to announce beforehand (that a thing will be)<br />1a) of prophecies<br />2) to preannounce in the sense of to promise<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:70, 10|<b>G4293</b><br />From G4253 and G2605; to <i>announce beforehand</i>, that is, <i>predict</i>, <i>promise:</i> - foretell, have notice (shew) before.<br />|4293|
προκαταρτίζω|prokatart�zw|qrpkatartifz|1) to prepare beforehand<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4294</b><br />From G4253 and G2675; to <i>prepare in advance:</i> - make up beforehand.<br />|4294|
πρόκειμαι|pr�keimai|qrpkeimai|1) to lie or be placed before (a person or a thing) or in front of<br />2) to set before<br />2a) to be placed before the eyes, to lie in sight<br />2a1) to stand forth<br />2b) to be appointed, destined<br />2c) to be there, be present, be at hand<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:656, 425|<b>G4295</b><br />From G4253 and G2749; to <i>lie before</i> the view, that is, (figuratively) to <i>be present</i> (to the mind), to <i>stand forth</i> (as an example or reward): - be first, set before (forth).<br />|4295|
προκηρύσσω|prokhr�ssw|qrpkgrussz|1) to announce or proclaim be herald beforehand<br />2) to announce beforehand (of the herald himself)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:717, 430|<b>G4296</b><br />From G4253 and G2784; to <i>herald</i> (that is, <i>proclaim</i>) <i>in advance:</i> - before (first) preach.<br />|4296|
προκοπή|prokop�|qrpkpqg|1) progress, advancement<br /><b>Part of Speech: </b>comparative<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:703, 939|<b>G4297</b><br />From G4298; <i>progress</i>, that is, <i>advancement</i> (subjectively or objectively): - furtherance, profit.<br />|4297|
προκόπτω|prok�ptw|qrpkpqtz|1) to beat forward<br />1a) to lengthen out by hammering (as a smith forges metals)<br />1b) metaphorically to promote, forward, further<br />2) to go forward, advance, proceed<br />2a) of time: the night is far spent<br />2b) metaphorically to increase, make progress<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:703, 939|<b>G4298</b><br />From G4253 and G2875; to <i>drive forward</i> (as if by beating), that is, (figuratively and intransitively) to <i>advance</i> (in amount, to <i>grow</i>; in time, to <i>be well along</i>): - increase, proceed, profit, be far spent, wax.<br />|4298|
πρόκριμα|pr�krima|qrpkrima|1) an opinion formed before the facts are known<br />2) a prejudgment, a prejudice<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:953, 469|<b>G4299</b><br />From a compound of G4253 and G2919; a <i>prejudgment</i> (<i>prejudice</i>), that is, <i>prepossession:</i> - prefer one before another.<br />|4299|
προκυρόω|prokur�w|qrpkurpz|1) to sanction, ratify, or establish beforehand<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:1100, 494|<b>G4300</b><br />From G4253 and G2964; to <i>ratify previously:</i> - confirm before.<br />|4300|
προλαμβάνω|prolamb�nw|qrplambanz|1) to take before<br />2) to anticipate, to forestall<br />3) to take one by forestalling (him, i.e. before he can flee or conceal his crime)<br />3a) surprise, detect<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:14, 495|<b>G4301</b><br />From G4253 and G2983; to <i>take in advance</i>, that is, (literally) <i>eat before</i> others have an opportunity; (figuratively) to <i>anticipate</i>, <i>surprise:</i> - come aforehand, overtake, take before.<br />|4301|
προλέγω|prol�gw|qrplecz|1) to say beforehand, to predict<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4302</b><br />From G4253 and G3004; to <i>say beforehand</i>, that is, <i>predict</i>, <i>forewarn:</i> - foretell, tell before.<br />|4302|
προμαρτύρομαι|promart�romai|qrpmarturpmai|1) antetestor<br />2) to testify beforehand<br />2a) to make known, predict<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:510, 564|<b>G4303</b><br />From G4253 and G3143; to <i>be a witness in advance</i>, that is, <i>predict:</i> - testify beforehand.<br />|4303|
προμελετάω|promelet�w|qrpmeletaz|1) to meditate beforehand<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4304</b><br />From G4253 and G3191; to <i>premeditate:</i> - meditate before.<br />|4304|
προμεριμνάω|promerimn�w|qrpmerimnaz|1) to be anxious beforehand<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:589, 584|<b>G4305</b><br />From G4253 and G3309; to <i>care</i> (anxiously) <i>in advance:</i> - take thought beforehand.<br />|4305|
προνοέω|prono�w|qrpnpez|1) to perceive before, foresee<br />2) to provide, think of beforehand<br />2a) to provide for one<br />2b) to take thought for, care for a thing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:1009, 636|<b>G4306</b><br />From G4253 and G3539; to <i>consider in advance</i>, that is, <i>look</i> out for <i>beforehand</i> (active voice by way of <i>maintenance</i> for others; middle voice by way of <i>circumspection</i> for oneself): - provide (for).<br />|4306|
πρόνοια|pr�noia|qrpnpia|1) forethought, providential care<br />2) to make provision for a thing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:1011, 636|<b>G4307</b><br />From G4306; <i>forethought</i>, that is, provident <i>care</i> or <i>supply:</i> - providence, provision.<br />|4307|
προοράω|proor�w|qrppraz|1) to see before (whether as respects place or time)<br />2) to keep before one's eye's<br />3) metaphorically to be mindful of one always<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:381, 706|<b>G4308</b><br />From G4253 and G3708; to <i>behold in advance</i>, that is, (active voice) to <i>notice</i> (another) <i>previously</i>, or (middle voice) to <i>keep in</i> (one's own) <i>view:</i> - foresee, see before.<br />|4308|
προορίζω|proor�zw|qrpprifz|1) to predetermine, decide beforehand<br />2) in the NT of God decreeing from eternity<br />3) to foreordain, appoint beforehand<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:456, 728|<b>G4309</b><br />From G4253 and G3724; to <i>limit in advance</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>predetermine:</i> - determine before, ordain, predestinate.<br />|4309|
προπάσχω|prop�scw|qrpqasxz|1) to suffer before<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:924, 798|<b>G4310</b><br />From G4253 and G3958; to <i>undergo</i> hardship <i>previously:</i> - suffer before.<br />|4310|
προπέμπω|prop�mpw|qrpqemqz|1) to send before<br />2) to send forward, bring on the way, accompany or escort<br />3) to set one forward, fit him out with the requisites for a journey<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4311</b><br />From G4253 and G3992; to <i>send forward</i>, that is, <i>escort</i> or <i>aid</i> in travel: - accompany, bring (forward) on journey (way), conduct forth.<br />|4311|
προπετής|propet�j|qrpqetgs|1) to fall forwards, headlong, sloping, precipitously<br />2) precipitate, rash, reckless<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4312</b><br />From a compound of G4253 and G4098; <i>falling forward</i>, that is, <i>headlong</i> (figuratively <i>precipitate</i>): - heady, rash [-ly].<br />|4312|
προπορεύομαι|propore�omai|qrpqpreupmai|1) to send before, to make to precede<br />2) to go before one<br />2a) of a leader<br />2b) of a messenger or a herald<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4313</b><br />From G4253 and G4198; to <i>precede</i> (as guide or herald): - go before.<br />|4313|
πρός|pr�j|qrps|1) to the advantage of<br />2) at, near, by<br />3) to, towards, with, with regard to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> preposition<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:720, 942|<b>G4314</b><br />A strengthened form of G4253; a preposition of direction; <i>forward to</i>, that is, <i>toward</i> (with the genitive case <i>the side</i> of, that is, <i>pertaining to</i>; with the dative case <i>by the side of</i>, that is, <i>near to</i>; usually with the accusative case the place, time, occasion, or respect, which is the <i>destination</i> of the relation, that is, <i>whither</i> or <i>for</i> which it is predicated): - about, according to, against, among, at, because of, before, between, ([where-]) by, for, X at thy house, in, for intent, nigh unto, of, which pertain to, that, to (the end that), + together, to ([you]) -ward, unto, with (-in). In compounds it denotes essentially the same applications, namely, motion towards, accession to, or nearness at.<br />|4314|
προσάββατον|pros�bbaton|qrpsabbatpn|1) the day before the sabbath<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G4315</b><br />From G4253 and G4521; a <i>fore sabbath</i>, that is, the <i>sabbath eve</i>: - day before the sabbath. Compare G3904.<br />|4315|
προσαγορεύω|prosagore�w|qrpsacpreuz|1) to speak to, to address, accost, salute<br />2) especially to address or accost by some name, call by name<br />3) to give a name in public, to style<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4316</b><br />From G4314 and a derivative of G58 (meaning to <i>harangue</i>); to <i>address</i>, that is, salute by <i>name:</i> - call.<br />|4316|
προσάγω|pros�gw|qrpsacz|1) to lead, to bring<br />1a) to open a way of access, for one to God<br />1a1) to render one acceptable to God<br />1b) in a forensic sense, to summon (to trial or punishment)<br />2) to draw near to, approach<br />2a) the land which a sailor is approaching seeming to approach him<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:131, 20|<b>G4317</b><br />From G4314 and G71; to <i>lead towards</i>, that is, (transitively) to <i>conduct near</i> (<i>summon</i>, <i>present</i>), or (intransitively) to <i>approach:</i> - bring, draw near,<br />|4317|
προσαγωγή|prosagwg�|qrpsaczcg|1) the act of bringing to, a moving to<br />2) access, approach<br />2a) to God, i.e. that relationship with God whereby we are acceptable to him and have assurance that he is favourably disposed towards him<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:133, 20|<b>G4318</b><br />From G4317 (compare G72); <i>admission:</i> - access.<br />|4318|
προσαιτέω|prosait�w|qrpsaitez|1) to ask for in addition<br />2) to approach one with supplications<br />3) to ask alms<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4319</b><br />From G4314 and G154; to <i>ask repeatedly</i> (<i>importune</i>), that is, <i>solicit:</i> - beg.<br />|4319|
προσαναβαίνω|prosanaba�nw|qrpsanabainz|1) to go up further<br />2) go up higher<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4320</b><br />From G4314 and G305; to <i>ascend farther</i>, that is, <i>be promoted</i> (<i>take an upper</i> (<i>more honorable</i>) <i>seat</i>): - go up.<br />|4320|
προσαναλίσκω|prosanal�skw|qrpsanaliskz|1) to expend besides (i.e. upon physicians)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4321</b><br />From G4314 and G355; to <i>expend further:</i> - spend.<br />|4321|
προσαναπληρόω|prosanaplhr�w|qrpsanaqlgrpz|1) to fill up by adding to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4322</b><br />From G4314 and G378; to <i>fill up further</i>, that is, <i>furnish fully:</i> - supply.<br />|4322|
προσανατίθεμαι|prosanat�qemai|qrpsanatihemai|1) to lay upon in addition to<br />2) to lay upon one's self in addition<br />2a) to undertake besides<br />2b) to put one's self upon another by going to him<br />2c) to commit or betake one's self to another for the purpose of consulting him<br />2d) to consult, to take one into counsel<br />2e) to add from one's store<br />3) to communicate, impart<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 1:353, 57|<b>G4323</b><br />From G4314 and G394; to <i>lay up in addition</i>, that is, (middle voice and figuratively) to <i>impart</i> or (by implication) to <i>consult:</i> - in conference add, confer.<br />|4323|
προσαπειλέομαι|prosapeil�omai|qrpsaqeilepmai|1) to add threats, threaten further<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4324</b><br />From G4314 and G546; to <i>menace additionally:</i> - threaten further.<br />|4324|
προσδαπανάω|prosdapan�w|qrpsdaqanaz|1) to spend besides<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4325</b><br />From G4314 and G1159; to <i>expend additionally:</i> - spend more.<br />|4325|
προσδέομαι|prosd�omai|qrpsdepmai|1) to want besides, need in addition<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:41, 143|<b>G4326</b><br />From G4314 and G1189; to <i>require additionally</i>, that is, <i>want further:</i> - need.<br />|4326|
προσδέχομαι|prosd�comai|qrpsdexpmai|1) to receive to one's self, to admit, to give access to one's self<br />1a) to admit one, receive one into intercourse and companionship<br />1b) to receive one (coming from some place)<br />1c) to accept (not to reject) a thing offered<br />2) to expect: the fulfilment of promises<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:57, 146|<b>G4327</b><br />From G4314 and G1209; to <i>admit</i> (to intercourse, hospitality, credence or (figuratively) endurance); by implication to <i>await</i> (with confidence or patience): - accept, allow, look (wait) for, take.<br />|4327|
προσδοκάω|prosdok�w|qrpsdpkaz|1) to expect (whether in thought, in hope, or in fear)<br />2) to look for, wait for<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:725, 943|<b>G4328</b><br />From G4314 and <span class="uni">δοκεύω</span> dokeu&ocirc; (to <i>watch</i>); to <i>anticipate</i> (in thought, hope or fear); by implication to <i>await:</i> - (be in) expect (-ation), look (for), when looked, tarry, wait for.<br />|4328|
προσδοκία|prosdok�a|qrpsdpkia|1) expectation (whether good or evil)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:725, 943|<b>G4329</b><br />From G4328; <i>apprehension</i> (of evil); by implication <i>infliction</i> anticipated: - expectation, looking after.<br />|4329|
προσεάω|prose�w|qrpseaz|1) to permit one to approach or arrive<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4330</b><br />From G4314 and G1439; to <i>permit further</i> progress: - suffer.<br />|4330|
προσεγγίζω|prosegg�zw|qrpseccifz|1) to approach unto<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:330, 194|<b>G4331</b><br />From G4314 and G1448; to <i>approach near:</i> - come nigh.<br />|4331|
παρεδρεύω|paredre�w|qaredreuz|1) to sit near<br />2) to attend assiduously<br />3) to be in attendance upon, not to quit one's side<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4332</b><br />From a compound of G4314 and the base of G1476; to <i>sit near</i>, that is, <i>attend</i> as a servant: - wait at.<br />|4332|
προσεργάζομαι|proserg�zomai|qrpsercafpmai|1) to work besides<br />2) by working or trading to make or gain besides<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4333</b><br />From G4314 and G2038; to <i>work additionally</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>acquire besides:</i> - gain.<br />|4333|
προσέρχομαι|pros�rcomai|qrpserxpmai|1) to come to, approach<br />2) draw near to<br />3) to assent to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:683, 257|<b>G4334</b><br />From G4314 and G2064 (including its alternate); to <i>approach</i>, that is, (literally) <i>come near</i>, <i>visit</i>, or (figuratively) <i>worship</i>, <i>assent to:</i> - (as soon as he) come (unto), come thereunto, consent, draw near, go (near, to, unto).<br />|4334|
προσευχή|proseuc�|qrpseuxg|1) prayer addressed to God<br />2) a place set apart or suited for the offering of prayer<br />2a) a synagogue<br />2b) a place in the open air where the Jews were wont to pray, outside the cities, where they had no synagogue<br />2b1) such places were situated upon the bank of a stream or the shore of a sea, where there was a supply of water for washing the hands before prayer<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:807, 279|<b>G4335</b><br />From G4336; <i>prayer</i> (<i>worship</i>); by implication an <i>oratory</i> (<i>chapel</i>): - X pray earnestly, prayer.<br />|4335|
προσεύχομαι|prose�comai|qrpseuxpmai|1) to offer prayers, to pray<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:807, 279|<b>G4336</b><br />From G4314 and G2172; to <i>pray to</i> God, that is, <i>supplicate</i>, <i>worship:</i> - pray (X earnestly, for), make prayer.<br />|4336|
προσέχω|pros�cw|qrpsexz|1) to bring to, bring near<br />1a) to bring a ship to land, and simply to touch at, put in<br />2) to turn the mind to, attend to be attentive<br />2a) to a person or a thing: of caring for, providing for<br />3) to attend to one's self, i.e. to give heed to one's self<br />3a) give attention to, take heed<br />4) to apply one's self to, attach one's self to, hold or cleave to a person or a thing<br />4a) to be given or addicted to<br />4b) to devote thought and effort to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4337</b><br />From G4314 and G2192; (figuratively) to <i>hold</i> the mind (G3563 implied) <i>towards</i>, that is, <i>pay attention to</i>, <i>be cautious about</i>, <i>apply oneself to</i>, <i>adhere to:</i> - (give) attend (-ance, -ance at, -ance to, unto), beware, be given to, give (take) heed (to, unto) have regard.<br />|4337|
προσηλόω|proshl�w|qrpsglpz|1) to fasten with nails to, nail to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4338</b><br />From G4314 and a derivative of G2247; to <i>peg to</i>, that is, <i>spike</i> fast: - nail to.<br />|4338|
προσήλυτος|pros�lutoj|qrpsglutps|1) a newcomer<br />1a) a stranger, alien<br />2) a proselyte<br />2a) one who has come over from a Gentile religion to Judaism<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:727, 943|<b>G4339</b><br />From the alternate of G4334; an <i>arriver</i> from a foreign region, that is, (specifically) an <i>acceder</i> (<i>convert</i>) to Judaism ("proselyte"): - proselyte.<br />|4339|
πρόσκαιρος|pr�skairoj|qrpskairps|1) for a season<br />2) enduring only for a while<br />3) temporary<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:463, 389|<b>G4340</b><br />From G4314 and G2540; <i>for</i> the <i>occasion</i> only, that is, <i>temporary:</i> - dur- [eth] for awhile, endure for a time, for a season, temporal.<br />|4340|
προσκαλέομαι|proskal�omai|qrpskalepmai|1) to call to<br />2) to call to one's self<br />3) to bid to come to one's self<br />4) metaphorically<br />4a) God is said to call to himself the Gentiles, aliens as they are from him, by inviting them, through the preaching of the gospel unto fellowship with himself in the Messiah's kingdom<br />4b) Christ and the Holy Sprit are said to call to themselves those preachers of the gospel to whom they have decided to intrust a service having reference to the extension of the gospel<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:500,*|<b>G4341</b><br />Middle voice from G4314 and G2564; to <i>call toward oneself</i>, that is, <i>summon</i>, <i>invite:</i> - call (for, to, unto).<br />|4341|
προσκαρτερέω|proskarter�w|qrpskarterez|1) to adhere to one, be his adherent, to be devoted or constant to one<br />2) to be steadfastly attentive unto, to give unremitting care to a thing<br />3) to continue all the time in a place<br />4) to persevere and not to faint<br />5) to show one's self courageous for<br />6) to be in constant readiness for one, wait on constantly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:618, 417|<b>G4342</b><br />From G4314 and G2594; to <i>be earnest towards</i>, that is, (to a thing) to <i>persevere</i>, <i>be constantly</i> diligent, or (in a place) to <i>attend</i> assiduously all the exercises, or (to a person) to <i>adhere</i> closely <i>to</i> (as a servitor): - attend (give self) continually (upon), continue (in, instant in, with), wait on (continually).<br />|4342|
προσκαρτέρησις|proskart�rhsij|qrpskartergsis|1) perseverance<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:619, 417|<b>G4343</b><br />From G4342; <i>persistency:</i> - perseverance.<br />|4343|
προσκεφάλαιον|proskef�laion|qrpskevalaipn|1) a pillow, cushion<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G4344</b><br />Neuter of a presumed compound of G4314 and G2776; something <i>for</i> the <i>head</i>, that is, a <i>cushion:</i> - pillow.<br />|4344|
προσκληρόομαι|prosklhr�omai|qrpsklgrppmai|1) to add or assign by lot, to allot<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:765, 442|<b>G4345</b><br />From G4314 and G2820; to <i>give</i> a common <i>lot to</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>associate with:</i> - consort with.<br />|4345|
πρόσκλισις|pr�sklisij|qrpsklisis|1) an inclination or proclivity of mind<br />2) a joining the party of one<br />3) partiality<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4346</b><br />From a compound of G4314 and G2827; a <i>leaning towards</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>proclivity</i> (<i>favoritism</i>): - partiality.<br />|4346|
προσκολλάομαι|proskoll�omai|qrpskpllapmai|1) to glue upon, glue to<br />2) to join one's self to closely, cleave to, stick to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:823, 452|<b>G4347</b><br />From G4314 and G2853; to <i>glue to</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>adhere:</i> - cleave, join (self).<br />|4347|
πρόσκομμα|pr�skomma|qrpskpmma|1) a stumbling block<br />1a) an obstacle in the way which if one strikes his foot against he stumbles or falls<br />1b) that over which a soul stumbles, i.e. by which is caused to sin<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:745, 946|<b>G4348</b><br />From G4350; a <i>stub</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>occasion of apostasy:</i> - offence, stumbling (-block,[-stone]).<br />|4348|
προσκοπή|proskop�|qrpskpqg|1) an occasion of stumbling<br />2) to do something which causes others to stumble<br />2a) i.e. leads them into error or sin<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:745, 946|<b>G4349</b><br />From G4350; a <i>stumbling</i>, that is, (figuratively and concretely) <i>occasion of sin:</i> - offence.<br />|4349|
προσκόπτω|prosk�ptw|qrpskpqtz|1) to strike against<br />1a) of those who strike against a stone or other obstacle in the path, to stumble<br />1b) to strike one's foot against a stone<br />1b1) i.e. to meet with some harm<br />1c) to rush upon, beat against<br />1d) to be made to stumble by a thing<br />1d1) i.e. metaphorically to be induced to sin<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:745, 946|<b>G4350</b><br />From G4314 and G2875; to <i>strike at</i>, that is, <i>surge against</i> (as water); specifically to <i>stub on</i>, that is, <i>trip up</i> (literally or figuratively): - beat upon, dash, stumble (at).<br />|4350|
προσκυλίω|proskul�w|qrpskuliz|1) to roll to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4351</b><br />From G4314 and G2947; to <i>roll towards</i>, that is, <i>block against:</i> - roll (to).<br />|4351|
προσκυνέω|proskun�w|qrpskunez|1) to kiss the hand to (towards) one, in token of reverence<br />2) among the Orientals, especially the Persians, to fall upon the knees and touch the ground with the forehead as an expression of profound reverence<br />3) in the NT by kneeling or prostration to do homage (to one) or make obeisance, whether in order to express respect or to make supplication<br />3a) used of homage shown to men and beings of superior rank<br />3a1) to the Jewish high priests<br />3a2) to God<br />3a3) to Christ<br />3a4) to heavenly beings<br />3a5) to demons<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:758, 948|<b>G4352</b><br />From G4314 and probably a derivative of G2965 (meaning to <i>kiss</i>, like a dog <i>licking</i> his master's hand); to <i>fawn</i> or <i>crouch to</i>, that is, (literally or figuratively) <i>prostrate</i> oneself in homage (<i>do reverence</i> to, <i>adore</i>): - worship.<br />|4352|
προσκυνητής|proskunht�j|qrpskungtgs|1) a worshipper<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:766, 948|<b>G4353</b><br />From G4352; an <i>adorer:</i> - worshipper.<br />|4353|
προσλαλέω|proslal�w|qrpslalez|1) to speak to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4354</b><br />From G4314 and G2980; to <i>talk to</i>, that is, <i>converse with:</i> - speak to (with).<br />|4354|
προσλαμβάνομαι|proslamb�nomai|qrpslambanpmai|1) to take to, take in addition, to take to one's self<br />1a) to take as one's companion<br />1b) to take by the hand in order to lead aside<br />1c) to take or receive into one's home, with the collateral idea of kindness<br />1d) to receive, i.e. grant one access to one's heart<br />1d1) to take into friendship and intercourse<br />1e) to take to one's self, to take: i.e. food<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:15, 495|<b>G4355</b><br />From G4314 and G2983; to <i>take to</i> oneself, that is, <i>use</i> (food), <i>lead</i> (aside), <i>admit</i> (to friendship or hospitality): - receive, take (unto).<br />|4355|
πρόσλημψις|pr�slhmyij|qrpslgmyis|1) a receiving: into the kingdom of God<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:15, 495|<b>G4356</b><br />From G4355; <i>admission:</i> - receiving.<br />|4356|
προσμένω|prosm�nw|qrpsmenz|1) to remain with, to continue with one<br />2) to hold fast to: the grace of God received in the Gospel<br />3) to remain still, tarry, stay<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:579, 581|<b>G4357</b><br />From G4314 and G3306; to <i>stay further</i>, that is, <i>remain</i> in a place, with a person; figuratively to <i>adhere</i> to, <i>persevere</i> in: - abide still, be with, cleave unto, continue in (with).<br />|4357|
προσορμίζομαι|prosorm�zomai|qrpsprmifpmai|1) to bring a ship to moorings<br />2) to take one's station near the shore<br />3) to moor, come to anchor<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4358</b><br />From G4314 and a derivative of the same as G3730 (meaning to <i>tie</i> (<i>anchor</i>) or <i>lull</i>); to <i>moor to</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>land at:</i> - draw to the shore.<br />|4358|
προσοφείλω|prosofe�lw|qrpspveilz|1) to owe beside<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4359</b><br />From G4314 and G3784; to <i>be indebted additionally:</i> - over besides.<br />|4359|
προσοχθίζω|prosocq�zw|qrpspxhifz|1) to be wroth or displeased with<br />2) to loathe<br />3) to spew out<br />4) to be disgusted with<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4360</b><br />From G4314 and a form of <span class="uni">ὀχθέω</span> ochthe&ocirc; (to <i>be vexed</i> with something irksome); to <i>feel indignant at:</i> - be grieved with.<br />|4360|
πρόσπεινος|pr�speinoj|qrpsqeinps|1) very hungry<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4361</b><br />From G4314 and the same as G3983; <i>hungering further</i>, that is, <i>intensely hungry:</i> - very hungry.<br />|4361|
προσπήγνυμι|prosp�gnumi|qrpsqgcnumi|1) to fasten<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4362</b><br />From G4314 and G4078; to <i>fasten to</i>, that is, (specifically) to <i>impale</i> (on a cross): - crucify.<br />|4362|
προσπίπτω|prosp�ptw|qrpsqiqtz|1) to fall forwards, fall down, prostrate one's self before, in homage or supplication: at one's feet<br />2) to rush upon, beat against<br />2a) of winds beating upon a house<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4363</b><br />From G4314 and G4098; to <i>fall towards</i>, that is, (gently) <i>prostrate</i> oneself (in supplication or homage), or (violently) to <i>rush</i> upon (in storm): - beat upon, fall (down) at (before).<br />|4363|
προσποιέομαι|prospoi�omai|qrpsqpiepmai|1) to take or claim a thing to one's self<br />2) to conform one's self to a thing, or rather to affect to one's self<br />2a) to pretend<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4364</b><br />Middle voice from G4314 and G4160; to <i>do forward for oneself</i>, that is, <i>pretend</i> (as if about to do a thing): - make as though.<br />|4364|
προσπορεύομαι|prospore�omai|qrpsqpreupmai|1) to draw near, approach<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4365</b><br />From G4314 and G4198; to <i>journey towards</i>, that is, <i>approach</i> (not the same as G4313): - go before.<br />|4365|
προσρήγνυμι|prosr�gnumi|qrpsrgcnumi|1) to break against, break by dashing against<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4366</b><br />From G4314 and G4486; to <i>tear towards</i>, that is, <i>burst upon</i> (as a tempest or flood): - beat vehemently against (upon).<br />|4366|
προστάσσω|prost�ssw|qrpstassz|1) to assign or ascribe to, join to<br />2) to enjoin, order, prescribe, command<br />2a) to appoint, to define<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:37, 1156|<b>G4367</b><br />From G4314 and G5021; to <i>arrange towards</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>enjoin:</i> - bid, command.<br />|4367|
προστάτις|prost�tij|qrpstatis|1) a woman set over others<br />2) a female guardian, protectress, patroness, caring for the affairs of others and aiding them with her resources<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4368</b><br />Feminine of a derivative of G4291; a <i>patroness</i>, that is, <i>assistant:</i> - succourer.<br />|4368|
προστίθημι|prost�qhmi|qrpstihgmi|1) to put to<br />2) to add<br />2a) i.e. to join to, gather with any company, the number of one's followers or companions<br />2a1) he was gathered to his fathers, i.e. died<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:167, 1176|<b>G4369</b><br />From G4314 and G5087; to <i>place additionally</i>, that is, <i>lay beside</i>, <i>annex</i>, <i>repeat:</i> - add, again, give more, increase, lay unto, proceed further, speak to any more.<br />|4369|
προστρέχω|prostr�cw|qrpstrexz|1) to run to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4370</b><br />From G4314 and G5143 (including its alternate); to <i>run towards</i>, that is, <i>hasten</i> to meet or join: - run (thither to, to).<br />|4370|
προσφάγιον|prosf�gion|qrpsvacipn|1) anything eaten with bread<br />1a) spoken of fish boiled or broiled<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G4371</b><br />Neuter of a presumed derivative of a compound of G4314 and G5315; something <i>eaten in addition</i> to bread, that is, a <i>relish</i> (specifically <i>fish</i>; compare G3795): - meat.<br />|4371|
πρόσφατος|pr�sfatoj|qrpsvatps|1) lately slaughtered, freshly killed<br />2) recently made, new<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:766, 950|<b>G4372</b><br />From G4253 and a derivative of G4969; <i>previously</i> (<i>recently</i>) <i>slain</i> (<i>fresh</i>), that is, (figuratively) <i>lately made:</i> - new.<br />|4372|
προσφάτως|prosf�twj|qrpsvatzs|1) lately<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:766, 950|<b>G4373</b><br />Adverb from G4372; <i>recently:</i> - lately.<br />|4373|
προσφέρω|prosf�rw|qrpsverz|1) to bring to, lead to<br />1a) one to a person who can heal him or is ready to show him some kindness, one to a person who is to judge him<br />1b) to bring a present or a thing, to reach or hand a thing to one<br />1c) to put to<br />2) to be borne towards one, to attack, assail<br />2a) to behave one's self towards one, deal with one<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:65, 1252|<b>G4374</b><br />From G4314 and G5342 (including its alternate); to <i>bear towards</i>, that is, <i>lead to</i>, <i>tender</i> (especially to God), <i>treat:</i> - bring (to, unto), deal with, do, offer (unto, up), present unto, put to.<br />|4374|
προσφιλής|prosfil�j|qrpsvilgs|1) acceptable, pleasing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4375</b><br />From a presumed compound of G4314 and G5368; <i>friendly towards</i>, that is, <i>acceptable:</i> - lovely.<br />|4375|
προσφορά|prosfor�|qrpsvpra|1) the act of offering, a bringing to<br />2) that which is offered, a gift, a present. In the NT a<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:68, 1252|<b>G4376</b><br />From G4374; <i>presentation</i>; concretely an <i>oblation</i> (bloodless) or <i>sacrifice:</i> - offering (up).<br />|4376|
προσφωνέω|prosfwn�w|qrpsvznez|1) to call to, to address by calling<br />2) to call to one's self, summon<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4377</b><br />From G4314 and G5455; to <i>sound towards</i>, that is, <i>address</i>, <i>exclaim</i>, <i>summon:</i> - call unto, speak (un-) to.<br />|4377|
πρόσχυσις|pr�scusij|qrpsxusis|1) a pouring or sprinkling upon, affusion<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4378</b><br />From a compound of G4314 and <span class="uni">χέω</span> che&ocirc; (to <i>pour</i>); a <i>shedding forth</i>, that is, <i>affusion:</i> - sprinkling.<br />|4378|
προσψαύω|prosya�w|qrpsyauz|1) to touch<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4379</b><br />From G4314 and <span class="uni">ψαύω</span> psau&ocirc; (to <i>touch</i>); to <i>impinge</i>, that is, <i>lay a finger on</i> (in order to relieve): - touch.<br />|4379|
προσωπολημπτέω|proswpolhmpt�w|qrpszqplgmqtez|1) to respect the person (i.e. the external condition of man)<br />2) to have respect of persons, discriminate<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:779, 950|<b>G4380</b><br />From G4381; to <i>favor an individual</i>, that is, <i>show partiality:</i> - have respect to persons.<br />|4380|
προσωπολήμπτης|proswpol�mpthj|qrpszqplgmqtgs|1) an acceptor of persons<br />2) one who discriminates<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:779, 950|<b>G4381</b><br />From G4383 and G2983; an <i>accepter</i> of <i>a face</i> (<i>individual</i>), that is, (specifically) one <i>exhibiting partiality:</i> - respecter of persons.<br />|4381|
προσωπολημψία|proswpolhmy�a|qrpszqplgmyia|1) respect of persons<br />2) partiality<br />2a) the fault of one who when called on to give judgment has respect of the outward circumstances of man and not to their intrinsic merits, and so prefers, as the more worthy, one who is rich, high born, or powerful, to another who does not have these qualities<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:779, 950|<b>G4382</b><br />From G4381; <i>partiality</i>, that is, <i>favoritism:</i> - respect of persons.<br />|4382|
πρόσωπον|pr�swpon|qrpszqpn|1) the face<br />1a) the front of the human head<br />1b) countenance, look<br />1b1) the face so far forth as it is the organ of sight, and by it various movements and changes) the index of the inward thoughts and feelings<br />1c) the appearance one presents by his wealth or property, his rank or low condition<br />1c1) outward circumstances, external condition<br />1c2) used in expressions which denote to regard the person in one's judgment and treatment of men<br />2) the outward appearance of inanimate things<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:768, 950|<b>G4383</b><br />From G4314 and <span class="uni">ὤψ</span> &ocirc;ps (the <i>visage</i>; from G3700); the <i>front</i> (as being <i>towards view</i>), that is, the <i>countenance</i>, <i>aspect</i>, <i>appearance</i>, <i>surface</i>; by implication <i>presence</i>, <i>person:</i> - (outward) appearance, X before, countenance, face, fashion, (men's) person, presence.<br />|4383|
προτάσσω|prot�ssw|qrptassz|1) to place before<br />2) to appoint before, define beforehand<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4384</b><br />From G4253 and G5021; to <i>pre-arrange</i>, that is, <i>prescribe:</i> - before appoint.<br />|4384|
προτείνω|prote�nw|qrpteinz|1) to stretch forth, stretch out<br />1a) when they had stretched one out on the thongs, i.e. to receive the blows of the thongs (by tying him up to a beam or a pillar)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4385</b><br />From G4253 and <span class="uni">τείνω</span> tein&ocirc; (to <i>stretch</i>); to <i>protend</i>, that is, <i>tie prostrate</i> (for scourging): - bind.<br />|4385|
πρότερος|pr�teroj|qrpterps|1) before, prior<br />1a) of time, previous, former<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4387</b><br />Comparative of G4253; <i>prior</i> or <i>previous:</i> - former.<br />|4387|
προτίθεμαι|prot�qemai|qrptihemai|1) to place before, to set forth<br />1a) to set forth to be looked at, expose to view<br />1b) to expose to public view<br />1b1) of the bodies of the dead<br />1b2) to let lie in state<br />2) to set before one's self, propose to one's self<br />2a) to purpose, determine<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:164, 1176|<b>G4388</b><br />Middle voice from G4253 and G5087; to <i>place before</i>, that is, (for oneself) to <i>exhibit</i>; (to oneself) to <i>propose</i> (<i>determine</i>): - purpose, set forth.<br />|4388|
προτρέπομαι|protr�pomai|qrptreqpmai|1) to urge forwards, exhort, encourage<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4389</b><br />Middle voice from G4253 and the base of G5157; to <i>turn forward</i> for oneself, that is, <i>encourage:</i> - exhort.<br />|4389|
προτρέχω|protr�cw|qrptrexz|1) to run before, to outrun<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4390</b><br />From G4253 and G5143 (including its alternate); to <i>run forward</i>, that is, <i>outstrip</i>, <i>precede:</i> - outrun, run before.<br />|4390|
προϋπάρχω|pro�p�rcw|qrpuqarxz|1) to be before, exist previously<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4391</b><br />From G4253 and G5225; to <i>exist before</i>, that is, (adverbially) to <i>be</i> or <i>do</i> something <i>previously:</i> - + be before (-time).<br />|4391|
πρόφασις|pr�fasij|qrpvasis|1) a pretext (alleged reason, pretended cause)<br />2) show<br />2a) under colour as though they would do something<br />2b) in pretence, ostensibly<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4392</b><br />From a compound of G4253 and G5316; an <i>outward showing</i>, that is, <i>pretext:</i> - cloke, colour, pretence, show.<br />|4392|
