Πρόχορος|Pr�coroj|qrpxprps|Prochorus = "leader of the chorus"<br />1) one of the seven deacons chosen by the church at Jerusalem<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G4402</b><br />From G4253 and G5525; <i>before</i> the <i>dance</i>; <i>Prochorus</i>, a Christian: - Prochorus.<br />|4402|
πρύμνα|pr�mna|qrumna|1) the stern or hinder part of the ship<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4403</b><br />Feminine of <span class="uni">πρυμνύς</span> prumnus (<i>hindmost</i>); the <i>stern</i> of a ship: - hinder part, stern.<br />|4403|
