Πτολεμαΐς|Ptolema�j|qtplemais|Ptolemais or Accho = "warlike"<br />1) a maritime city of Phoenicia, which got its name, apparently, from Ptolemy Lathyrus, who captured it 103 BC, and rebuilt it more beautifully<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G4424</b><br />From "ptolemaios" (<i>Ptolemy</i>, after whom it was named); <i>Ptolemais</i>, a place in Palestine: - Ptolemais.<br />|4424|
