σκάφη|sk�fh|skavg|1) anything dug out, hollow vessel, trough, tray, tub<br />2) of a boat<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4627</b><br />A "skiff" (as if <i>dug</i> out), or <i>yawl</i> (carried aboard a large vessel for landing): - boat.<br />|4627|
σκέλος|sk�loj|skelps|1) the leg, from the hip to the toes inclusive<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G4628</b><br />Apparently from <span class="uni">σκέλλω</span> skell&ocirc; (to <i>parch</i>; through the idea of <i>leanness</i>); the <i>leg</i> (as <i>lank</i>): - leg.<br />|4628|
