σκιρτάω|skirt�w|skirtaz|1) to leap<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:401, 1046|<b>G4640</b><br />Akin to <span class="uni">σκαίρω</span> skair&ocirc; (to <i>skip</i>); to <i>jump</i>, that is, sympathetically <i>move</i> (as the <i>quickening</i> of a fetus): - leap (for joy).<br />|4640|
σκληροκαρδία|sklhrokard�a|sklgrpkardia|1) hardness of heart<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 3:613, 415|<b>G4641</b><br />Feminine of a compound of G4642 and G2588; <i>hard heartedness</i>, that is, (specifically) <i>destitution of</i> (spiritual) <i>perception:</i> - hardness of heart.<br />|4641|
