σκόλοψ|sk�loy|skplpy|1) a pointed piece of wood, a pale, a stake<br />2) a sharp stake, splinter<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:409, 1047|<b>G4647</b><br />Perhaps form the base of G4628 and G3700; <i>withered</i> at the <i>front</i>, that is, a <i>point</i> or <i>prickle</i> (figuratively a bodily <i>annoyance</i> or <i>disability</i>): - thorn.<br />|4647|
