σκορπίος|skorp�oj|skprqips|1) a scorpion, the name of a little animal, somewhat resembling a lobster, which in warm regions lurk, especially in stone walls; it has a poisonous sting in its tail<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G4651</b><br />Probably from <span class="uni">σκέρπω</span> skerp&ocirc;, an obsolete word, (perhaps strengthened from the base of G4649 and meaning to <i>pierce</i>); a "scorpion" (from its <i>sting</i>): - scorpion.<br />|4651|
