σκυθρωπός|skuqrwp�j|skuhrzqps|1) of a sad and gloomy countenance<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:450, 1053|<b>G4659</b><br />From <span class="uni">σκυθρός</span> skuthros (<i>sullen</i>) and a derivative of G3700; <i>angry visaged</i>, that is, <i>gloomy</i> or affecting a <i>mournful</i> appearance: - of a sad countenance.<br />|4659|
