σμυρνίζω|smurn�zw|smurnifz|1) to be like myrrh<br />2) to mix and so flavour with myrrh<br />2a) wine with myrrh: i.e. wine flavoured with myrrh. The ancients used to infuse myrrh into wine to give it a more agreeable fragrance and flavour<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:458, 1055|<b>G4669</b><br />From G4667; to <i>tincture with myrrh</i>, that is, <i>embitter</i> (as a narcotic): - mingle with myrrh.<br />|4669|
