σπαργανόω|spargan�w|sqarcanpz|1) to wrap in swaddling clothes<br />1a) of an infant just born<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4683</b><br />From <span class="uni">σπάργανον</span> sparganon (a <i>strip</i>; from a derivative of the base of G4682 meaning to <i>strap</i> or <i>wrap</i> with strips); to <i>swathe</i> (an infant after the Oriental custom): - wrap in swaddling clothes.<br />|4683|
