σπεῖρα|spe�ra|sqeira|1) anything rolled into a circle or ball, anything wound, rolled up, folded together<br />2) a military cohort<br />2a) the tenth part of legion<br />2a1) about 600 men, i.e. legionaries<br />2a2) if auxiliaries either 500 or 1000<br />2a3) a maniple, or the thirtieth part of a legion<br />2b) any band, company, or detachment, of soldiers<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4686</b><br />Of immediate Latin origin, but ultimately a derivative of G138 in the sense of its cognate, G1507; a <i>coil</i> (<i>spira</i>, "spire"), that is, (figuratively) a <i>mass</i> of men (a Roman military <i>cohort</i>; also [by analogy] a <i>squad</i> of Levitical janitors): - band.<br />|4686|
