στενάζω|sten�zw|stenafz|1) a sigh, to groan<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:600, 1076|<b>G4727</b><br />From G4728; to <i>make</i> (intransitively <i>be</i>) <i>in straits</i>, that is, (by implication) to <i>sigh</i>, <i>murmur</i>, <i>pray</i> inaudibly: - with grief, groan, grudge, sigh.<br />|4727|
