στενοχωρέομαι|stenocwr�omai|stenpxzrepmai|1) to be in a narrow place<br />2) to straiten, compress, cramp, reduce to straits<br />2a) to be sorely straitened in spirit<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:604, 1077|<b>G4729</b><br />From the same as G4730; to <i>hem</i> in closely, that is, (figuratively) <i>cramp:</i> - distress, straiten.<br />|4729|
στενοχωρία|stenocwr�a|stenpxzria|1) narrowness of place, a narrow place<br />2) metaphorically dire calamity, extreme affliction<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:604, 1077|<b>G4730</b><br />From a compound of G4728 and G5561; <i>narrowness of room</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>calamity:</i> - anguish, distress.<br />|4730|
