στίλβω|st�lbw|stilbz|1) to shine, glisten<br />1a) of garments<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:665, 1087|<b>G4744</b><br />Apparently a primary verb; to <i>gleam</i>, that is, <i>flash</i> intensely: - shining.<br />|4744|
στοά|sto�|stpa|1) a portico, a covered colonnade where people can stand or walk protected from the weather and the heat of the sun<br />2) the portico built by Solomon in the eastern part of the temple<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4745</b><br />Probably from G2476; a <i>colonnade</i> or interior <i>piazza:</i> - porch.<br />|4745|
