στρατεία|strate�a|strateia|1) an expedition, campaign, military service, warfare<br />2) metaphorically Paul likens his contest with the difficulties that oppose him in the discharge of his apostolic duties, as warfare<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:701, 1091|<b>G4752</b><br />From G4754; military <i>service</i>, that is, (figuratively) the apostolic <i>career</i> (as one of hardship and danger): - warfare.<br />|4752|
