στρώννυμι|str�nnumi|strznnumi|1) to spread<br />2) furnish<br />3) to spread with couches or divans<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4766</b><br />Or a simpler form <span class="uni">στρωννύω</span> str&ocirc;nnu&ocirc; <i>strone'-noo'-o</i>, prolonged from a still simpler form <span class="uni">στρόω</span> stro&ocirc; <i>stro'-o</i> (used only as an alternate in certain tenses; probably akin to G4731 through the idea of <i>positing</i>); to "strew", that is, <i>spread</i> (as a carpet or couch): - make bed, furnish, spread, strew.<br />|4766|
στυγητός|stught�j|stucgtps|1) hated, detestable<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G4767</b><br />From a derivative of an obsolete, apparently primary, word <span class="uni">στύγω</span> stug&ocirc; (to <i>hate</i>); <i>hated</i>, that is, <i>odious:</i> - hateful.<br />|4767|
