συλλυπέομαι|sullup�omai|sulluqepmai|1) to affect with grief together<br />2) give with one's self<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:323,*|<b>G4818</b><br />From G4862 and G3076; to <i>afflict jointly</i>, that is, (passively) <i>sorrow at</i> (on account of) some one: - be grieved.<br />|4818|
