συμβάλλω|sumb�llw|sumballz|1) to throw together, to bring together<br />1a) to converse<br />1b) to bring together in one's mind, confer with one's self<br />1c) to come together, meet<br />1c1) to encounter in a hostile sense<br />1c2) to fight with one<br />1c3) to bring together of one's property, to contribute, aid, help<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4820</b><br />From G4862 and G906; to <i>combine</i>, that is, (in speaking) to <i>converse</i>, <i>consult</i>, <i>dispute</i>, (mentally) to <i>consider</i>, (by implication) to <i>aid</i>, (personally) to <i>join</i>, <i>attack:</i> - confer, encounter, help, make, meet with, ponder.<br />|4820|
