Συμεών|Sume�n|sumezn|Simon = "harkening"<br />1) the second son of Jacob by Leah<br />2) one of Abraham's descendants<br />3) the one who took the infant Jesus in his arms in the temple<br />4) a teacher at the church of Antioch<br />5) the original name of Peter the apostle<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G4826</b><br />From the same as G4613; <i>Symeon</i> (that is, <i>Shimon</i>), the name of five Israelites: - Simeon, Simon.<br />|4826|
συμμαθητής|summaqht�j|summahgtgs|1) a fellow disciple<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:460, 552|<b>G4827</b><br />From a compound of G4862 and G3129; a <i>co-learner</i> (of Christianity): - fellowdisciple.<br />|4827|
