συμφωνέω|sumfwn�w|sumvznez|1) to agree together<br />2) to agree with one in making a bargain, to make an agreement, to bargain<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:304, 1287|<b>G4856</b><br />From G4859; to be <i>harmonious</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>accord</i> (<i>be suitable</i>, <i>concur</i>) or <i>stipulate</i> (by compact): - agree (together, with).<br />|4856|
