συνδοξάζομαι|sundox�zomai|sundpoafpmai|1) to approve together, to join in approving<br />2) to glorify together<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:253 & 7:787, 178 & 1102|<b>G4888</b><br />From G4862 and G1392; to <i>exalt</i> to dignity in company (that is, <i>similarly</i>) <i>with:</i> - glorify together.<br />|4888|
σύνδουλος|s�ndouloj|sundpulps|1) a fellow servant, one who serves the same master with another<br />1a) the associate of a servant (or slave)<br />1b) one who with others serves (ministers to) a king<br />1c) a colleague of one who is Christ's servant in publishing the gospel<br />1d) one who with others acknowledges the same Lord, Jesus, and obeys his commands<br />1e) one who with others is subject to the same divine authority in the Messianic economy<br />1e1) of angels as the fellow servants of Christians<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:261, 182|<b>G4889</b><br />From G4862 and G1401; a <i>co-slave</i>, that is, <i>servitor</i> or <i>ministrant of the same master</i> (human or divine): - fellowservant.<br />|4889|
συνδρομή|sundrom�|sundrpmg|1) a running together, concourse, especially hostile or riotous<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4890</b><br />From (the alternate of) G4936; a <i>running together</i>, that is, (riotous) <i>concourse:</i> - run together.<br />|4890|
συνεγείρω|sunege�rw|suneceirz|1) to raise together, to cause to raise together<br />2) to raise up together from mortal death to a new and blessed life dedicated to God<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:786, 1102|<b>G4891</b><br />From G4862 and G1453; to <i>rouse</i> (from death) in company <i>with</i>, that is, (figuratively) to <i>revivify</i> (spiritually) in resemblance to: - raise up together, rise with.<br />|4891|
συνέδριον|sun�drion|sunedripn|1) any assembly (especially of magistrates, judges, ambassadors), whether convened to deliberate or pass judgment<br />2) any session or assembly or people deliberating or adjudicating<br />2a) the Sanhedrin, the great council at Jerusalem, consisting of the seventy one members, viz. scribes, elders, prominent members of the high priestly families and the high priest, the president of the assembly. The most important causes were brought before this tribunal, inasmuch as the Roman rulers of Judaea had left to it the power of trying such cases, and also of pronouncing sentence of death, with the limitation that a capital sentence pronounced by the Sanhedrin was not valid unless it was confirmed by the Roman procurator.<br />2b) a smaller tribunal or council which every Jewish town had for the decision of less important cases.<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:860, 1115|<b>G4892</b><br />Neuter of a presumed derivative of a compound of G4862 and the base of G1476; a <i>joint session</i>, that is, (specifically) the Jewish <i>Sanhedrim</i>; by analogy a subordinate <i>tribunal:</i> - council.<br />|4892|
συνείδησις|sune�dhsij|suneidgsis|1) the consciousness of anything<br />2) the soul as distinguishing between what is morally good and bad, prompting to do the former and shun the latter, commending one, condemning the other<br />2a) the conscience<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:898, 1120|<b>G4893</b><br />From a prolonged form of G4894; <i>co-perception</i>, that is, moral <i>consciousness:</i> - conscience.<br />|4893|
σύνοιδα|s�noida|sunpida|1) to see (have seen) together with others<br />2) to see (have seen) in one's mind with one's self<br />2a) to understand, perceive, comprehend<br />3) to know with another<br />4) to know in one's mind or with one's self, to be conscience of<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:898,*|<b>G4894</b><br />From G4862 and G1492; to <i>see completely</i>; used (like its primary) only in two past tenses, respectively meaning to <i>understand</i> or <i>become aware</i>, and to <i>be conscious</i> or (clandestinely) <i>informed of:</i> - consider, know, be privy, be ware of.<br />|4894|
