συνέχω|sun�cw|sunexz|1) to hold together<br />1a) any whole, lest it fall to pieces or something fall away from it<br />2) to hold together with constraint, to compress<br />2a) to press together with the hand<br />2a) to hold one's ears, to shut the heavens that it may not rain<br />2b) to press on every side<br />2b1) of a besieged city<br />2b2) of a strait, that forces a ship into a narrow channel<br />2b3) of a cattle squeeze, that pushing in on each side, forcing the beast into a position where it cannot move so the farmer can administer medication<br />3) to hold completely<br />3a) to hold fast<br />3a1) of a prisoner<br />3b) metaphorically<br />3b1) to be held by, closely occupied with any business<br />3b2) in teaching the word<br />3b3) to constrain, oppress, of ills laying hold of one and distressing him<br />3b4) to be held with, afflicted with, suffering from<br />3b5) to urge, impel<br />3b5a) of the soul<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:877, 1117|<b>G4912</b><br />From G4862 and G2192; to <i>hold together</i>, that is, to <i>compress</i> (the ears, with a crowd or siege) or <i>arrest</i> (a prisoner); figuratively to <i>compel</i>, <i>perplex</i>, <i>afflict</i>, <i>preoccupy:</i> - constrain, hold, keep in, press, lie sick of, stop, be in a strait, straiten, be taken with, throng.<br />|4912|
