συνίστημι|sun�sthmi|sunistgmi|1) to place together, to set in the same place,to bring or band together<br />1a) to stand with (or near)<br />2) to set one with another<br />2a) by way of presenting or introducing him<br />2b) to comprehend<br />3) to put together by way of composition or combination, to teach by combining and comparing<br />3a) to show, prove, establish, exhibit<br />4) to put together, unite parts into one whole<br />4a) to be composed of, consist<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:896, 1120|<b>G4921</b><br />From G4862 and G2476 (including its collateral forms); to <i>set together</i>, that is, (by implication) to <i>introduce</i> (favorably), or (figuratively) to <i>exhibit</i>; intransitively to <i>stand near</i>, or (figuratively) to <i>constitute:</i> - approve, commend, consist, make, stand (with).<br />|4921|
συνοδεύω|sunode�w|sunpdeuz|1) to journey with, travel in company with<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4922</b><br />From G4862 and G3593; to <i>travel</i> in company <i>with:</i> - journey with.<br />|4922|
συνοδία|sunod�a|sunpdia|1) a journey in company<br />1a) of a company of travellers, associates on a journey, a caravan<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4923</b><br />From a compound of G4862 and G3598 ("synod"); <i>companionship</i> on a journey, that is, (by implication) a <i>caravan:</i> - company.<br />|4923|
συνοικέω|sunoik�w|sunpikez|1) to dwell together<br />1a) of the domestic association<br />1b) of intercourse of a husband and wife<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G4924</b><br />From G4862 and G3611; to <i>reside together</i> (as a family): - dwell together.<br />|4924|
συνοικοδομέω|sunoikodom�w|sunpikpdpmez|1) to build together<br />1a) to build together or with others<br />1b) to put together or construct by building, out of several things to build up one whole<br />1b1) of the human body<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 5:148, 674|<b>G4925</b><br />From G4862 and G3618; to <i>construct</i>, that is, (passively) to <i>compose</i> (in company with other Christians, figuratively): - build together.<br />|4925|
