ταπεινός|tapein�j|taqeinps|1) not rising far from the ground<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) as a condition, lowly, of low degree<br />2b) brought low with grief, depressed<br />2c) lowly in spirit, humble<br />2d) in a bad sense, deporting one's self abjectly, deferring servilely to others<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 8:1, 1152|<b>G5011</b><br />Of uncertain derivation; <i>depressed</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>humiliated</i> (in circumstances or disposition): - base, cast down, humble, of low degree (estate), lowly.<br />|5011|
