φίλημα|f�lhma|vilgma|1) a kiss<br />2) the kiss with which, as a sign of fraternal affection, Christians were accustomed to welcome or dismiss their companions in the faith<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:114, 1262|<b>G5370</b><br />From G5368; a <i>kiss:</i> - kiss.<br />|5370|
Φιλήμων|Fil�mwn|vilgmzn|Philemon = "one who kisses"<br />1) a resident of Colosse, converted to Christianity by Paul, and the recipient of the letter bearing his name<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G5371</b><br />From G5368; <i>friendly</i>; <i>Philemon</i>, a Christian: - Philemon.<br />|5371|
Φίλητος|F�lhtoj|vilgtps|Philetus = "beloved"<br />1) a heretic and a disciple of Hymenaeus<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G5372</b><br />From G5368; <i>amiable</i>; <i>Philetus</i>, an opposer of Christianity: - Philetus.<br />|5372|
