φιλόστοργος|fil�storgoj|vilpstprcps|1) the mutual love of parents and children and wives and husbands<br />2) loving affection, prone to love, loving tenderly<br />2a) chiefly of the reciprocal tenderness of parents and children<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G5387</b><br />From G5384 and <span class="uni">στοργή</span> storg&ecirc; (<i>cherishing</i> one's kindred, especially parents or children); <i>fond of</i> natural <i>relatives</i>, that is, <i>fraternal</i> towards fellow Christians: - kindly affectioned.<br />|5387|
