φραγμός|fragm�j|vracmps|1) a hedge, a fence<br />2) that which separates, prevents two from coming together<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5418</b><br />From G5420; a <i>fence</i>, or inclosing <i>barrier</i> (literally or figuratively): - hedge (+ round about), partition.<br />|5418|
φράζω|fr�zw|vrafz|1) to indicate plainly, make known, declare, whether by gesture or by writing or speaking, or in some other ways<br />2) to explain<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5419</b><br />Probably akin to G5420 through the idea of <i>defining</i>; to <i>indicate</i> (by word or act), that is, (specifically) to <i>expound:</i> - declare.<br />|5419|
