φυλακή|fulak�|vulakg|1) guard, watch<br />1a) a watching, keeping watch<br />1a1) to keep watch<br />1b) persons keeping watch, a guard, sentinels<br />1c) of the place where captives are kept, a prison<br />1d) of the time (of night) during which guard was kept, a watch, i.e. a period of time during which part of the guard was on duty, and at the end of which others relieved them. As the earlier Greeks divided the night commonly into three parts, so, previous to the exile, the Israelites also had three watches in a night; subsequently, however, after they became subject to the Romans, they adopted the Roman custom of dividing the night into four watches<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:241, 1280|<b>G5438</b><br />From G5442; a <i>guarding</i> or (concretely <i>guard</i>), the act, the parson; figuratively the place, the condition, or (specifically) the time (as a division of day or night), literally or figuratively: - cage, hold, (im-) prison (-ment), ward, watch.<br />|5438|
φυλακίζω|fulak�zw|vulakifz|1) to cast into prison, imprison<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5439</b><br />From G5441; to <i>incarcerate:</i> - imprison.<br />|5439|
φυλακτήριον|fulakt�rion|vulaktgripn|1) a fortified place provided with a garrison, a station for a guard or garrison<br />2) a preservative or safeguard , an amulet. The Jews used this word to describe small strips of parchment on which were written the following passages of the law of Moses, Exo 13:1-10, Exo 13:11-16; Deu 6:4-9; and Deu 11:13-21<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G5440</b><br />Neuter of a derivative of G5442; a <i>guard case</i>, that is, "phylactery" for wearing slips of Scripture texts: - phylactery.<br />|5440|
φύλαξ|f�lax|vulao|1) a guard, keeper<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5441</b><br />From G5442; a <i>watcher</i> or <i>sentry:</i> - keeper.<br />|5441|
φυλάσσω|ful�ssw|vulassz|1) to guard<br />1a) to watch, keep watch<br />1b) to guard or watch, have an eye upon: lest he escape<br />1c) to guard a person (or thing) that he may remain safe<br />1c1) lest he suffer violence, be despoiled, etc. to protect<br />1c2) to protect one from a person or thing<br />1c3) to keep from being snatched away, preserve safe and unimpaired<br />1c4) to guard from being lost or perishing<br />1c5) to guard one's self from a thing<br />1d) to guard, i.e. care for, take care not to violate<br />1d1) to observe<br />2) to observe for one's self something to escape<br />2a) to avoid, shun flee from<br />2b) to guard for one's self (i.e. for one's safety's sake) so as not to violate, i.e. to keep, observe (the precepts of the Mosaic law)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:236, 1280|<b>G5442</b><br />Probably from G5443 through the idea of <i>isolation</i>; to <i>watch</i>, that is, <i>be on guard</i> (literally or figuratively); by implication to <i>preserve</i>. <i>obey</i>, <i>avoid:</i> - beware, keep (self), observe, save. Compare G5083.<br />|5442|
φυλή|ful�|vulg|1) a tribe<br />1a) in the NT all the persons descending from one of the twelve sons of the patriarch, Jacob<br />2) a nation, people<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:245, 1280|<b>G5443</b><br />From G5453 (compare G5444); an <i>offshoot</i>, that is, <i>race</i> or <i>clan:</i> - kindred, tribe.<br />|5443|
φύλλον|f�llon|vullpn|1) a leaf<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G5444</b><br />From the same as G5443; a <i>sprout</i>, that is, <i>leaf:</i> - leaf.<br />|5444|
φύραμα|f�rama|vurama|1) any substance mixed with water and kneaded<br />2) a mass, a lump<br />2a) of dough<br />2b) of clay<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G5445</b><br />From a prolonged form of <span class="uni">φύρω</span> phur&ocirc; (to <i>mix</i> a liquid with a solid; perhaps akin to G5453 through the idea of <i>swelling</i> in bulk), mean to <i>knead</i>; a <i>mass</i> of dough: - lump.<br />|5445|
φυσικός|fusik�j|vusikps|1) produced by nature, inborn<br />2) agreeable to nature<br />3) governed by (the instincts of) nature<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:251, 1283|<b>G5446</b><br />From G5449; "physical", that is, (by implication) <i>instinctive</i>: - natural. Compare G5591.<br />|5446|
φυσικῶς|fusik�j|vusikzs|1) in a natural manner, by nature, under the guidance of nature: by the aid of the bodily senses<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:251, 1283|<b>G5447</b><br />Adverb frm G5446; "physically", that is, (by implication) <i>instinctively:</i> - naturally.<br />|5447|
φυσιόω|fusi�w|vusipz|1) to make natural, to cause a thing to pass into nature<br />2) to inflate, blow up, to cause to swell up<br />2a) to puff up, make proud<br />2b) to be puffed up, to bear one's self loftily, be proud<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5448</b><br />From G5449 in the primary sense of <i>blowing</i>; to <i>inflate</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>make proud</i> (<i>haughty</i>): - puff up.<br />|5448|
φύσις|f�sij|vusis|1) nature<br />1a) the nature of things, the force, laws, order of nature<br />1a) as opposed to what is monstrous, abnormal, perverse<br />1b) as opposed what has been produced by the art of man: the natural branches, i.e. branches by the operation of nature<br />1b) birth, physical origin<br />1c) a mode of feeling and acting which by long habit has become nature<br />1d) the sum of innate properties and powers by which one person differs from others, distinctive native peculiarities, natural characteristics: the natural strength, ferocity, and intractability of beasts<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:251, 1283|<b>G5449</b><br />From G5453; <i>growth</i> (by <i>germination</i> or <i>expansion</i>), that is, (by implication) natural <i>production</i> (lineal <i>descent</i>); by extension a <i>genus</i> or <i>sort</i>; figuratively native <i>disposition</i>, <i>constitution</i> or <i>usage:</i> - ([man-]) kind, nature ([-al]).<br />|5449|
φυσίωσις|fus�wsij|vusizsis|1) a puffing up of soul, loftiness, pride<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G5450</b><br />From G5448; <i>inflation</i>, that is, (figuratively) <i>haughtiness:</i> - swelling.<br />|5450|
φυτεία|fute�a|vuteia|1) a planting<br />2) the thing planted, a plant<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G5451</b><br />From G5452; trans <i>planting</i>, that is, (concretely) a <i>shrub</i> or <i>vegetable:</i> - plant.<br />|5451|
φυτεύω|fute�w|vuteuz|1) to plant<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5452</b><br />From a derivative of G5453; to <i>set out</i> in the earth, that is, <i>implant</i>. Figuratively to <i>instil</i> doctrine: - plant.<br />|5452|
φύω|f�w|vuz|1) to beget, bring forth, produce<br />2) to be born, to spring up, to grow<br />3) to shoot forth, spring up<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5453</b><br />A primary verb; probably originally to "puff" or <i>blow</i>, that is, to <i>swell</i> up; but only used in the implied sense, to <i>germinate</i> or <i>grow</i> (<i>sprout</i>, <i>produce</i>), literally or figuratively: - spring (up).<br />|5453|
φωλεός|fwle�j|vzleps|1) a lurking hole, a burrow<br />2) a lair<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5454</b><br />Of uncertain derivation; a <i>burrow</i> or <i>lurking place:</i> - hole.<br />|5454|
φωνέω|fwn�w|vznez|1) to sound, emit a sound, to speak<br />1a) of a cock: to crow<br />1b) of men: to cry, cry out, cry aloud, speak with a loud voice<br />2) to call, to call one's self, either by one's own voice or though another<br />3) to send for, summon<br />3a) to call out of (i.e. bid one to quit a place and come to one<br />3b) to invite<br />3c) to address, accost, call by a name<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:301, 1287|<b>G5455</b><br />From G5456; to emit a <i>sound</i> (animal, human or instrumental); by implication to <i>address</i> in words or by name, also in imitation: - call (for), crow, cry.<br />|5455|
φωνή|fwn�|vzng|1) a sound, a tone<br />1a) of inanimate things, as musical instruments<br />2) a voice<br />2a) of the sound of uttered words<br />3) speech<br />3a) of a language, tongue<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:278, 1287|<b>G5456</b><br />Probably akin to G5316 through the idea of <i>disclosure</i>; a <i>tone</i> (articulate, bestial or artificial); by implication an <i>address</i> (for any purpose), <i>saying</i> or <i>language:</i> - noise, sound, voice.<br />|5456|
φῶς|f�j|vzs|1) light<br />1a) the light<br />1a1) emitted by a lamp<br />1a2) a heavenly light such as surrounds angels when they appear on earth<br />1b) anything emitting light<br />1b1) a star<br />1b2) fire because it is light and sheds light<br />1b3) a lamp or torch<br />1c) light, i.e brightness<br />1c1) of a lamp<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) God is light because light has the extremely delicate, subtle, pure, brilliant quality<br />2b) of truth and its knowledge, together with the spiritual purity associated with it<br />2c) that which is exposed to the view of all, openly, publicly<br />2d) reason, mind<br />2d1) the power of understanding especially moral and spiritual truth<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:310, 1293|<b>G5457</b><br />From an obsolete<span class="uni">φάω</span> pha&ocirc; (to <i>shine</i> or make <i>manifest</i>, especially by <i>rays</i>; compare G5316 and G5346); <i>luminousness</i> (in the widest application, natural or artificial, abstract or concrete, literal or figurative): - fire, light.<br />|5457|
φωστήρ|fwst�r|vzstgr|1) that which gives light, an illuminator<br />1a) of the stars, sun and moon<br />2) light, brightness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:310, 1293|<b>G5458</b><br />From G5457; an <i>illuminator</i>, that is, (concretely) a <i>luminary</i>, or (abstractly) <i>brilliancy:</i> - light.<br />|5458|
φωσφόρος|fwsf�roj|vzsvprps|1) light bringing, giving light<br />2) the planet Venus, the morning star, day star<br />3) metaphorically Christ<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:310, 1293|<b>G5459</b><br />From G5457 and G5342; <i>light bearing</i> ("phosphorus"), that is, (specifically) the <i>morning star</i> (figuratively): - day star.<br />|5459|
φωτεινός|fwtein�j|vzteinps|1) light<br />1a) composed of light<br />1b) of a bright character<br />1c) full of light<br />1d) well lit<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:310, 1293|<b>G5460</b><br />From G5457; <i>lustrous</i>, that is, <i>transparent</i> or <i>well illuminated</i> (figurative): - bright, full of light.<br />|5460|
φωτίζω|fwt�zw|vztifz|1) to give light, to shine<br />2) to enlighten, light up, illumine<br />3) to bring to light, render evident<br />3a) to cause something to exist and thus come to light and become clear to all<br />4) to enlighten, spiritually, imbue with saving knowledge<br />4a) to instruct, to inform, teach<br />4b) to give understanding to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:310, 1293|<b>G5461</b><br />From G5457; to <i>shed rays</i>, that is, to <i>shine</i> or (transitively) to <i>brighten</i> up (literally or figuratively): - enlighten, illuminate, (bring to, give) light, make to see.<br />|5461|
φωτισμός|fwtism�j|vztismps|1) the act of enlightening, illumination<br />2) brightness, bright light<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:310, 1293|<b>G5462</b><br />From G5461; <i>illumination</i> (figurative): - light.<br />|5462|
χαίρω|ca�rw|xairz|1) to rejoice, be glad<br />2) to rejoice exceedingly<br />3) to be well, thrive<br />4) in salutations, hail!<br />5) at the beginning of letters: to give one greeting, salute<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:359, 1298|<b>G5463</b><br />A primary verb; to be full of <i>"cheer"</i>, that is, calmly <i>happy</i> or well off; impersonal especially as a salutation (on meeting or parting), <i>be well:</i> - farewell, be glad, God speed, greeting, hail, joy (-fully), rejoice.<br />|5463|
χάλαζα|c�laza|xalafa|1) hail<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G5464</b><br />Probably from G5465; <i>hail:</i> - hail.<br />|5464|
χαλάω|cal�w|xalaz|1) to loosen, slacken, relax<br />2) to let down from a higher place to a lower<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5465</b><br />From the base of G5490; to <i>lower</i> (as into a <i>void</i>): - let down, strike.<br />|5465|
Χαλδαῖος|Calda�oj|xaldaips|Chaldean = "as clod breakers"<br />1) a Chaldean<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper masculine|<b>G5466</b><br />Probably of Hebrew origin [H3778]; a <i>Chaldaean</i> (that is, <i>Kasdi</i>), or native of the region of the lower Euphrates: - Chaldan.<br />|5466|
χαλεπός|calep�j|xaleqps|1) hard to do, to take, to approach<br />2) hard to bear, troublesome, dangerous<br />2a) harsh, fierce, savage<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G5467</b><br />Perhaps from G5465 through the idea of <i>reducing</i> the strength; <i>difficult</i>, that is, <i>dangerous</i>, or (by implication) <i>furious:</i> - fierce, perilous.<br />|5467|
χαλιναγωγέω|calinagwg�w|xalinaczcez|1) to lead by a bridle, to guide<br />2) to bridle, hold in check, restrain<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5468</b><br />From a compound of G5469 and the reduplicated form of G71; to <i>be</i> a <i>bit leader</i>, that is, to <i>curb</i> (figuratively): - bridle.<br />|5468|
χαλινός|calin�j|xalinps|1) a bridle<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5469</b><br />From G5465 a <i>curb</i> or <i>head stall</i> (as <i>curbing</i> the spirit): - bit, bridle.<br />|5469|
χαλκοῦς|calko�j|xalkpus|1) brazen, made of brass<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G5470</b><br />From G5475; <i>coppery:</i> - brass.<br />|5470|
χαλκεύς|calke�j|xalkeus|1) a worker in copper or iron, a smith<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5471</b><br />From G5475; a <i>copper worker</i> or <i>brazier:</i> - coppersmith.<br />|5471|
χαλκηδών|calkhd�n|xalkgdzn|1) chalcedony is a precious stone of misty grey colour, clouded with blue, yellow, or purple<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5472</b><br />From G5475 and perhaps G1491; <i>copper like</i>, that is, "chalcedony": - chalcedony.<br />|5472|
χαλκίον|calk�on|xalkipn|1) a (copper or) brazen vessel<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G5473</b><br />Diminutive from G5475; a <i>copper dish:</i> - brazen vessel.<br />|5473|
χαλκολίβανον|calkol�banon|xalkplibanpn|1) some metal like gold if not more precious<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G5474</b><br />Neuter of a compound of G5475 and G3030 (in the implied mean of <i>whiteness</i> or <i>brilliancy</i>); <i>burnished copper</i>, an alloy of copper (or gold) and silver having a brilliant lustre: - fine brass.<br />|5474|
χαλκός|calk�j|xalkps|1) brass<br />2) what is made of brass, money, coins of brass (also of silver and gold)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5475</b><br />Perhaps from G5465 through the idea of <i>hollowing</i> out as a vessel (this metal being chiefly used for that purpose); <i>copper</i> (the substance, or some implement or coin made of it): - brass, money.<br />|5475|
χαμαί|cama�|xamai|1) on the ground, on the earth<br />2) to the ground<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adverb|<b>G5476</b><br />Adverb perhaps from the base of G5490 through the idea of a <i>fissure</i> in the soil; <i>earthward</i>, that is, <i>prostrate:</i> - on (to) the ground.<br />|5476|
Χανάαν|Can�an|xanaan|Canaan = "lowland"<br />1) the land of Canaan<br />2) in a narrower sense: the part of Palestine lying west of the Jordan<br />3) in a wider sense: all of Palestine<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G5477</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H3667]; <i>Chanaan</i> (that is, <i>Kenaan</i>), the early name of Palestine: - Chanaan.<br />|5477|
Χαναναῖος|Canana�oj|xananaips|1) Canaanite, the name of the ancient inhabitants of Palestine before its conquest by the Israelites<br />2) in Christ's time: a Phoenician<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G5478</b><br />From G5477; a <i>Chanaanaean</i> (that is, <i>Kenaanite</i>), or native of gentile Palestine: - of Canaan.<br />|5478|
χαρά|car�|xara|1) joy, gladness<br />1a) the joy received from you<br />1b) the cause or occasion of joy<br />1b1) of persons who are one's joy<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:359, 1298|<b>G5479</b><br />From G5463; <i>cheerfulness</i>, that is, calm <i>delight:</i> - gladness, X greatly, (X be exceeding) joy (-ful, -fully, -fulness, -ous).<br />|5479|
χάραγμα|c�ragma|xaracma|1) a stamp, an imprinted mark<br />1a) of the mark stamped on the forehead or the right hand as the badge of the followers of the Antichrist<br />1b) the mark branded upon horses<br />2) thing carved, sculpture, graven work<br />2a) of idolatrous images<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:416, 1308|<b>G5480</b><br />From the same as G5482; a <i>scratch</i> or <i>etching</i>, that is, <i>stamp</i> (as a <i>badge</i> of servitude), or <i>sculptured</i> figure (<i>statue</i>): - graven, mark.<br />|5480|
χαρακτήρ|carakt�r|xaraktgr|1) the instrument used for engraving or carving<br />2) the mark stamped upon that instrument or wrought out on it<br />2a) a mark or figure burned in (Lev 13:28) or stamped on, an impression<br />2b) the exact expression (the image) of any person or thing, marked likeness, precise reproduction in every respect, i.e facsimile<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:418, 1308|<b>G5481</b><br />From the same as G5482; a <i>graver</i> (the tool or the person), that is, (by implication) <i>engraving</i> (["character"], the <i>figure</i> stamped, that is, an exact <i>copy</i> or [figuratively] <i>representation</i>): - express image.<br />|5481|
χάραξ|c�rax|xarao|1) a pale or stake, a palisade<br />2) a palisade or rampart<br />2a) pales between which earth, stones, trees, and timbers are heaped and packed together<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5482</b><br />From "charasso" (to <i>sharpen</i> to a point; akin to G1125 through the idea of <i>scratching</i>); a <i>stake</i>, that is, (by implication) a <i>palisade</i> or <i>rampart</i> (millitary <i>mound</i> for circumvallation in a siege): - trench.<br />|5482|
χαρίζομαι|car�zomai|xarifpmai|1) to do something pleasant or agreeable (to one), to do a favour to, gratify<br />1a) to show one's self gracious, kind, benevolent<br />1b) to grant forgiveness, to pardon<br />1c) to give graciously, give freely, bestow<br />1c1) to forgive<br />1c2) graciously to restore one to another<br />1c3) to preserve for one a person in peril<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:372, 1298|<b>G5483</b><br />Middle voice from G5485; to grant as a <i>favor</i>, that is, gratuitously, in kindness, pardon or rescue: - deliver, (frankly) forgive, (freely) give, grant.<br />|5483|
χάριν|c�rin|xarin|1) in favour of, for the pleasure of<br />2) for, for the sake of<br />3) on this account, for this cause<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> preposition|<b>G5484</b><br />Accusative case of G5485 as preposition; through <i>favor</i> of, that is, <i>on account</i> of: - be- (for) cause of, for sake of, + . . . fore, X reproachfully.<br />|5484|
χάρις|c�rij|xaris|1) grace<br />1a) that which affords joy, pleasure, delight, sweetness, charm, loveliness: grace of speech<br />2) good will, loving-kindness, favour<br />2a) of the merciful kindness by which God, exerting his holy influence upon souls, turns them to Christ, keeps, strengthens, increases them in Christian faith, knowledge, affection, and kindles them to the exercise of the Christian virtues<br />3) what is due to grace<br />3a) the spiritual condition of one governed by the power of divine grace<br />3b) the token or proof of grace, benefit<br />3b1) a gift of grace<br />3b2) benefit, bounty<br />4) thanks, (for benefits, services, favours), recompense, reward<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:372, 1298|<b>G5485</b><br />From G5463; <i>graciousness</i> (as <i>gratifying</i>), of manner or act (abstract or concrete; literal, figurative or spiritual; especially the divine influence upon the heart, and its reflection in the life; including <i>gratitude</i>): - acceptable, benefit, favour, gift, grace (-ious), joy liberality, pleasure, thank (-s, -worthy).<br />|5485|
χάρισμα|c�risma|xarisma|1) a favour with which one receives without any merit of his own<br />2) the gift of divine grace<br />3) the gift of faith, knowledge, holiness, virtue<br />4) the economy of divine grace, by which the pardon of sin and eternal salvation is appointed to sinners in consideration of the merits of Christ laid hold of by faith<br />5) grace or gifts denoting extraordinary powers, distinguishing certain Christians and enabling them to serve the church of Christ, the reception of which is due to the power of divine grace operating on their souls by the Holy Spirit<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:402, 1298|<b>G5486</b><br />From G5483; a (divine) <i>gratuity</i>, that is, <i>deliverance</i> (from danger or passion); (specifically) a (spiritual) <i>endowment</i>, that is, (subjectively) religious <i>qualification</i>, or (objectively) miraculous <i>faculty:</i> - (free) gift.<br />|5486|
χαριτόω|carit�w|xaritpz|1) to make graceful<br />1a) charming, lovely, agreeable<br />2) to peruse with grace, compass with favour<br />3) to honour with blessings<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:372, 1298|<b>G5487</b><br />From G5485; to <i>grace</i>, that is, indue with special <i>honor:</i> - make accepted, be highly favoured.<br />|5487|
Χαρράν|Carr�n|xarran|Haran = "a mountaineer"<br />1) a city in Mesopotamia, of great antiquity and made famous by the defeat of Crassus<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper locative|<b>G5488</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H2771]; <i>Charrhan</i> (that is, <i>Charan</i>), a place in Mesopotamia: - Charran.<br />|5488|
χάρτης|c�rthj|xartgs|1) paper<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5489</b><br />From the same as G5482; a <i>sheet</i> ("chart") of writing material (as to be <i>scribbled</i> over): - paper.<br />|5489|
χάσμα|c�sma|xasma|1) a gaping opening, a chasm, a gulf<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G5490</b><br />From a form of an obsolete primary "chao" (to "gape" or "yawn"); a "chasm" or <i>vacancy</i> (impassable <i>interval</i>): - gulf.<br />|5490|
