χρυσός|crus�j|xrusps|1) precious things made of gold, golden ornaments<br />1a) an image made of gold<br />1b) stamped gold, gold coin<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5557</b><br />Perhaps from the base of G5530 (through the idea of the <i>utility</i> of the metal); <i>gold</i>; by extension a <i>golden</i> article, as an ornament or coin: - gold.<br />|5557|
χρυσόω|crus�w|xruspz|1) to adorn with gold, to gild<br />1a) of a woman ornamented with gold so profusely that she seems to be gilded<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5558</b><br />From G5557; to <i>gild</i>, that is, <i>bespangle</i> with golden ornaments: - deck.<br />|5558|
χρώς|cr�j|xrzs|1) the surface of the body, the skin<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5559</b><br />Probably akin to the base of G5530 through the idea of <i>handling</i>; the <i>body</i> (properly its <i>surface</i> or <i>skin</i>): - body.<br />|5559|
