ψευδολόγος|yeudol�goj|yeudplpcps|1) speaking (teaching) falsely, speaking lies<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective|<b>G5573</b><br />From G5571 and G3004; <i>mendacious</i>, that is, <i>promulgating erroneous</i> Christian <i>doctrine:</i> - speaking lies.<br />|5573|
ψεύδομαι|ye�domai|yeudpmai|1) to lie, to speak deliberate falsehoods<br />2) to deceive one by a lie, to lie to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:594, 1339|<b>G5574</b><br />Middle voice of an apparently primary verb; to <i>utter an untruth</i> or attempt to <i>deceive</i> by falsehood: - falsely, lie.<br />|5574|
ψευδόμαρτυς|yeud�martuj|yeudpmartus|1) a false witness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:513,*|<b>G5575</b><br />From G5571 and a kindred form of G3144; a <i>spurious witness</i>, that is, <i>bearer of untrue testimony:</i> - false witness.<br />|5575|
ψευδομαρτυρέω|yeudomartur�w|yeudpmarturez|1) to utter falsehoods in giving testimony, to testify falsely, to bear false witness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:513, 564|<b>G5576</b><br />From G5575; to <i>be an untrue testifier</i>, that is, offer <i>falsehood in evidence:</i> - be a false witness.<br />|5576|
ψευδομαρτυρία|yeudomartur�a|yeudpmarturia|1) false witness, false testimony<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 4:513, 564|<b>G5577</b><br />From G5575; <i>untrue testimony:</i> - false witness.<br />|5577|
ψευδοπροφήτης|yeudoprof�thj|yeudpqrpvgtgs|1) one who, acting the part of a divinely inspired prophet, utters falsehoods under the name of divine prophecies<br />2) a false prophet<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 6:781, 952|<b>G5578</b><br />From G5571 and G4396; a <i>spurious prophet</i>, that is, <i>pretended foreteller</i> or religious <i>impostor:</i> - false prophet.<br />|5578|
