ψεῦσμα|ye�sma|yeusma|1) a falsehood, a lie<br />2) the perfidy by which a man by sinning breaks faith with God<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:594, 1339|<b>G5582</b><br />From G5574; a <i>fabrication</i>, that is, <i>falsehood:</i> - lie.<br />|5582|
ψεύστης|ye�sthj|yeustgs|1) a liar<br />2) one who breaks faith<br />3) a false and faithless man<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:594, 1339|<b>G5583</b><br />From G5574; a <i>falsifier:</i> - liar.<br />|5583|
ψηλαφάω|yhlaf�w|yglavaz|1) to handle, touch and feel<br />2) metaphorically mentally to seek after tokens of a person or a thing<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5584</b><br />From the base of G5567 (compare G5586); to <i>manipulate</i>, that is, <i>verify</i> by contact; figuratively to <i>search</i> for: - feel after, handle, touch.<br />|5584|
ψηφίζω|yhf�zw|ygvifz|1) to count with pebbles, to compute, calculate, reckon<br />2) to give one's vote by casting a pebble into the urn<br />3) to decide by voting<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:604, 1341|<b>G5585</b><br />From G5586; to <i>use pebbles</i> in enumeration, that is, (genitive case) to <i>compute:</i> - count.<br />|5585|
ψῆφος|y�foj|ygvps|1) a small worn smooth stone, a pebble<br />1a) in the ancient courts of justice the accused were condemned by black pebbles and the acquitted by white<br />2) a vote (on account of the use of pebbles in voting)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:604, 1341|<b>G5586</b><br />From the same as G5584; a <i>pebble</i> (as worn smooth by <i>handling</i>), that is, (by implication of use as a <i>counter</i> or <i>ballot</i>) a <i>verdict</i> (of acquittal) or <i>ticket</i> (of admission); a <i>vote:</i> - stone, voice.<br />|5586|
