ψιθυριστής|yiqurist�j|yihuristgs|1) a whisperer, secret slanderer, detractor<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun masculine|<b>G5588</b><br />From the same as G5587; a secret <i>calumniator:</i> - whisperer.<br />|5588|
ψίξ|y�x|yio|1) a little morsel, a crumb<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G5589</b><br />Diminutive from a derivative of the base of G5567 (meaning a <i>crumb</i>); a <i>little bit</i> or <i>morsel:</i> - crumb.<br />|5589|
ψυχή|yuc�|yuxg|1) breath<br />1a) the breath of life<br />1a1) the vital force which animates the body and shows itself in breathing<br />1a1a) of animals<br />1a1b) of men<br />1b) life<br />1c) that in which there is life<br />1c1) a living being, a living soul<br />2) the soul<br />2a) the seat of the feelings, desires, affections, aversions (our heart, soul etc.)<br />2b) the (human) soul in so far as it is constituted that by the right use of the aids offered it by God it can attain its highest end and secure eternal blessedness, the soul regarded as a moral being designed for everlasting life<br />2c) the soul as an essence which differs from the body and is not dissolved by death (distinguished from other parts of the body)<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:608, 1342|<b>G5590</b><br />From G5594; <i>breath</i>, that is, (by implication) <i>spirit</i>, abstractly or concretely (the <i>animal</i> sentient principle only; thus distinguished on the one hand from G4151, which is the rational and immortal <i>soul</i>; and on the other from G2222, which is mere <i>vitality</i>, even of plants: these terms thus exactly correspond respectively to the Hebrew [H5315], [H7307] and [H2416]: - heart (+ -ily), life, mind, soul, + us, + you.<br />|5590|
ψυχικός|yucik�j|yuxikps|1) of or belonging to breath<br />1a) having the nature and characteristics of the breath<br />1a1) the principal of animal life, which men have in common with the brutes<br />1b) governed by breath<br />1b1) the sensuous nature with its subjection to appetite and passion<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 9:661, 1342|<b>G5591</b><br />From G5590; <i>sensitive</i> that is, <i>animate</i> (in distinction on the one hand from G4152, which is the higher or <i>renovated</i> nature; and on the other from G5446, which is the lower or <i>bestial</i> nature): - natural, sensual.<br />|5591|
ψῦχος|y�coj|yuxps|1) cold<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G5592</b><br />From G5594; <i>coolness:</i> - cold.<br />|5592|
ψυχρός|yucr�j|yuxrps|1) cold, cool<br />1a) of cool water<br />2) metaphorically<br />2a) cold, i.e. sluggish, inert<br />2b) in mind: of one destitute of warm Christian faith and the desire for holiness<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 2:876, 296|<b>G5593</b><br />From G5592; <i>chilly</i> (literally or figuratively): - cold.<br />|5593|
ψύχομαι|y�comai|yuxpmai|1) to breathe, blow, cool by blowing<br />2) to be made or grow cool or cold<br />3) metaphorically of waning love<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5594</b><br />A primary verb; to <i>breathe</i> (<i>voluntarily</i> but <i>gently</i>; thus differing on the one hand from G4154, which denotes properly a <i>forcible</i> respiration; and on the other from the base of G109, which refers properly to an inanimate <i>breeze</i>), that is, (by implication of reduction of temperature by evaporation) to <i>chill</i> (figuratively): - wax cold.<br />|5594|
ψωμίζω|ywm�zw|yzmifz|1) to feed by putting a bit or crumb (of food) into the mouth<br />1a) of infants, young animals etc.<br />2) to feed, nourish<br />3) to give a thing to feed someone, feed out to<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5595</b><br />From the base of G5596; to <i>supply</i> with <i>bits</i>, that is, (genitive case) to <i>nourish:</i> - (bestow to) feed.<br />|5595|
ψωμίον|ywm�on|yzmipn|1) a fragment, bit, morsel<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G5596</b><br />Diminutive from a derivation of the base of G5597; a <i>crumb</i> or <i>morsel</i> (as if <i>rubbed</i> off), that is, a <i>mouthful:</i> - sop.<br />|5596|
ψώχω|y�cw|yzxz|1) to rub, to rub to pieces<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> verb|<b>G5597</b><br />Prolongation from the same base as G5567; to <i>triturate</i>, that is, (by analogy) to <i>rub</i> out (kernels from husks with the fingers or hand): - rub.<br />|5597|
