Μαριάμ|Mar�a|maria|Mary or Miriam = "their rebellion"<br />1) Mary the mother of Jesus<br />2) Mary Magdalene, a women from Magdala<br />3) Mary, the sister of Lazarus and Martha<br />4) Mary of Cleophas the mother of James the less<br />5) Mary the mother of John Mark, a sister of Barnabas<br />6) Mary, a Roman Christian who is greeted by Paul in Rom 16:6<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun proper feminine|<b>G3137</b><br />Of Hebrew origin [H4813]; <i>Maria</i> or <i>Mariam</i> (that is, <i>Mirjam</i>), the name of six Christian females: - Mary.<br />|3137|
