Σεβαστός|sebast�j|sebastps|1) reverend, venerable<br />2) the title of the Roman emperors<br />2a) Augustan, i,e, taking its name from the emperor<br />2b) a title of honour which used to be given certain legions, or cohorts, or battalions, "for valour"<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> adjective<br /><b>Citing in TDNT:</b> 7:174, 1010|<b>G4575</b><br />From G4573; <i>venerable</i> (<i>august</i>), that is, (as noun) a title of the Roman <i>Emperor</i>, or (as adjective) <i>imperial:</i> - Augustus (-').<br />|4575|
