στάδιος|st�dion|stadipn|1) a space or distance of about 600 feet (185 m)<br />2) a race course<br />2a) place in which contests in running were held, the one who outstripped the rest and reached the goal first, receiving the prize. Courses of this description were found in most of the larger Greek cities, and were like that at Olympia, 600 Greek feet in length<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun neuter|<b>G4712</b><br />Or the masculine plural form, <span class="uni">στάδιος</span> stadios <i>stad'-ee-os</i>. <br />From the base of G2476 (as <i>fixed</i>); a <i>stade</i> or certain measure of distance; by implication a <i>stadium</i> or <i>race course:</i> - furlong, race.<br />|4712|
