Ταβέρνη|tab�rnh|taberng|1) taverns<br />2) Three Taverns, the name of a halting place on the Appian way between Rome and the Market of Appius; it was 10 miles (16 km) from the latter place and 33 miles (50 km) ) from Rome<br /><b>Part of Speech:</b> noun feminine|<b>G4999</b><br />Plural of Latin origin; <i>huts</i> or <i>wooden walled</i> buildings; <i>Tabernae:</i> - taverns.<br />|4999|
